{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","id":"05693046-7b94-4ab6-b178-b8f4cffe8a12","timestamp":"2026-11-03T05:39:34.641Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"963960cb5609eb497f32fdcbfcf167f69d06bc05dc2addf3579e09e199fb65f2","params":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":64000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"ade032fc-6bb5-42f2-a8f1-5da8dea9cf0a","keep":431,"tail":["bca3f92e9591b9989c0751b323de15ed6a3301eda7e1a7774342278b58d347e8","d0308ee7d24e27b85600433f97c0365a6e38433c4f651f1005b42d55988b016f","7bc8e5bd8d8503a2ae314aeab3bf5220746165685022102601f256e06b6ee163","fd45c40b25ab2bc033d485d0e1d865199e6d98d240b67fae5912b30ba5e3b54c"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",433,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"f5276430749eed64e7b6029f11a5d01f3beb6bfa3ab5f726b16c96b362407c25"}
{"parentUuid":"7f04c5d1-63e0-4f23-b281-865c1674309e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgfTUG8M5cS2CrSExtox3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, the three branches are the right starting point, and the JusPrin one is closer than I expected. It already contains most of the machinery the new flow needs. What it lacks is the shape: it runs the old five-step onboarding inside the Home page, so the work is a rework of its screens and step order, not a rebuild.\n\n**Where the branches stand.** All three are named `credits-integration-2026-11`, all from today, none behind their base.\n\n| Repo | Ahead of base | What it carries |\n|---|---|---|\n| JusPrin | 5 commits on today's jusprin-newui, worktree `.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding` with a build | Credits in the app, plus the onboarding port from the month-old branch, merged with today's main line |\n| tsd-enterprise | 4 commits on master | The credit ledger, charging, raw chat capture, print-report rewards |\n| ops | 2 commits on master | The Standard model alias in the gateway config |\n\nThe gateway and ops branches do not touch onboarding. They matter only because the \"Sign in for 500 credits\" door needs the ledger to grant the first-month lot, and that is built there.\n\n**What the JusPrin branch already gives the new flow:**\n\n- **A controller.** `OnboardingModel` is a pure function from saved progress plus facts about the install to the next step, with tests. Progress persists in the app config, and \"done\" is written only when the sequence ends. That is exactly the controller the flow board describes. Its steps are the wrong ones, but the design is right.\n- **OrcaSlicer detection and import.** It finds the OrcaSlicer folder beside the app's own data folder, reads which preset folder is configured, lists printers, filaments and processes by name, imports the chosen kinds through OrcaSlicer's own preset import, and keeps a list of files that failed for a retry. The import step on canvas board 07 maps onto this almost one to one.\n- **A printer step.** Confirm the imported printer, run OrcaSlicer's printer wizard, or \"I don't have a printer here\", which installs a Generic Klipper printer under its own name. That last path is the \"Skip, use a default\" branch, except the default is Klipper rather than a marked assumed printer.\n- **The detour mechanics.** Its \"Sign in\" door already calls the shell to open Preferences › Agent, and the step function re-evaluates when Preferences closes because it reads whether the agent is enabled. The loopback sign-in exists on the main line.\n- **The v1 case.** A v1 import marks the person as returning and hides onboarding, as the flow wants.\n\n**What has to change to match the decided flow:**\n\n- **The welcome.** The branch's welcome is a Home page state with the old headline, \"Explore first\", a \"Dismiss onboarding\" link and the Agent header. The new one is a full-window screen with the clip, title A, four doors and the corner lockup. The clip needs a video element the Home page does not have yet.\n- **Step order.** The branch goes Welcome → Profiles → Setup → Project, and treats a configured agent as a reason to skip the welcome. The new flow is Welcome → Printers → Home with no Project step, and the welcome shows once regardless. Both are changes to the step function and its tests, which is the cheap kind of change.\n- **The sign-in detour.** The branch opens Preferences for sign-in and waits for the agent to be enabled. The flow instead waits on the card itself and advances on the callback. That is new page state plus a host message when the sign-in lands.\n- **The Printers step.** Board 07 shows printers with filament counts and one Import button. The branch shows three tick boxes by preset kind, a partial-import screen, a \"choose a bundle\" file picker and a \"choose a folder\" picker. Those are extra screens to retire. The \"Neither\" branch should open the add-printer form, not OrcaSlicer's wizard, and the skip should mark the chip assumed, which needs the stored origin the design session flagged.\n- **Home after.** The collapsed doors in the agent column and the assumed mark on the printer card are not there.\n\n**Two cautions before building on it.** The branch's onboarding was ported from the old wizard boards, so its strings and layout came from Figma frames and are all superseded by canvas version 89; nothing on its screens should be kept by default. And the branch is a shared worktree another session made today, so the implementation session should branch from it into a worktree of its own rather than work there.\n\nMy recommendation is to start a session from `credits-integration-2026-11` in JusPrin, keep the controller, the detection and import code, the printer install and the persistence, and replace the screens and the step function with the flow on board 11. The gateway and ops branches stay as they are."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":517,"cache_read_input_tokens":362582,"output_tokens":1539,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":517,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":1539,"cache_read_input_tokens":362582,"cache_creation_input_tokens":517,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":517},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgfTUFoFj3rBWPWy4gVDz","requestRef":"05693046-7b94-4ab6-b178-b8f4cffe8a12","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-1","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"30209e61-43e9-43a0-b46e-705a4b6eef09","timestamp":"2026-11-03T05:40:03.894Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
