{"parentUuid":"ceb92186-7fc9-4f2e-b348-2a454c6c33e8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgfTsuYXN8uLeGSWXE9zF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm setting up the first-run flow on a branch off credits-integration-2026-11, running in its own worktree on Opus 5.5 with the flow, canvas boards and keep-or-replace list as the brief.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4089,"cache_read_input_tokens":364738,"output_tokens":3857,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":255},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4089,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":3857,"cache_read_input_tokens":364738,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4089,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4089},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":2,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgfTsuEuthgvkNPr4m8Yu","requestRef":"dd58a541-76d4-4bac-bf66-dadb4836419e","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-1","type":"assistant","uuid":"a873fdf3-7f7e-4aea-a5af-51b2e4e0e50f","timestamp":"2026-11-03T05:45:02.955Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
{"parentUuid":"a873fdf3-7f7e-4aea-a5af-51b2e4e0e50f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgfTsuYXN8uLeGSWXE9zF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DgRb7wYJmX5teTQunpBXtu","name":"mcp__ccd_session__start_session","input":{"initiation":"user_asked","title":"Build the first-run flow on top of the credits branch","name":"first-run-flow","context":"fresh","model":"claude-opus-5-5","use_worktree":true,"source_branch":"credits-integration-2026-11","branch_name":"first-run-flow","wake_when_done":true,"background":"JusPrin 2 is a fork of OrcaSlicer with an in-app AI agent. On 2026-11-02 Kenneth decided the first-launch experience from rendered comparisons: no wizard; one welcome screen with a looping silent clip on the left and the title, subtitle and four \"doors\" on the right; then a Printers step; then Home. The proposition is expert help with a failed print from an AI that sees the person's file, settings and slice and fixes the settings. The design is on the JusPrin v2 canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ), page \"On boarding experience\", version 89: boards `first-run-welcome-01..03` and `first-run-04..11`, where 11 is the flow board. PNGs of every board are in `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/` at the repo root of `~/Projects/JusPrin` (untracked; read them from there, never commit them). The decision records are the memory notes `~/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/first-run-value-prop-decisions.md` and `first-run-flow-sequence.md`; read both first.\n\nThe branch `credits-integration-2026-11` (five commits on today's `jusprin-newui`, checked out by another session in `.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding`, which you must not touch) already ports an older onboarding into Home: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OnboardingModel.{hpp,cpp}` (a pure step function with tests in `tests/jusprin/test_onboarding_model.cpp`), `OrcaHomeBackend.cpp` (OrcaSlicer folder detection `detect_orca_profiles`, preset import `use_detected_profiles`, `choose_offline_example` installing a Generic Klipper printer, progress persisted in AppConfig section `kOnboardingSection`, `complete_onboarding`), `HomeHost.cpp` (the `onboarding_*` messages), and `HomeUI/src/components/Onboarding.tsx` (the old screens). Its screens and strings came from retired Figma frames and are superseded. Kenneth's words: \"probably a good idea to branch off of credits-integration-2026-11 instead of commit directly to it.\" Your worktree is cut from that branch; commit there, never to the branch itself.\n\nHouse rules that bite: read `AGENTS.md`, `agent-docs/jusprin/README.md`, `fork-stewardship.md` and `design-system.md` before editing; every colour, size and radius comes from the token file through `ShellTheme`, the shell recipes or the CSS variables, never a literal; changes to OrcaSlicer-owned files stay small and additive; untracked working docs at the repo root are never committed or hidden via ignore files; never commit submodules. The Mac is shared by several agent sessions: check `uptime` and `pgrep -fl ninja` before a build, build with `cmake --build build/arm64 --config RelWithDebInfo --target all -- -j4` in your own worktree (configure per the `jusprin-worktree-build` memory note, reusing the deps), one build at a time, never restart a running build. Web bundles are CMake-built and gitignored. The shell harness under `tests/shell/` drives the built app without a screen; the branch's `--fresh-example` mode exercises the old onboarding.","prompt":"Build the decided first-run flow on your branch, keeping the credits branch's onboarding machinery and replacing its screens and step order.\n\nTHE FLOW (board 11; `first-run-flow-sequence.md` has the same in words). Onboarding is a sequence, Welcome → Printers → Home, owned by a controller. The agent doors on the welcome are detours that return into the sequence, never exits.\n\nStep 1, Welcome, a full-window screen with no shell header and no footer, the brand lockup top-left (`resources/jusprin/overlay/images/OrcaSlicer_horizontal_light.svg`, 43 px tall), the clip on the left, and on the right: title \"The AI slicer that fixes failed prints.\", subtitle \"Show it a photo of what went wrong. The agent reads your file, your settings and your slice, changes the settings and slices again.\", a label \"Pick how the agent should think. Change it any time in Preferences › Agent.\", then the doors: a selected card \"Your first month: 500 credits\" / \"An Expert message is 5 credits. Then paid, or your own key.\" / primary button \"Sign in for 500 credits\"; two rows \"Your own API key\" with cost \"Free\" and \"Claude Code or Claude Desktop\" with cost \"Free · MCP server\"; the link \"Just slice for now\". Board PNGs: `welcome-01-clip-beat-1.png`, `04-welcome-sign-in-waiting.png`, `05-welcome-signed-in.png`, `06-preferences-over-welcome.png`.\n- Sign in: start the existing loopback sign-in (`Agent/CloudAccount.hpp`, `CloudSignInMachine`); the card becomes \"Finish signing in in your browser\" with a Cancel link and the other doors dimmed; when the sign-in lands the card reads \"Signed in as <email> · 500 credits\" briefly, then the controller advances to step 2. Cancel restores the card.\n- Own key / MCP: open Preferences › Agent on that section through the shell's existing modal path (`ShellController::request_preferences`); when it closes with a verified key or with Done on the MCP section, advance; closed unfinished, stay on the welcome with nothing chosen. Preferences never navigates; it only closes.\n- Just slice for now: advance to step 2 at once.\n\nStep 2, Printers. The app needs one printer. One of three screens by what the app finds: an OrcaSlicer folder → \"Bring your printers from OrcaSlicer?\" listing printers by name with a filament count, the source folder, Import (primary), Start fresh, Back (board `07-orcaslicer-import.png`; reuse `detect_orca_profiles` and `use_detected_profiles`, importing all kinds, no tick boxes, no partial-import or choose-a-bundle screens); JusPrin v1 import happened → skip the step, the existing welcome-back window shows over Home; neither → the existing add-printer form as this step with a \"Skip, use a default\" link (board `08-add-printer.png`) that installs the default printer (the branch installs Generic Klipper; keep that unless a better default is already defined) and records that it is assumed. Back returns to the welcome; finished detours stay finished. A 3MF opened on first launch still shows the welcome, then skips this step because the file carries its printer.\n\nStep 3, Home, first-run state: after sign-in the agent column shows the connection and the balance (board `09-home-after-sign-in.png`); after Just slice it shows the three doors collapsed under \"Set up the agent\" (board `10-home-after-just-slice.png`); the Printers column lists what was imported, added, or the assumed default marked \"assumed\". Onboarding is marked done only when Home is reached; quitting earlier shows the welcome again next launch with finished detours reflected.\n\nKEEP from the branch: `OnboardingModel` as the controller (rewrite its steps to Welcome, Printers, Hidden and its progress fields to what this flow needs; update `test_onboarding_model.cpp` to the new transitions); the AppConfig persistence and the save fix; `detect_orca_profiles` and `use_detected_profiles`; the printer install in `choose_offline_example`; the v1 `returning_user` fact. REPLACE: `Onboarding.tsx` and its strings; the Welcome → Profiles → ConfirmSetup → Setup → Project order; the rule that a configured agent hides the welcome (the welcome shows once regardless); the \"Explore first\" and \"Dismiss onboarding\" links; the wizard call in `run_manual_setup`; the tick-box, partial-import, choose-bundle and choose-folder screens; the Project step and \"Try the example\". Decide where the welcome lives: the Home web view can host it full-window if the shell header can be hidden for it; if not, say what you chose and why.\n\nTHE CLIP: the real clip is not recorded yet (it must be a recording of the real app). Wire a looping, silent, autoplaying video element at 620×388 and use `design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/animatic/animatic-stringing.mp4` as the placeholder, copied into `resources/jusprin/` and named as a placeholder in the commit message. It contains two CC BY 2.0 photos (`design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/photo/ATTRIBUTION.md`); if the placeholder ships, their credit must appear in the About box or an equivalent visible place.\n\nNOT in scope: the gateway (tsd-enterprise) and ops; the credits UI already on the branch; the five states the design session left undrawn (the MCP door's Preferences state, Home after a 3MF on first launch, the assumed mark on Prepare's chip, the add-printer form's later steps, the welcome after a quit) beyond making them behave per the flow text.\n\nDONE means: the new step function and its tests; HomeUI Vitest and tsc green; `jusprin_tests` and `agent_bridge_tests` green; the shell harness's first-run mode updated to the new sequence and passing; and the real app run on an empty `--datadir` through all four doors on this Mac, with a screenshot of the welcome, the Printers step and Home after Just slice sent back with SendUserFile. Windows and Linux need not run. Commit on your branch in small commits with messages that say what changed and what was tested; open no PR and push nothing unless Kenneth asks. Report what you built, what you could not verify, and any decision you had to make that the boards do not settle."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4089,"cache_read_input_tokens":364738,"output_tokens":3857,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":255},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"ser