{"parentUuid":"82b211b6-7ed4-4e8e-8049-bba04a7251a1","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/animatic/src/composite.py","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/animatic/src/composite.py","content":"\"\"\"Welcome-screen composites. Imports the chosen layout (vp-8) from build3.py, copied unchanged into vp8/, and swaps\nonly its clip for the animatic. build3 renders its own boards on import, so its subprocess call is stubbed out.\"\"\"\nimport subprocess, sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\nHERE = Path(__file__).parent\nsys.path.insert(0, str(HERE / 'vp8'))\n_run = subprocess.run\nsubprocess.run = lambda *a, **k: None\nimport build3\nsubprocess.run = _run\nfor f in ('vp-7-split-equal.html', 'vp-8-split-primary.html'):\n    (HERE / 'vp8' / f).unlink(missing_ok=True)\n\ndef clip(photo, t, half=False, caption=True):\n    q = f'photo={photo}&t={t}' + ('' if caption else '&caption=0')\n    if half:\n        return f'<div style=\"position:relative;width:310px;height:194px;flex:none;border-radius:var(--radius-medium);overflow:hidden;box-shadow:var(--elevation-medium)\"><iframe src=\"animatic.html?{q}\" width=\"620\" height=\"388\" style=\"border:0;display:block;transform:scale(.5);transform-origin:0 0\"></iframe></div>'\n    return f'<div style=\"position:relative;width:620px;height:388px;flex:none;border-radius:var(--radius-medium);overflow:hidden;box-shadow:var(--elevation-medium)\"><iframe src=\"animatic.html?{q}\" width=\"620\" height=\"388\" style=\"border:0;display:block\"></iframe></div>'\n\nassert build3.CLIP in build3.B\nfor photo in ('stringing',):\n    (HERE / f'welcome-{photo}.html').write_text(build3.B.replace(build3.CLIP, clip(photo, 2.2)))\n    for i, t in ((1, 2.2), (2, 4.6), (3, 6.9), ('4a', 8.2), (4, 11.8)):\n        (HERE / f'welcome-half-{photo}-{i}.html').write_text(build3.B.replace(build3.CLIP, clip(photo, t, half=True, caption=False)))\nprint('ok')\n","numLines":26,"startLine":1,"totalLines":26}},"displayPath":"../../../design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/animatic/src/composite.py"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"25a5c0fc-d682-49f6-9fe7-925d66fd32cd","timestamp":"2026-11-03T06:47:35.666Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/animatic/src/composite.py\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t\"\"\"Welcome-screen composites. Imports the chosen layout (vp-8) from build3.py, copied unchanged into vp8/, and swaps\n2\tonly its clip for the animatic. build3 renders its own boards on import, so its subprocess call is stubbed out.\"\"\"\n3\timport subprocess, sys\n4\tfrom pathlib import Path\n5\tHERE = Path(__file__).parent\n6\tsys.path.insert(0, str(HERE / 'vp8'))\n7\t_run = subprocess.run\n8\tsubprocess.run = lambda *a, **k: None\n9\timport build3\n10\tsubprocess.run = _run\n11\tfor f in ('vp-7-split-equal.html', 'vp-8-split-primary.html'):\n12\t    (HERE / 'vp8' / f).unlink(missing_ok=True)\n13\t\n14\tdef clip(photo, t, half=False, caption=True):\n15\t    q = f'photo={photo}&t={t}' + ('' if caption else '&caption=0')\n16\t    if half:\n17\t        return f'<div style=\"position:relative;width:310px;height:194px;flex:none;border-radius:var(--radius-medium);overflow:hidden;box-shadow:var(--elevation-medium)\"><iframe src=\"animatic.html?{q}\" width=\"620\" height=\"388\" style=\"border:0;display:block;transform:scale(.5);transform-origin:0 0\"></iframe></div>'\n18\t    return f'<div style=\"position:relative;width:620px;height:388px;flex:none;border-radius:var(--radius-medium);overflow:hidden;box-shadow:var(--elevation-medium)\"><iframe src=\"animatic.html?{q}\" width=\"620\" height=\"388\" style=\"border:0;display:block\"></iframe></div>'\n19\t\n20\tassert build3.CLIP in build3.B\n21\tfor photo in ('stringing',):\n22\t    (HERE / f'welcome-{photo}.html').write_text(build3.B.replace(build3.CLIP, clip(photo, 2.2)))\n23\t    for i, t in ((1, 2.2), (2, 4.6), (3, 6.9), ('4a', 8.2), (4, 11.8)):\n24\t        (HERE / f'welcome-half-{photo}-{i}.html').write_text(build3.B.replace(build3.CLIP, clip(photo, t, half=True, caption=False)))\n25\tprint('ok')\n26\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"credits-integration-2026-11","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
{"parentUuid":"25a5c0fc-d682-49f6-9fe7-925d66fd32cd","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/first-run-value-prop-decisions.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/first-run-value-prop-decisions.md","content":"---\nname: first-run-value-prop-decisions\ndescription: \"Kenneth's 2026-11-02 decisions on the first launch: the proposition is expert help with a failed print (not simpler slicing); title \\\"The AI slicer that fixes failed prints.\\\"; one split welcome screen, clip left, one primary door over three equal free doors; a 12 s four-beat clip on a stringing Benchy with a clean-boat ending; the wizard is dropped; quick renders beat a design session.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34\n  modified: 2026-11-03T00:07:16.607Z\n---\n\nDecided 2026-11-02 (late), in the session that critiqued the onboarding wizard against the pricing goals.\n\n- **Proposition:** expert help with a printing problem, now, from an agent that can see the person's file, settings and slice and fixes the settings, instead of waiting for a forum reply. Kenneth: \"I feel more strongly about expert help too.\" \"Simpler slicing\" was the other candidate; it is what keeps people, not what brings them.\n- **First launch:** one welcome screen, no wizard, split: the clip on the left, the headline and doors on the right.\n- **Title, chosen 2026-11-02 late evening (\"ok go with a\"):** \"The AI slicer that fixes failed prints.\" Kenneth's brief: the title must be short and say what JusPrin is for, and it must say AI; the earlier \"Your print failed. Ask someone who can see why.\" lost because it named neither the slicer nor the AI. Subtitle for patient readers: \"Show it a photo of what went wrong. The agent reads your file, your settings and your slice, changes the settings and slices again.\" The line \"Pick how the agent should think. Change it any time in Preferences › Agent.\" sits as a label directly above the doors. The runner-up was F, \"Slice with AI. Fix failed prints tonight.\", the only one carrying the no-waiting comparison.\n- **Doors, Kenneth's pick \"One primary\":** the first-month offer card with \"Sign in for 500 credits\" on top, then two equal slim rows, \"Your own API key · Free\" and \"Claude Code or Claude Desktop · Free · MCP server\", then \"Just slice for now\" as a link. Every free door shows its cost; nothing is hidden. Kenneth's worry was feeling pushed to the cloud; the answer is honest cost lines and the reversibility line, not equal pixel size.\n- **The clip:** about 12 s (Kenneth cut it from 25: \"nobody has the patience to wait for it to finish\"), silent, looping. Four beats, one caption each: \"Show it what happened.\" / \"It reads your photo, your file and your slice.\" / \"It changes the settings for you.\" / \"And slices again. Tonight.\" Motion only at beat changes, short holds, last frame longest. The failed print is a real CC BY 2.0 photo of a stringing blue-and-white 3DBenchy (Flickr 19273965123, #3DBenchy account; chosen over a peeled black hull because the strings are failure and cause in one picture); beat 1 shows the intact boat on the plate beside it; beat 3 shows two big settings, Retraction 0.8 → 2 mm and Nozzle 220 → 200 °C; beat 4 is a bar labelled \"Slicing NN%\" that, at 100 %, fades the stringy thumbnail to a clean print of the same boat (Flickr 19239738473, CC BY 2.0), then a green check and \"Sliced · ready · 1 h 34 min · 34 g\". No confetti, no time-lapse. The agent's words and the setting values are placeholders until a live run is recorded for this photo; the shipped clip is a recording of the real app. Photos, crops and credit text: `design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/photo/ATTRIBUTION.md` (CC BY needs a visible credit somewhere in the app).\n- **Logo, header, footer (2026-11-02, late):** the welcome is a full-window screen with no shell header (the breadcrumb and \"Agent not connected\" status read as an error before a choice) and no footer sentence. The brand lockup sits top-left of the window as a corner anchor, 43 px tall (120 px wide, the design-system minimum), the way Stripe, Dropbox, Zoom, Canva and Figma anchor theirs on split sign-in screens; Kenneth called a lockup or lone mark placed inside the content column above the title \"pretty ugly\" and asked to \"check how other products do that\" rather than reinvent. Nine captured first screens are in `design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/logo-refs/`: centred small mark above the title, or wordmark top-left of the window; never a display-size lockup in the content column.\n- **After the welcome:** an OrcaSlicer import belongs on a conditional screen right after the door, asked (not silent like the v1 import in `V1Import/`), shown only when an OrcaSlicer folder exists; the same action lives later in Home's Printers column and the add-printer form. Follow-up screens per door: sign-in in the browser then Home with the agent connected; own key and MCP open Preferences › Agent; Just slice goes to Home with the doors collapsed in the agent column. Not yet drawn: Home after Just slice, the assumed-printer chip.\n- **Wall of text:** under about 30 words outside the clip. The transcript panel that duplicated the clip was the failure.\n- **Method:** Kenneth stopped the design session (\"a lot more effective if we explore this way\"): render a few 1280×800 screens from the app's tokens with headless Chrome, send PNGs, iterate. Renders, clips and generators: `design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/` (untracked: `tagline/`, `animatic/`, `photo/`) and the session scratchpads `vp/build*.py`, `tag/build4.py`, `tag/build5.py`.\n\n**Why:** the wizard asked for commitment before showing value; the proposition decides the headline, the proof and the door order, so it had to be settled first.\n\n**How to apply:** the canvas boards from [[first-run-flow-boards]] (variants A and B) predate these decisions; variant B's welcome is the nearer one but its headline, weighting and proof must follow this note. Say \"AI\" to a first-time visitor and introduce \"the agent\" in the subtitle; keep \"Agent\" explained, never \"trial\", no dollar figure on the offer. Related: [[sign-up-reason-must-be-prominent]], [[show-the-board-when-asking-kenneth]], [[mockup-strings-from-real-output]].\n","numLines":26,"startLine":1,"totalLines":26}},"displayPath":"../../../../../.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/first-run-value-prop-decisions.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"13f0e6ee-f9db-4276-8f5c-1ec678f3c2a7","timestamp":"2026-11-03T06:47:35.666Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/first-run-value-prop-decisions.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t---\n2\tname: first-run-value-prop-decisions\n3\tdescription: \"Kenneth's 2026-11-02 decisions on the first launch: the proposition is expert help with a failed print (not simpler slicing); title \\\"The AI slicer that fixes failed prints.\\\"; one split welcome screen, clip left, one primary door over three equal free doors; a 12 s four-beat clip on a stringing Benchy with a clean-boat ending; the wizard is dropped; quick renders beat a design session.\"\n4\tmetadata:\n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34\n8\t  modified: 2026-11-03T00:07:16.607Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tDecided 2026-11-02 (late), in the session that critiqued the onboarding wizard against the pricing goals.\n12\t\n13\t- **Proposition:** expert help with a printing problem, now, from an agent that can see the person's file, settings and slice and fixes the settings, instead of waiting for a forum reply. Kenneth: \"I feel more strongly about expert help too.\" \"Simpler slicing\" was the other candidate; it is what keeps people, not what brings them.\n14\t- **First launch:** one welcome screen, no wizard, split: the clip on the left, the headline and doors on the right.\n15\t- **Title, chosen 2026-11-02 late evening (\"ok go with a\"):** \"The AI slicer that fixes failed prints.\" Kenneth's brief: the title must be short and say what JusPrin is for, and it must say AI; the earlier \"Your print failed. Ask someone who can see why.\" lost because it named neither the slicer nor the AI. Subtitle for patient readers: \"Show it a photo of what went wrong. The agent reads your file, your settings and your slice, changes the settings and slices again.\" The line \"Pick how the agent should think. Change it any time in Preferences › Agent.\" sits as a label directly above the doors. The runner-up was F, \"Slice with AI. Fix failed prints tonight.\", the only one carrying the no-waiting comparison.\n16\t- **Doors, Kenneth's pick \"One primary\":** the first-month offer card with \"Sign in for 500 credits\" on top, then two equal slim rows, \"Your own API key · Free\" and \"Claude Code or Claude Desktop · Free · MCP server\", then \"Just slice for now\" as a link. Every free door shows its cost; nothing is hidden. Kenneth's worry was feeling pushed to the cloud; the answer is honest cost lines and the reversibility line, not equal pixel size.\n17\t- **The clip:** about 12 s (Kenneth cut it from 25: \"nobody has the patience to wait for it to finish\"), silent, looping. Four beats, one caption each: \"Show it what happened.\" / \"It reads your photo, your file and your slice.\" / \"It changes the settings for you.\" / \"And slices again. Tonight.\" Motion only at beat changes, short holds, last frame longest. The failed print is a real CC BY 2.0 photo of a stringing blue-and-white 3DBenchy (Flickr 19273965123, #3DBenchy account; chosen over a peeled black hull because the strings are failure and cause in one picture); beat 1 shows the intact boat on the plate beside it; beat 3 shows two big settings, Retraction 0.8 → 2 mm and Nozzle 220 → 200 °C; beat 4 is a bar labelled \"Slicing NN%\" that, at 100 %, fades the stringy thumbnail to a clean print of the same boat (Flickr 19239738473, CC BY 2.0), then a green check and \"Sliced · ready · 1 h 34 min · 34 g\". No confetti, no time-lapse. The agent's words and the setting values are placeholders until a live run is recorded for this photo; the shipped clip is a recording of the real app. Photos, crops and credit text: `design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/photo/ATTRIBUTION.md` (CC BY needs a visible credit somewhere in the app).\n18\t- **Logo, header, footer (2026-11-02, late):** the welcome is a full-window screen with no shell header (the breadcrumb and \"Agent not connected\" status read as an error before a choice) and no footer sentence. The brand lockup sits top-left of the window as a corner anchor, 43 px tall (120 px wide, the design-system minimum), the way Stripe, Dropbox, Zoom, Canva and Figma anchor theirs on split sign-in screens; Kenneth called a lockup or lone mark placed inside the content column above the title \"pretty ugly\" and asked to \"check how other products do that\" rather than reinvent. Nine captured first screens are in `design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/logo-refs/`: centred small mark above the title, or wordmark top-left of the window; never a display-size lockup in the content column.\n19\t- **After the welcome:** an OrcaSlicer import belongs on a conditional screen right after the door, asked (not silent like the v1 import in `V1Import/`), shown only when an OrcaSlicer folder exists; the same action lives later in Home's Printers column and the add-printer form. Follow-up screens per door: sign-in in the browser then Home with the agent connected; own key and MCP open Preferences › Agent; Just slice goes to Home with the doors collapsed in the agent column. Not yet drawn: Home after Just slice, the assumed-printer chip.\n20\t- **Wall of text:** under about 30 words outside the clip. The transcript panel that duplicated the clip was the failure.\n21\t- **Method:** Kenneth stopped the design session (\"a lot more effective if we explore this way\"): render a few 1280×800 screens from the app's tokens with headless Chrome, send PNGs, iterate. Renders, clips and generators: `design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/` (untracked: `tagline/`, `animatic/`, `photo/`) and the session scratchpads `vp/build*.py`, `tag/build4.py`, `tag/build5.py`.\n22\t\n23\t**Why:** the wizard asked for commitment before showing value; the proposition decides the headline, the proof and the door order, so it had to be settled first.\n24\t\n25\t**How to apply:** the canvas boards from [[first-run-flow-boards]] (variants A and B) predate these decisions; variant B's welcome is the nearer one but its headline, weighting and proof must follow this note. Say \"AI\" to a first-time visitor and introduce \"the agent\" in the subtitle; keep \"Agent\" explained, never \"trial\", no dollar figure on the offer. Related: [[sign-up-reason-must-be-prominent]], [[show-the-board-when-asking-kenneth]], [[mockup-strings-from-real-output]].\n26\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"credits-integration-2026-11","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
{"parentUuid":"13f0e6ee-f9db-4276-8f5c-1ec678f3c2a7","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/6d33a5c2-733f-4189-ab1a-515789ac1ac2/scratchpad/vp/build2.py","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/6d33a5c2-733f-4189-ab1a-515789ac1ac2/scratchpad/vp/build2.py","content":"\"\"\"Reduced welcome (headline, clip, one button) and the clip's storyboard. Words in frames are the agent's own (j3-opus-photo run).\"\"\"\nimport subprocess, tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom build import HEAD, header, CHROME\n\nHERE = Path(__file__).parent\n\ndef frame(caption, inner, t):\n    return f'''<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--space-8);width:460px\">\n  <div style=\"position:relative;width:460px;height:288px;border-radius:var(--radius-medium);overflow:hidden;background:var(--surface-canvas);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px var(--border-subtle)\">{inner}\n    <div style=\"position:absolute;left:var(--space-12);right:var(--space-12);bottom:var(--space-12);padding:var(--space-8) var(--space-12);background:var(--surface-failure-inverse);color:var(--text-on-failure-primary);border-radius:var(--radius-small)\" class=\"body-bold\">{caption}</div>\n    <div class=\"label\" style=\"position:absolute;right:var(--space-12);top:var(--space-12);color:var(--text-on-failure-primary);background:var(--surface-failure-inverse);padding:2px 6px;border-radius:var(--radius-small)\">{t}</div>\n  </div></div>'''\n\n# Mini app chrome for frames: chat column on the right, plate on the left.\ndef app(left, right):\n    return f'''<div style=\"position:absolute;inset:0;display:flex\">\n  <div style=\"flex:1;background:var(--surface-subtle);position:relative\">{left}</div>\n  <div style=\"width:220px;background:var(--surface-canvas);box-shadow:inset 1px 0 0 0 var(--border-subtle);padding:var(--space-12);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--space-8)\">{right}</div></div>'''\n\nplate = '<div style=\"position:absolute;left:24px;top:40px;width:180px;height:150px;border-radius:var(--radius-small);background:var(--surface-raised);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px var(--border-subtle)\"><div style=\"position:absolute;left:60px;top:40px;width:60px;height:80px;border-radius:30px 30px 10px 10px;background:var(--brand-bloom);opacity:.7\"></div></div>'\nplate_brim = plate.replace('opacity:.7\"></div>', 'opacity:.7\"></div><div style=\"position:absolute;left:46px;top:112px;width:88px;height:10px;border-radius:44px/5px;background:var(--brand-violet);opacity:.5\"></div>')\nphoto = '<div style=\"width:100%;height:70px;border-radius:var(--radius-small);background:url(failed.jpg) center/cover\"></div>'\nyou = lambda t: f'<div class=\"label\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">You</div><div class=\"label\">{t}</div>'\nagent = lambda t: f'<div class=\"label\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">Agent</div><div class=\"label\">{t}</div>'\nsetup = '''<div style=\"margin-top:auto;padding:var(--space-8);background:var(--surface-subtle);border-radius:var(--radius-small)\" class=\"label\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between\"><span style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">Bed</span><b>55 → 60 °C</b></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between\"><span style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">Brim</span><b>5 → 10 mm</b></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between\"><span style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">Fan</span><b>off, layers 1–3</b></div></div>'''\nready = '<div class=\"label\" style=\"margin-top:auto;padding:var(--space-8);background:var(--surface-subtle);border-radius:var(--radius-small)\"><b style=\"color:var(--status-success)\">Sliced · ready</b><br>1 h 34 min · 35 g PLA</div>'\n\nframes = [\n frame('Show it what happened.', app(plate, photo + you('I printed it and it failed. One side of the base lifted off the plate.')), '0:02'),\n frame('It reads your photo, your file and your slice.', app(plate, photo + you('…lifted off the plate.') + agent('Your photo shows the base rings went down, but once one side came loose the nozzle kept printing into thin air. The settings are normal for PLA on textured PEI… the base is narrow and the wall flares out.')), '0:07'),\n frame('It changes the settings for you.', app(plate, agent('Should I apply a wider brim, a warmer bed and slower early walls, and slice again?') + '<div class=\"label-bold\" style=\"color:var(--action-primary)\">Yes, apply them</div>' + setup), '0:13'),\n frame('And slices again. Tonight.', app(plate_brim, agent('I made all four changes and I\\'m slicing the vase again now.') + ready), '0:19'),\n]\n# Note: the \"1 h 34 min · 35 g\" ready line is illustrative; the recorded run's second slice time was not captured in the turn files.\n\nCLIP = '''<div style=\"position:relative;width:640px;height:400px;border-radius:var(--radius-medium);overflow:hidden;box-shadow:var(--elevation-medium)\">''' + app(plate, photo + you('I printed it and it failed. One side of the base lifted off the plate.') + agent('Your photo shows the base rings went down, but once one side came loose the nozzle kept printing into thin air…')) + '''\n  <div style=\"position:absolute;left:var(--space-16);bottom:var(--space-16);padding:var(--space-8) var(--space-12);background:var(--surface-failure-inverse);color:var(--text-on-failure-primary);border-radius:var(--radius-small)\" class=\"body-bold\">It reads your photo, your file and your slice.</div>\n  <div style=\"position:absolute;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;height:4px;background:var(--border-subtle)\"><div style=\"width:30%;height:100%;background:var(--action-primary)\"></div></div>\n</div>'''\n\nwelcome = f'''{HEAD}<div class=\"screen\">{header()}\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;align-items:center;gap:var(--space-32);padding-bottom:var(--space-32)\">\n  <div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:var(--space-8);text-align:center;max-width:720px\">\n    <span class=\"page-title\">Your print failed. Ask someone who can see why.</span>\n    <span class=\"body\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">It reads your file, your settings and your slice, and fixes them for the next try.</span></div>\n  {CLIP}\n  <div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:var(--space-8)\">\n    <span class=\"btn-p body-small-bold\" style=\"padding:var(--space-12) var(--space-24)\">Sign in for 500 credits</span>\n    <span class=\"label\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">Your first month is 500 credits. <span style=\"color:var(--action-primary);font-weight:700\">Own API key</span> · <span style=\"color:var(--action-primary);font-weight:700\">MCP server</span> · <span style=\"color:var(--action-primary);font-weight:700\">Just slice</span></span></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftr\"><span class=\"label\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">Slicing works without an account. The agent needs one, or your own API key.</span></div>\n</div></body></html>'''\n\nboard = f'''{HEAD}<div style=\"width:1000px;padding:var(--space-24);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--space-16);background:var(--surface-canvas)\">\n<span class=\"section\">The clip, 25 seconds, silent, looping</span>\n<div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:460px 460px;gap:var(--space-16)\">{''.join(frames)}</div>\n<span class=\"label\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">A screen recording of the real app in the vase session. The agent's words are its own; captions are the only added text. The ready line in the last frame is illustrative.</span>\n</div></body></html>'''\n\nfor name, html, size in ((('vp-5-reduced-welcome', welcome, '1280,800'), ('vp-6-storyboard', board, '1000,760')) if __name__ == '__main__' else ()):\n    (HERE / f'{name}.html').write_text(html)\n    png = HERE / f'{name}.png'\n    subprocess.run([CHROME, '--headless=new', '--disable-gpu', '--no-first-run', f'--user-data-dir={tempfile.mkdtemp()}', '--hide-scrollbars',\n                    f'--window-size={size}', '--force-device-scale-factor=2', '--virtual-time-budget=4000', f'--screenshot={png}',\n                    f'file://{HERE}/{name}.html'], check=True, capture_output=True, timeout=90)\n    print(png)\n","numLines":71,"startLine":1,"totalLines":71}},"displayPath":"../../../../../../../private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/6d33a5c2-733f-4189-ab1a-515789ac1ac2/scratchpad/vp/build2.py"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3120fff1-796f-4d78-9314-d4d6eef3d78d","timestamp":"2026-11-03T06:47:35.666Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/6d33a5c2-733f-4189-ab1a-515789ac1ac2/scratchpad/vp/build2.py\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t\"\"\"Reduced welcome (headline, clip, one button) and the clip's storyboard. Words in frames are the agent's own (j3-opus-photo run).\"\"\"\n2\timport subprocess, tempfile\n3\tfrom pathlib import Path\n4\tfrom build import HEAD, header, CHROME\n5\t\n6\tHERE = Path(__file__).parent\n7\t\n8\tdef frame(caption, inner, t):\n9\t    return f'''<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--space-8);width:460px\">\n10\t  <div style=\"position:relative;width:460px;height:288px;border-radius:var(--radius-medium);overflow:hidden;background:var(--surface-canvas);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px var(--border-subtle)\">{inner}\n11\t    <div style=\"position:absolute;left:var(--space-12);right:var(--space-12);bottom:var(--space-12);padding:var(--space-8) var(--space-12);background:var(--surface-failure-inverse);color:var(--text-on-failure-primary);border-radius:var(--radius-small)\" class=\"body-bold\">{caption}</div>\n12\t    <div class=\"label\" style=\"position:absolute;right:var(--space-12);top:var(--space-12);color:var(--text-on-failure-primary);background:var(--surface-failure-inverse);padding:2px 6px;border-radius:var(--radius-small)\">{t}</div>\n13\t  </div></div>'''\n14\t\n15\t# Mini app chrome for frames: chat column on the right, plate on the left.\n16\tdef app(left, right):\n17\t    return f'''<div style=\"position:absolute;inset:0;display:flex\">\n18\t  <div style=\"flex:1;background:var(--surface-subtle);position:relative\">{left}</div>\n19\t  <div style=\"width:220px;background:var(--surface-canvas);box-shadow:inset 1px 0 0 0 var(--border-subtle);padding:var(--space-12);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--space-8)\">{right}</div></div>'''\n20\t\n21\tplate = '<div style=\"position:absolute;left:24px;top:40px;width:180px;height:150px;border-radius:var(--radius-small);background:var(--surface-raised);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px var(--border-subtle)\"><div style=\"position:absolute;left:60px;top:40px;width:60px;height:80px;border-radius:30px 30px 10px 10px;background:var(--brand-bloom);opacity:.7\"></div></div>'\n22\tplate_brim = plate.replace('opacity:.7\"></div>', 'opacity:.7\"></div><div style=\"position:absolute;left:46px;top:112px;width:88px;height:10px;border-radius:44px/5px;background:var(--brand-violet);opacity:.5\"></div>')\n23\tphoto = '<div style=\"width:100%;height:70px;border-radius:var(--radius-small);background:url(failed.jpg) center/cover\"></div>'\n24\tyou = lambda t: f'<div class=\"label\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">You</div><div class=\"label\">{t}</div>'\n25\tagent = lambda t: f'<div class=\"label\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">Agent</div><div class=\"label\">{t}</div>'\n26\tsetup = '''<div style=\"margin-top:auto;padding:var(--space-8);background:var(--surface-subtle);border-radius:var(--radius-small)\" class=\"label\">\n27\t<div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between\"><span style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">Bed</span><b>55 → 60 °C</b></div>\n28\t<div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between\"><span style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">Brim</span><b>5 → 10 mm</b></div>\n29\t<div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between\"><span style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">Fan</span><b>off, layers 1–3</b></div></div>'''\n30\tready = '<div class=\"label\" style=\"margin-top:auto;padding:var(--space-8);background:var(--surface-subtle);border-radius:var(--radius-small)\"><b style=\"color:var(--status-success)\">Sliced · ready</b><br>1 h 34 min · 35 g PLA</div>'\n31\t\n32\tframes = [\n33\t frame('Show it what happened.', app(plate, photo + you('I printed it and it failed. One side of the base lifted off the plate.')), '0:02'),\n34\t frame('It reads your photo, your file and your slice.', app(plate, photo + you('…lifted off the plate.') + agent('Your photo shows the base rings went down, but once one side came loose the nozzle kept printing into thin air. The settings are normal for PLA on textured PEI… the base is narrow and the wall flares out.')), '0:07'),\n35\t frame('It changes the settings for you.', app(plate, agent('Should I apply a wider brim, a warmer bed and slower early walls, and slice again?') + '<div class=\"label-bold\" style=\"color:var(--action-primary)\">Yes, apply them</div>' + setup), '0:13'),\n36\t frame('And slices again. Tonight.', app(plate_brim, agent('I made all four changes and I\\'m slicing the vase again now.') + ready), '0:19'),\n37\t]\n38\t# Note: the \"1 h 34 min · 35 g\" ready line is illustrative; the recorded run's second slice time was not captured in the turn files.\n39\t\n40\tCLIP = '''<div style=\"position:relative;width:640px;height:400px;border-radius:var(--radius-medium);overflow:hidden;box-shadow:var(--elevation-medium)\">''' + app(plate, photo + you('I printed it and it failed. One side of the base lifted off the plate.') + agent('Your photo shows the base rings went down, but once one side came loose the nozzle kept printing into thin air…')) + '''\n41\t  <div style=\"position:absolute;left:var(--space-16);bottom:var(--space-16);padding:var(--space-8) var(--space-12);background:var(--surface-failure-inverse);color:var(--text-on-failure-primary);border-radius:var(--radius-small)\" class=\"body-bold\">It reads your photo, your file and your slice.</div>\n42\t  <div style=\"position:absolute;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;height:4px;background:var(--border-subtle)\"><div style=\"width:30%;height:100%;background:var(--action-primary)\"></div></div>\n43\t</div>'''\n44\t\n45\twelcome = f'''{HEAD}<div class=\"screen\">{header()}\n46\t<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;align-items:center;gap:var(--space-32);padding-bottom:var(--space-32)\">\n47\t  <div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:var(--space-8);text-align:center;max-width:720px\">\n48\t    <span class=\"page-title\">Your print failed. Ask someone who can see why.</span>\n49\t    <span class=\"body\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">It reads your file, your settings and your slice, and fixes them for the next try.</span></div>\n50\t  {CLIP}\n51\t  <div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:var(--space-8)\">\n52\t    <span class=\"btn-p body-small-bold\" style=\"padding:var(--space-12) var(--space-24)\">Sign in for 500 credits</span>\n53\t    <span class=\"label\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">Your first month is 500 credits. <span style=\"color:var(--action-primary);font-weight:700\">Own API key</span> · <span style=\"color:var(--action-primary);font-weight:700\">MCP server</span> · <span style=\"color:var(--action-primary);font-weight:700\">Just slice</span></span></div>\n54\t</div>\n55\t<div class=\"ftr\"><span class=\"label\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">Slicing works without an account. The agent needs one, or your own API key.</span></div>\n56\t</div></body></html>'''\n57\t\n58\tboard = f'''{HEAD}<div style=\"width:1000px;padding:var(--space-24);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--space-16);background:var(--surface-canvas)\">\n59\t<span class=\"section\">The clip, 25 seconds, silent, looping</span>\n60\t<div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:460px 460px;gap:var(--space-16)\">{''.join(frames)}</div>\n61\t<span class=\"label\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">A screen recording of the real app in the vase session. The agent's words are its own; captions are the only added text. The ready line in the last frame is illustrative.</span>\n62\t</div></body></html>'''\n63\t\n64\tfor name, html, size in ((('vp-5-reduced-welcome', welcome, '1280,800'), ('vp-6-storyboard', board, '1000,760')) if __name__ == '__main__' else ()):\n65\t    (HERE / f'{name}.html').write_text(html)\n66\t    png = HERE / f'{name}.png'\n67\t    subprocess.run([CHROME, '--headless=new', '--disable-gpu', '--no-first-run', f'--user-data-dir={tempfile.mkdtemp()}', '--hide-scrollbars',\n68\t                    f'--window-size={size}', '--force-device-scale-factor=2', '--virtual-time-budget=4000', f'--screenshot={png}',\n69\t                    f'file://{HERE}/{name}.html'], check=True, capture_output=True, timeout=90)\n70\t    print(png)\n71\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"credits-integration-2026-11","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
{"parentUuid":"3120fff1-796f-4d78-9314-d4d6eef3d78d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/6d33a5c2-733f-4189-ab1a-515789ac1ac2/scratchpad/vp/build3.py","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/6d33a5c2-733f-4189-ab1a-515789ac1ac2/scratchpad/vp/build3.py","content":"\"\"\"Split welcome: clip left, doors right. Two weightings of the doors.\"\"\"\nimport subprocess, tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom build import HEAD, header, CHROME\nfrom build2 import app, plate_brim, agent, ready\n\nHERE = Path(__file__).parent\n\n# Clip frame at its held final beat (the frame most often seen peripherally).\nCLIP = '''<div style=\"position:relative;width:620px;height:388px;border-radius:var(--radius-medium);overflow:hidden;box-shadow:var(--elevation-medium)\">''' + app(plate_brim, '<div style=\"width:100%;height:70px;border-radius:var(--radius-small);background:url(failed.jpg) center/cover;opacity:.9\"></div>' + agent('I made all four changes and I\\'m slicing the vase again now.') + ready) + '''\n  <div style=\"position:absolute;left:var(--space-16);bottom:var(--space-16);padding:var(--space-8) var(--space-12);background:var(--surface-failure-inverse);color:var(--text-on-failure-primary);border-radius:var(--radius-small)\" class=\"body-bold\">And slices again. Tonight.</div>\n  <div style=\"position:absolute;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;height:4px;background:var(--border-subtle)\"><div style=\"width:84%;height:100%;background:var(--action-primary)\"></div></div>\n</div>'''\n\ndef door(title, cost, primary=False, small=False):\n    if primary:\n        return f'''<div class=\"card sel\" style=\"padding:var(--space-16);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--space-4)\">\n  <span class=\"section\">{title}</span><span class=\"body-small\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">{cost}</span>\n  <span class=\"btn-p body-small-bold\" style=\"align-self:flex-start;margin-top:var(--space-8)\">Sign in for 500 credits</span></div>'''\n    cls = 'body-small' if small else 'body-bold'\n    pad = 'var(--space-8) var(--space-16)' if small else 'var(--space-12) var(--space-16)'\n    return f'''<div class=\"card\" style=\"padding:{pad};display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:var(--space-16)\">\n  <span class=\"{cls}\">{title}</span><span class=\"label\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary);white-space:nowrap\">{cost}</span></div>'''\n\ndef equal_door(title, cost, grow=1.0, shrink=False):\n    pad = 'var(--space-12) var(--space-16)' if not shrink else 'var(--space-8) var(--space-16)'\n    return f'''<div class=\"card{' sel' if grow>1 else ''}\" style=\"padding:{pad};display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--space-4);transform:scale({grow});transform-origin:left center\">\n  <span class=\"{'body-small' if shrink else 'body-bold'}\">{title}</span><span class=\"label\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">{cost}</span></div>'''\n\nHEADLINE = '''<span class=\"page-title\">Your print failed. Ask someone who can see why.</span>\n<span class=\"body\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">Pick how the agent should think. Change it any time in Preferences › Agent.</span>'''\n\ndef screen(doors):\n    return f'''{HEAD}<div class=\"screen\">{header()}\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;justify-content:center;align-items:center;padding-bottom:var(--space-32)\">\n <div style=\"width:1120px;display:flex;gap:var(--space-48);align-items:center\">\n  {CLIP}\n  <div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--space-20)\">\n   <div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--space-8)\">{HEADLINE}</div>\n   <div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--space-8)\">{doors}</div>\n  </div>\n </div></div>\n<div class=\"ftr\"><span class=\"label\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">Slicing works without an account. The agent needs one, or your own API key.</span></div>\n</div></body></html>'''\n\n# Kenneth's weighting: four nearly equal, cloud slightly bigger, just-slice slightly smaller.\nA = screen(''.join([\n  equal_door('JusPrin cloud', '500 credits in your first month, then paid', grow=1.06),\n  equal_door('Your own API key', 'Free. OpenAI, Anthropic, OpenRouter or DeepSeek'),\n  equal_door('Claude Code or Claude Desktop', 'Free. Connect JusPrin as an MCP server'),\n  equal_door('Just slice for now', 'No agent. Set one up later from Preferences', shrink=True),\n]))\n# One primary, three equal secondaries, just-slice as a link.\nB = screen(''.join([\n  door('Your first month: 500 credits', 'An Expert message is 5 credits. Then paid, or your own key.', primary=True),\n  door('Your own API key', 'Free'),\n  door('Claude Code or Claude Desktop', 'Free · MCP server'),\n  '<span class=\"label-bold\" style=\"color:var(--action-primary);padding:var(--space-4) 0\">Just slice for now</span>',\n]))\n\nfor name, html in (('vp-7-split-equal', A), ('vp-8-split-primary', B)):\n    (HERE / f'{name}.html').write_text(html)\n    png = HERE / f'{name}.png'\n    subprocess.run([CHROME, '--headless=new', '--disable-gpu', '--no-first-run', f'--user-data-dir={tempfile.mkdtemp()}', '--hide-scrollbars',\n                    '--window-size=1280,800', '--force-device-scale-factor=2', '--virtual-time-budget=4000', f'--screenshot={png}',\n                    f'file://{HERE}/{name}.html'], check=True, capture_output=True, timeout=90)\n    print(png)\n","numLines":68,"startLine":1,"totalLines":68}},"displayPath":"../../../../../../../private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/6d33a5c2-733f-4189-ab1a-515789ac1ac2/scratchpad/vp/build3.py"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"47602d68-3ceb-4eba-9ed7-406b54790b99","timestamp":"2026-11-03T06:47:35.666Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/6d33a5c2-733f-4189-ab1a-515789ac1ac2/scratchpad/vp/build3.py\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t\"\"\"Split welcome: clip left, doors right. Two weightings of the doors.\"\"\"\n2\timport subprocess, tempfile\n3\tfrom pathlib import Path\n4\tfrom build import HEAD, header, CHROME\n5\tfrom build2 import app, plate_brim, agent, ready\n6\t\n7\tHERE = Path(__file__).parent\n8\t\n9\t# Clip frame at its held final beat (the frame most often seen peripherally).\n10\tCLIP = '''<div style=\"position:relative;width:620px;height:388px;border-radius:var(--radius-medium);overflow:hidden;box-shadow:var(--elevation-medium)\">''' + app(plate_brim, '<div style=\"width:100%;height:70px;border-radius:var(--radius-small);background:url(failed.jpg) center/cover;opacity:.9\"></div>' + agent('I made all four changes and I\\'m slicing the vase again now.') + ready) + '''\n11\t  <div style=\"position:absolute;left:var(--space-16);bottom:var(--space-16);padding:var(--space-8) var(--space-12);background:var(--surface-failure-inverse);color:var(--text-on-failure-primary);border-radius:var(--radius-small)\" class=\"body-bold\">And slices again. Tonight.</div>\n12\t  <div style=\"position:absolute;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;height:4px;background:var(--border-subtle)\"><div style=\"width:84%;height:100%;background:var(--action-primary)\"></div></div>\n13\t</div>'''\n14\t\n15\tdef door(title, cost, primary=False, small=False):\n16\t    if primary:\n17\t        return f'''<div class=\"card sel\" style=\"padding:var(--space-16);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--space-4)\">\n18\t  <span class=\"section\">{title}</span><span class=\"body-small\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">{cost}</span>\n19\t  <span class=\"btn-p body-small-bold\" style=\"align-self:flex-start;margin-top:var(--space-8)\">Sign in for 500 credits</span></div>'''\n20\t    cls = 'body-small' if small else 'body-bold'\n21\t    pad = 'var(--space-8) var(--space-16)' if small else 'var(--space-12) var(--space-16)'\n22\t    return f'''<div class=\"card\" style=\"padding:{pad};display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:var(--space-16)\">\n23\t  <span class=\"{cls}\">{title}</span><span class=\"label\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary);white-space:nowrap\">{cost}</span></div>'''\n24\t\n25\tdef equal_door(title, cost, grow=1.0, shrink=False):\n26\t    pad = 'var(--space-12) var(--space-16)' if not shrink else 'var(--space-8) var(--space-16)'\n27\t    return f'''<div class=\"card{' sel' if grow>1 else ''}\" style=\"padding:{pad};display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--space-4);transform:scale({grow});transform-origin:left center\">\n28\t  <span class=\"{'body-small' if shrink else 'body-bold'}\">{title}</span><span class=\"label\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">{cost}</span></div>'''\n29\t\n30\tHEADLINE = '''<span class=\"page-title\">Your print failed. Ask someone who can see why.</span>\n31\t<span class=\"body\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">Pick how the agent should think. Change it any time in Preferences › Agent.</span>'''\n32\t\n33\tdef screen(doors):\n34\t    return f'''{HEAD}<div class=\"screen\">{header()}\n35\t<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;justify-content:center;align-items:center;padding-bottom:var(--space-32)\">\n36\t <div style=\"width:1120px;display:flex;gap:var(--space-48);align-items:center\">\n37\t  {CLIP}\n38\t  <div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--space-20)\">\n39\t   <div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--space-8)\">{HEADLINE}</div>\n40\t   <div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--space-8)\">{doors}</div>\n41\t  </div>\n42\t </div></div>\n43\t<div class=\"ftr\"><span class=\"label\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">Slicing works without an account. The agent needs one, or your own API key.</span></div>\n44\t</div></body></html>'''\n45\t\n46\t# Kenneth's weighting: four nearly equal, cloud slightly bigger, just-slice slightly smaller.\n47\tA = screen(''.join([\n48\t  equal_door('JusPrin cloud', '500 credits in your first month, then paid', grow=1.06),\n49\t  equal_door('Your own API key', 'Free. OpenAI, Anthropic, OpenRouter or DeepSeek'),\n50\t  equal_door('Claude Code or Claude Desktop', 'Free. Connect JusPrin as an MCP server'),\n51\t  equal_door('Just slice for now', 'No agent. Set one up later from Preferences', shrink=True),\n52\t]))\n53\t# One primary, three equal secondaries, just-slice as a link.\n54\tB = screen(''.join([\n55\t  door('Your first month: 500 credits', 'An Expert message is 5 credits. Then paid, or your own key.', primary=True),\n56\t  door('Your own API key', 'Free'),\n57\t  door('Claude Code or Claude Desktop', 'Free · MCP server'),\n58\t  '<span class=\"label-bold\" style=\"color:var(--action-primary);padding:var(--space-4) 0\">Just slice for now</span>',\n59\t]))\n60\t\n61\tfor name, html in (('vp-7-split-equal', A), ('vp-8-split-primary', B)):\n62\t    (HERE / f'{name}.html').write_text(html)\n63\t    png = HERE / f'{name}.png'\n64\t    subprocess.run([CHROME, '--headless=new', '--disable-gpu', '--no-first-run', f'--user-data-dir={tempfile.mkdtemp()}', '--hide-scrollbars',\n65\t                    '--window-size=1280,800', '--force-device-scale-factor=2', '--virtual-time-budget=4000', f'--screenshot={png}',\n66\t                    f'file://{HERE}/{name}.html'], check=True, capture_output=True, timeout=90)\n67\t    print(png)\n68\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"credits-integration-2026-11","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
