{"parentUuid":"21b71d29-9849-4add-ba6b-0b2ebbb3c2fc","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e2e91100-76b3-486d-b8c2-2d0b03ac4407","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 1\n# First-run flow: live checks still to do\n\nBranch `claude/first-run-flow-f7be35` (commits ae9cf1f2ac, b8fd2727d9, 7d68c4f91b, 914e48b77f). The build is at\n`.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35/build/arm64/src/Release/OrcaSlicer.app`.\n\nThe screen was locked for most of the run. WebKit does not run the pages of a hidden window, so the built app's Home page could not be driven. These doors were not run in the built app:\n\n1. Your own API key. Preferences should open on Agent. Closing it unfinished should leave the welcome.\n2. Claude Code or Claude Desktop. Done should move to Printers. Pressing Done for real means connecting a tool, which writes to the real Claude config, so send `shell_action {action:'close', done:'tool'}` from the Preferences page instead.\n3. Just slice. This should show the OrcaSlicer import step. Then test Back, Start fresh, and \"Skip, use a default\", which should land on Home with the doors and an \"assumed\" Generic Klipper.\n4. Import. This should land on Home with the imported printers.\n\nThe OrcaSlicer import step appears only when a folder named `OrcaSlicer` sits next to the data folder. With `--datadir X/JusPrin`, put a copy at `X/OrcaSlicer`, holding `user/`, `system/`, and an `OrcaSlicer.conf` that contains only `app.preset_folder`.\n\nThe method: set `JUSPRIN_HOME_DEV_URL` and `JUSPRIN_AGENT_DEV_URL` to copies of the bundled pages, with an injected script that polls a local server for commands. The scripts are in this session's scratchpad: `drive/server.py`, `drive/run.sh`, and `drive/watch.sh`.\n\nDo NOT press \"Sign in for 500 credits\" on this Mac. The default browser is already signed in to JusPrin as k@obico.io, so the sign-in finishes on its own.\n(eval):1: == not found","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rac4uvxynRSaoDSmNvt6mF"}]},"uuid":"a671037c-bd29-400e-ad33-cd32e115b1f6","timestamp":"2026-11-03T06:48:31.026Z","toolUseResult":"Error: Exit code 1\n# First-run flow: live checks still to do\n\nBranch `claude/first-run-flow-f7be35` (commits ae9cf1f2ac, b8fd2727d9, 7d68c4f91b, 914e48b77f). The build is at\n`.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35/build/arm64/src/Release/OrcaSlicer.app`.\n\nThe screen was locked for most of the run. WebKit does not run the pages of a hidden window, so the built app's Home page could not be driven. These doors were not run in the built app:\n\n1. Your own API key. Preferences should open on Agent. Closing it unfinished should leave the welcome.\n2. Claude Code or Claude Desktop. Done should move to Printers. Pressing Done for real means connecting a tool, which writes to the real Claude config, so send `shell_action {action:'close', done:'tool'}` from the Preferences page instead.\n3. Just slice. This should show the OrcaSlicer import step. Then test Back, Start fresh, and \"Skip, use a default\", which should land on Home with the doors and an \"assumed\" Generic Klipper.\n4. Import. This should land on Home with the imported printers.\n\nThe OrcaSlicer import step appears only when a folder named `OrcaSlicer` sits next to the data folder. With `--datadir X/JusPrin`, put a copy at `X/OrcaSlicer`, holding `user/`, `system/`, and an `OrcaSlicer.conf` that contains only `app.preset_folder`.\n\nThe method: set `JUSPRIN_HOME_DEV_URL` and `JUSPRIN_AGENT_DEV_URL` to copies of the bundled pages, with an injected script that polls a local server for commands. The scripts are in this session's scratchpad: `drive/server.py`, `drive/run.sh`, and `drive/watch.sh`.\n\nDo NOT press \"Sign in for 500 credits\" on this Mac. The default browser is already signed in to JusPrin as k@obico.io, so the sign-in finishes on its own.\n(eval):1: == not found","sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"21b71d29-9849-4add-ba6b-0b2ebbb3c2fc","permissionDec