{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01Fx7UioTfpW8SzPs9UUUq8x","lastSequenceNum":0,"ownerAccountUuid":"7911d73c-5552-4877-a943-6a0eba3d7c4d","ownerOrganizationUuid":"68a648b0-98a4-49c7-902b-ff471f8d1d46"}
{"parentUuid":"8b86dd20-311e-4136-9de8-2f2f7a9112ed","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgfYo5SXy9HP9MnSBLJbk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Opus session [Build the first-run flow on top of the credits branch](#local_cea7b182-1404-4ee3-afa3-e87cbafe7c2d) has finished. The flow you drew (Welcome, then Printers, then Home, with the agent doors as detours that return) is built on branch `claude/first-run-flow-f7be35`, four commits on top of `credits-integration-2026-11`. Nothing is pushed and there is no PR.\n\n**What it did**\n\n- Rewrote the step controller in `OnboardingModel` to the decided order and dropped the old steps, the wizard call, the tick-box and partial-import screens, the example project, and the rule that hid the welcome once an agent was configured.\n- Kept the credits branch's OrcaSlicer detection and import, the Generic Klipper install, the saved progress, and the v1 import fact.\n- Preferences can now close itself after one task (a verified key or a connected AI tool) and tell the caller which happened, so the own-key and MCP doors return to the flow.\n- The welcome plays the placeholder animatic, bundled as `resources/jusprin/welcome/welcome-clip.mp4`. The two CC BY photo credits sit in a \"Photo credits\" disclosure under the clip rather than the About box. The commit says plainly that the clip is a placeholder.\n- Home gained an Agent group above Printers with the three doors, and the default printer carries the \"assumed\" mark.\n\n**Verification.** All test suites pass, and the shell harness runs the whole sequence through the real backend (Just slice, Back, Start fresh, the printer form, Skip, the assumed printer, Home's doors). In the built app on an empty data folder it only got through the welcome, the sign-in door and the add-printer form. The sign-in completed by itself because your browser is already signed in as k@obico.io, so no one should press that button on this Mac during a check. The other six doors were never run in the built app because the screen was locked and WebKit does not run pages in a hidden window. The steps left are in [first-run-flow-live-checks-left.md](first-run-flow-live-checks-left.md), untracked at the repo root. The three screenshots above are the committed pages rendered under Playwright, now saved under `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/built/`.\n\n**Decisions it made that the boards did not settle.** Coming Back already signed in shows a Continue button rather than moving on by itself. The filament count on the OrcaSlicer step is for the whole folder, not per printer. The MCP door counts the agent as set up. The old \"dismissed\" status counts as completed.\n\n**Not built.** Opening a 3MF on first launch should show the welcome and then skip Printers. That is not implemented. Separately, the account card shows no balance after sign-in because the production gateway returns 404 for the account endpoint, which is gateway-side work."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":617,"cache_read_input_tokens":139862,"output_tokens":936,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":617,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":936,"cache_read_input_tokens":139862,"cache_creation_input_tokens":617,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":617},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgfYo59BDDmEgPX8bPJys","requestRef":"e4b9b82a-5f2a-4bfd-aeec-ec310d18c04a","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-1","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMc