edit ledger needs: one-time packs sold as a non-recurring add-on on a placeholder subscription (`pre-paid-detective-hour-pack`, credited from the `invoice_generated` webhook, keyed `inv:<invoice id>`), and per-term included credits keyed `sub:<resource_version>:<suffix>` so a repeated webhook never double-credits. `DetectiveHourTransaction` is a ledger of signed amounts with a `forfeitable` flag; balance is a sum.\npricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md:58:**Desktop app.** `ProviderProfile.hpp` row `jusprin` (default model `slicer-1`, `account_sign_in` true) makes `ProviderAgent` send `X-JusPrin-Turn`, `X-JusPrin-Request` (reply or title) and `X-JusPrin-Chat`. `ProviderAgent::http_error` maps 402 to `quota_exhausted` with the text \"Your JusPrin account has used its Agent allowance for now. See your account for more.\" The Agent page gets `model_catalog` (per provider: models with `efforts`), `chat_model`, `account_status` (sign-in phase only) and `setup_keys` (the signed-in email). `ModelPickers.tsx` draws the per-chat model and effort pickers; `Preferences.tsx` has an `account` section. Print records (`ManufacturingHistory.hpp`, `GcodeRecord` with destinations and prints) live in the project file; nothing about them reaches the server.\npricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md:60:**Cache control.** `AnthropicCodec.cpp` sets `cache_control: {type: ephemeral}` with no `ttl` on the last tool, the system text and the last user message. The append-only chat record (commit 1635438d4f) already makes the slice-finished turn read the whole prior prompt from cache, so only expiry during a pause remains.\npricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md:98:4. Not enough credits: raise, which the gateway answers as 402 with code `credits_exhausted` and the body `{\"balance\": 3, \"cost\": 5, \"plan\": null}`. `errors.py` grows that entry; the old `quota_exhausted` text stays for v1.\npricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md:128:- **Your first month** (decided: about $10, one month, not called a trial): 500 credits, `expires_at` one calendar month after the grant, `source_ref = signup`, created on the person's first v2 request or first `/models` call when they have no lot at all. One per account, ever. No device checks; Obico sign-up already requires a verified email, and a second account to farm another $5 of model cost is not worth defending against now.\npricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md:143:- **Obico discount** (decided: 20%): a Chargebee coupon with `duration_type = forever`, applied at checkout when `user.subscription.active()` is true locally (no live Chargebee retrieve; the v1 code's try/except around one is exactly the kind of swallowed error AGENTS.md forbids). When Obico's `upsert_subscription` handles a cancellation, it removes the coupon from any active `jusprin-credits-` subscription of that person with `Subscription.remove_coupons`. Annual JusPrin plans are not in the decided plan; if added later, the same code path works.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"07b01e51-5771-433b-860d-eae7faebd48a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-flow-f7be35","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
