{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","hash":"965a07ce7e4f664bf6957e14efeaa993ffe0515b61428c6095c60d8d020f4e54","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ERcPGYvbZWDDtUaM1GK1ou","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin && git ls-tree -r --name-only main -- src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin | head -40; echo \"== main grep\"; git grep -n -i -E 'verification|verify|login|sign ?in|sign ?up' main -- src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin 2>/dev/null | grep -v -i test | head -30","description":"Look at the main branch's JusPrin v1 code for the sign-in with a code"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0139CjT64akvGmUz5o9t5MbE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise && git grep -n -i -E 'verification.?code|verify.?code|one.?time.?code|login_code|email.?code|otp' credits-integration-2026-11 -- '*.py' '*.vue' '*.js' 2>/dev/null | grep -v -i -E 'test|builds/|node_modules|chunk-vendors' | head -30","description":"Search the server's source for a code-based sign-in"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011KRGBChAM2oN25ravcs6hj","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin && grep -n -i -E 'verification|verify|code|browser|sign' credits-and-onboarding-handoff-2026-11.md pricing-touchpoints-design-2026-11.md first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md 2>/dev/null | grep -i -E 'verif|code' | head -20","description":"Search the handoff docs for a sign-in with a code"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","hash":"8fdf0b7678163267cb5837e8e497f889ee2988982aec8bbfbfb55c6ec06af3ed","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ERcPGYvbZWDDtUaM1GK1ou","type":"tool_result","content":"src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinChatPanel.cpp\nsrc/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinChatPanel.hpp\nsrc/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp\nsrc/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.hpp\nsrc/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinNotificationManager.cpp\nsrc/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinNotificationManager.hpp\nsrc/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinPlateUtils.cpp\nsrc/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinPlateUtils.hpp\nsrc/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinPresetConfigUtils.cpp\nsrc/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinPresetConfigUtils.hpp\nsrc/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinPricingPlanDialog.cpp\nsrc/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinPricingPlanDialog.hpp\nsrc/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinUtils.cpp\nsrc/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinUtils.hpp\nsrc/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinView3D.cpp\nsrc/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinView3D.hpp\n== main grep\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinChatPanel.cpp:89:    void_action_handlers[\"show_login\"] = &JusPrinChatPanel::handle_show_login;\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinChatPanel.cpp:185:void JusPrinChatPanel::handle_show_login(const nlohmann::json& params) {\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinChatPanel.cpp:187:        wxGetApp().show_jusprin_login();\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinChatPanel.hpp:80:    void handle_show_login(const nlohmann::json& params);\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:1:#include \"JusPrinLoginDialog.hpp\"\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:22:JusPrinLoginDialog::JusPrinLoginDialog()\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:23:    : wxDialog((wxWindow*)(wxGetApp().mainframe), wxID_ANY, \"JusPrin Login\")\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:27:    // Set up the URL for JusPrin login\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:32:        auth_url = base_url + \"/accounts/login/?hide_navbar=true&next=/o/authorize/%3Fresponse_type%3Dtoken%26client_id%3DJusPrin\";\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:39:        wxLogError(\"Could not create JusPrin login webview\");\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:46:    Bind(wxEVT_WEBVIEW_NAVIGATING, &JusPrinLoginDialog::OnNavigationRequest, this, m_browser->GetId());\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:47:    Bind(wxEVT_WEBVIEW_NAVIGATED, &JusPrinLoginDialog::OnNavigationComplete, this, m_browser->GetId());\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:48:    Bind(wxEVT_WEBVIEW_LOADED, &JusPrinLoginDialog::OnDocumentLoaded, this, m_browser->GetId());\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:49:    Bind(wxEVT_WEBVIEW_ERROR, &JusPrinLoginDialog::OnError, this, m_browser->GetId());\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:50:    Bind(wxEVT_WEBVIEW_NEWWINDOW, &JusPrinLoginDialog::OnNewWindow, this, m_browser->GetId());\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:51:    Bind(wxEVT_WEBVIEW_TITLE_CHANGED, &JusPrinLoginDialog::OnTitleChanged, this, m_browser->GetId());\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:52:    Bind(wxEVT_WEBVIEW_FULLSCREEN_CHANGED, &JusPrinLoginDialog::OnFullScreenChanged, this, m_browser->GetId());\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:53:    Bind(wxEVT_WEBVIEW_SCRIPT_MESSAGE_RECEIVED, &JusPrinLoginDialog::OnScriptMessage, this, m_browser->GetId());\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:56:    SetTitle(_L(\"JusPrin Login\"));\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:69:bool JusPrinLoginDialog::run()\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:74:void JusPrinLoginDialog::load_url(wxString& url)\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:86:void JusPrinLoginDialog::OnNavigationRequest(wxWebViewEvent& evt)\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:119:void JusPrinLoginDialog::OnNavigationComplete(wxWebViewEvent& evt)\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:126:void JusPrinLoginDialog::OnDocumentLoaded(wxWebViewEvent& evt)\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:135:void JusPrinLoginDialog::OnNewWindow(wxWebViewEvent& evt)\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:142:void JusPrinLoginDialog::OnTitleChanged(wxWebViewEvent& evt)\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:147:void JusPrinLoginDialog::OnFullScreenChanged(wxWebViewEvent& evt)\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:152:void JusPrinLoginDialog::OnError(wxWebViewEvent& evt)\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:160:void JusPrinLoginDialog::OnScriptMessage(wxWebViewEvent& evt)\nmain:src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/JusPrinLoginDialog.cpp:167:        if (strCmd == \"jusprint_login\") {","is_error":false},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0139CjT64akvGmUz5o9t5MbE","type":"tool_result","content":"(Bash completed with no output)","is_error":false},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011KRGBChAM2oN25ravcs6hj","type":"tool_result","content":"first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md:3:The two no-wizard first-run variants (A: no welcome screen, an anonymous first turn and a sign-in prompt on Send; B: a welcome screen with three equal doors) are withdrawn. On 2026-11-02 Kenneth chose a different first launch from rendered comparisons: one split welcome screen with a looping clip on the left and the words and doors on the right, built around expert help with a failed print. That screen is now on the JusPrin v2 canvas. No code has changed, and nothing here is committed.\nfirst-run-flow-design-2026-11.md:32:| `first-run-11-flow` | The three steps as boxes, an arrow from each door to step 2, the four Printers cases, Back, the quit rule, and the two code facts as footnotes. |\nfirst-run-flow-design-2026-11.md:34:Both code facts on the flow board were checked in the source: the sign-in callback port is `kCloudCallbackPort = 41172` (`src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/CloudAccount.hpp:40`), and the shell opens Preferences with `ShowModal()` and carries on when it closes (`Shell/ShellController.cpp:1438`). PNGs of all eight boards, plus the flow board in dark, are in `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/`.\nfirst-run-flow-design-2026-11.md:66:- **Not drawn in the flow:** the Claude Code or Claude Desktop door's Preferences state (06 draws the key door only), Home after a 3MF opened on first launch, the assumed mark on Prepare's printer chip (10 draws it on Home's printer card), the add-printer form's steps 2 and 3, and the welcome after a quit with a finished detour (it looks like 05 without the advance).\nfirst-run-flow-design-2026-11.md:73:These came from reading the code for the withdrawn variants and still matter for \"Just slice for now\" and the printer order Kenneth decided:\ncredits-and-onboarding-handoff-2026-11.md:25:## 3. Where the code lives\ncredits-and-onboarding-handoff-2026-11.md:74:- **Design tokens.** Every colour, radius, font and control size in UI code comes from the token file through `ShellTheme`, the shell recipes, or the CSS variables (`agent-docs/jusprin/design-system.md`, \"Writing UI code\"). A value with no token gets a token and a guard first. The two-line tooltip on board 2c needs a design-system change, since tooltips are one line today.\ncredits-and-onboarding-handoff-2026-11.md:85:- Report in four parts, under 500 words: the problem, what you built, what you tested and how, what remains. Say plainly what you did not verify.\npricing-touchpoints-design-2026-11.md:61:Kenneth, on the first draft's sentence-and-lines popover: \"Don't reinvent the wheel\", and later, with screenshots of Claude's and ChatGPT's usage screens, that both converge on a progress bar per kind of credit. Opinion, as drawn: in the composer only a small ring of what is left, \"just like how claude code behaves\", with no number beside it and no animation. Hovering or tapping it opens the panel: the total in credits only (\"562 credits left.\"), then one bar per kind of credit with what is left and its date, soonest to expire first (\"First-month credits · 62 of 500 left · Expires 1 Dec\"; \"Free Standard credits · 50 of 50 left · Resets 1 Dec · Standard only\"). Every bar's fill is what is left, ChatGPT's way. Bought credits are drawn as a plain number with no bar (\"Bought credits · 500 left · Never expire\"); Kenneth asked why they get no bar, the design session recommended the plain number because there is no limit to measure against and a \"450 of 500\" bar would change its 500 on every top-up, and he has not answered, so this is open. What the ring itself measures against is also open (the board uses every credit in the balance when each kind started, a placeholder). One line, \"Expiring credits are used first.\", then \"Get more credits\" and \"See usage\". A person with only their own API key sees no ring.\npricing-touchpoints-design-2026-11.md:117:Opinion: show the reward before the work, in the button itself: \"Tell us how it printed · 25 credits\", on the Print history entry beside Print again and Export (8a), absent while printing, one report per G-code. Kenneth pointed at the print-history lesson of 2026-10-27, \"don't assume users can easily go back to the original chat and find the card\" and \"when the print fails, the user is likely in a new chat already\", so the chat's one-line G-code marker keeps its \"history\" link and gets no button. People come back to Home with the part in hand, so the offer is visible before they open Print history (8d): a project card gets the line when its latest G-code has finished and has no report, and it opens Print history filtered to that project; after two weeks the line goes away (the design session's guess at the limit, open). Export-only entries also get the button, because a print from USB never reports back; that sits oddly beside a Home card reading \"Exported once · never printed\" and is open too. The form (8b) opens from the entry and names it (\"Plate 1 · a71f 8c04 → Bambu X1C\"), says what earns the reward (\"A photo of the printed object and a few sentences earn 25 credits.\"), takes the photo, the text and the person's own answer to \"How did it come out?\" (It worked / Partly / It didn't work), which is the report's outcome, not a print state: Print history stays without a failure state (decided 2026-10-27). Print history has no composer, so the confirmation is the entry's own row, \"Report sent · 16:10 · 25 credits added\" (8c), which says nothing about how the print went. A review no longer takes credits back and writes no Account row (Kenneth, 2026-11-02: \"I thought the clawback are removed, rigth?\"). Decided the same day: a report earns 25 credits, one per G-code, with no daily limit and no stop after invalid reports (Kenneth: \"Remove these. on ly keep the 1st one\").\npricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md:12:- Print-report rules, ruled 2026-11-02: of \"25 credits\", \"three rewarded reports a day\" and \"rewards stop after two reports are marked invalid\", Kenneth said \"Remove these. only keep the 1st one\". So 25 credits per report, one report per G-code, nothing else limits earning.\npricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md:14:Untracked working document. It turns the pricing plan Kenneth settled on 2026-11-01 into concrete work on the three codebases involved: the gateway in `tsd-enterprise` (`web_ent/jusprin/v2/`), the Obico server it is built on (`obico-server`, where the v1 credit table lives), and the desktop app (`src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/` and the Agent page under `AgentUI/`). Companion docs: `pricing-mental-model-2026-10.md`, `journey-cost-2026-10.md`, `obico-pro-pricing-data-2026-10.md`, `v1-pricing-data-2026-10.md`.\npricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md:16:Every \"recommend\" below is my opinion; every \"decided\" is Kenneth's. Code facts were read from the checkouts on 2026-11-01 (tsd-enterprise master, JusPrin `jusprin-newui` at 69780c7af4, ops master).\npricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md:46:**Gateway.** `web_ent/jusprin/v2/gateway.py` is a raw ASGI endpoint on daphne (`tsdws-prod`) that streams `POST /ent/jusprin/v2/messages` (Anthropic format) and `/responses` (OpenAI format) to an upstream model. `credits.py` admits each turn: a Redis rate limit of 60 turns a minute per person (`JUSPRIN_V2_TURNS_PER_MINUTE`), then one v1 credit per turn through `consume_credit_for_pipeline` in `obico-server/backend/app/jusprin/ai_credits.py`, which decrements `JusPrinAICredit.ai_credit_used_current_month` against `ai_credit_free_monthly_quota` (50 a month, -1 for unlimited). A turn is every request that carries the same `X-JusPrin-Turn` header; title requests (`X-JusPrin-Request: title`) are free. The Redis keys `seen` and `charged` make the charge idempotent per turn for an hour. Exhaustion is a 402 with code `quota_exhausted`.\npricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md:52:**Billing.** Chargebee, site `obico`. v1 sells `jusprin-unlimited-monthly` ($6.99) and `jusprin-unlimited-annual` ($59.99) through `web_ent/jusprin/jusprin_cb_views.py`: hosted checkout pages, a callback, a webhook that upserts `JusPrinPlan` and flips the v1 quota to -1. An Obico Pro discount coupon (30%) is applied at checkout after a live Chargebee status call. Obico's own code (`web_ent/app_ent/cb_views.py`, `detective_hour_accounting.py`) already has the two patterns the credit ledger needs: one-time packs sold as a non-recurring add-on on a placeholder subscription (`pre-paid-detective-hour-pack`, credited from the `invoice_generated` webhook, keyed `inv:<invoice id>`), and per-term included credits keyed `sub:<resource_version>:<suffix>` so a repeated webhook never double-credits. `DetectiveHourTransaction` is a ledger of signed amounts with a `forfeitable` flag; balance is a sum.\npricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md:58:**Desktop app.** `ProviderProfile.hpp` row `jusprin` (default model `slicer-1`, `account_sign_in` true) makes `ProviderAgent` send `X-JusPrin-Turn`, `X-JusPrin-Request` (reply or title) and `X-JusPrin-Chat`. `ProviderAgent::http_error` maps 402 to `quota_exhausted` with the text \"Your JusPrin account has used its Agent allowance for now. See your account for more.\" The Agent page gets `model_catalog` (per provider: models with `efforts`), `chat_model`, `account_status` (sign-in phase only) and `setup_keys` (the signed-in email). `ModelPickers.tsx` draws the per-chat model and effort pickers; `Preferences.tsx` has an `account` section. Print records (`ManufacturingHistory.hpp`, `GcodeRecord` with destinations and prints) live in the project file; nothing about them reaches the server.\npricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md:60:**Cache control.** `AnthropicCodec.cpp` sets `cache_control: {type: ephemeral}` with no `ttl` on the last tool, the system text and the last user message. The append-only chat record (commit 1635438d4f) already makes the slice-finished turn read the whole prior prompt from cache, so only expiry during a pause remains.\npricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md:98:4. Not enough credits: raise, which the gateway answers as 402 with code `credits_exhausted` and the body `{\"balance\": 3, \"cost\": 5, \"plan\": null}`. `errors.py` grows that entry; the old `quota_exhausted` text stays for v1.\npricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md:128:- **Your first month** (decided: about $10, one month, not called a trial): 500 credits, `expires_at` one calendar month after the grant, `source_ref = signup`, created on the person's first v2 request or first `/models` call when they have no lot at all. One per account, ever. No device checks; Obico sign-up already requires a verified email, and a second account to farm another $5 of model cost is not worth defending against now.\npricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md:143:- **Obico discount** (decided: 20%): a Chargebee coupon with `duration_type = forever`, applied at checkout when `user.subscription.active()` is true locally (no live Chargebee retrieve; the v1 code's try/except around one is exactly the kind of swallowed error AGENTS.md forbids). When Obico's `upsert_subscription` handles a cancellation, it removes the coupon from any active `jusprin-credits-` subscription of that person with `Subscription.remove_coupons`. Annual JusPrin plans are not in the decided plan; if added later, the same code path works.","is_error":false}]}}
