{"parentUuid":"9581e95e-bf17-41d0-9225-34a39eddb673","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f0a006f5-d56d-44ea-9f1d-526ada1ecfad","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014ezfi41XPv51uwEJ7NL8Do","type":"tool_result","content":"  modified: 2026-10-27T20:28:20.888Z\n---\n\nKenneth, 2026-10-20: \"We're not changing Figma anymore. We have migrated to\nCloud artifact.\" The two Claude artifacts are now the design source of truth:\nthe Design System (https://claude.ai/artifact/3zgiix8rAw3rXextQnR5UL) and the\n\"JusPrin v2\" canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/VCEppdwfT7v32W4beUxL1v). They\nstarted as copies of Figma ([[jusprin-claude-design-system-artifact]]), but\nthey are no longer re-synced from it.\n\n**Why:** design changes now happen in the artifacts, so a Figma-based argument\nor a \"change Figma\" proposal points at a dead file.\n\n**How to apply:** check designs by reading the artifact files (Artifact read\nwith `path`, e.g. `project/<page>-<frame>.dc.html` on the canvas); never\nsuggest editing Figma or waiting for Figma seat allowance; when citing a\ndesign, name the artifact board, not a Figma node. Describe what the board\nactually draws, not what a component's internal properties imply: a menu row\nwith no fill or border draws no shape at all, so it is not \"a square row\".\nOlder memories that say \"Figma is the source of truth\"\n([[design-token-sync-decisions]], [[figma-jusprin-v2-file]]) are superseded on\nthat point.\n\n**Restated by Kenneth later on 2026-10-20:** \"from now on, we should assume claude design artifact is the up to date design. figma is out of date.\" Docs changed the same day (uncommitted on jusprin-newui): agent-docs/jusprin/design-system.md no longer points at Figma, and the repo skill .claude/skills/figma-agent-design is marked retired.\n\n**Also frozen (Kenneth, 2026-10-27):** the old Claude Design project \"OrcaSlicer AI redesign concepts\" (claude.ai/design/p/d981c5e2-…, files like `Orca Chat Panel.dc.html`). It is history for how a decision was reached, never the current design. For the chat panel, including G-code entries and print bands, the current boards are the five `main-print-timeline-panel-full*` boards on the canvas's Main Page. **The canvas moved (2026-10-27):** VCEppdwfT7v32W4beUxL1v is itself frozen (\"JusPrin v2 (frozen 2026-10-27)\" title, a `frozen-pointer-*` note on every page). The current canvas is https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, with numbered board names (`main-05-print-timeline-panel-full-no-revert`, `main-07-…full`, `agent-ui-01-timeline-cards-manufacturing-history-state-matrix`) and shared parts as `<dc-import>` components that render.py can't draw. Check the canvas title before editing. On it (version 1793132250-e29e) `plates-26e3-project-print-history` and the state matrix were redrawn to the G-code design (matrix now 3 variants, 772 px tall). I also edited 26e3 on the frozen canvas by mistake (version 1793132033-a81d); at Kenneth's request it was restored byte-for-byte to the original BUILD 1 board in version 1793132895-0706.\n\n**How to apply:** when a memory note, commit message, doc or old plan cites a Figma frame, node id or value, treat it as history and check the artifact board instead. Edit the artifacts directly (recipe in [[jusprin-claude-design-system-artifact]]); never re-sync them from Figma, which would overwrite newer design.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"9ac3c07f-48fd-4eea-8738-a440c6765cd5","timestamp":"2026-11-03T13:49:57.109Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"  modified: 2026-10-27T20:28:20.888Z\n---\n\nKenneth, 2026-10-20: \"We're not changing Figma anymore. We have migrated to\nCloud artifact.\" The two Claude artifacts are now the design source of truth:\nthe Design System (https://claude.ai/artifact/3zgiix8rAw3rXextQnR5UL) and the\n\"JusPrin v2\" canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/VCEppdwfT7v32W4beUxL1v). They\nstarted as copies of Figma ([[jusprin-claude-design-system-artifact]]), but\nthey are no longer re-synced from it.\n\n**Why:** design changes now happen in the artifacts, so a Figma-based argument\nor a \"change Figma\" proposal points at a dead file.\n\n**How to apply:** check designs by reading the artifact files (Artifact read\nwith `path`, e.g. `project/<page>-<frame>.dc.html` on the canvas); never\nsuggest editing Figma or waiting for Figma seat allowance; when citing a\ndesign, name the artifact board, not a Figma node. Describe what the board\nactually draws, not what a component's internal properties imply: a menu row\nwith no fill or border draws no shape at all, so it is not \"a square row\".\nOlder memories that say \"Figma is the source of truth\"\n([[design-token-sync-decisions]], [[figma-jusprin-v2-file]]) are superseded on\nthat point.\n\n**Restated by Kenneth later on 2026-10-20:** \"from now on, we should assume claude design artifact is the up to date design. figma is out of date.\" Docs changed the same day (uncommitted on jusprin-newui): agent-docs/jusprin/design-system.md no longer points at Figma, and the repo skill .claude/skills/figma-agent-design is marked retired.\n\n**Also frozen (Kenneth, 2026-10-27):** the old Claude Design project \"OrcaSlicer AI redesign concepts\" (claude.ai/design/p/d981c5e2-…, files like `Orca Chat Panel.dc.html`). It is history for how a decision was reached, never the current design. For the chat panel, including G-code entries and print bands, the current boards are the five `main-print-timeline-panel-full*` boards on the canvas's Main Page. **The canvas moved (2026-10-27):** VCEppdwfT7v32W4beUxL1v is itself frozen (\"JusPrin v2 (frozen 2026-10-27)\" title, a `frozen-pointer-*` note on every page). The current canvas is https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, with numbered board names (`main-05-print-timeline-panel-full-no-revert`, `main-07-…full`, `agent-ui-01-timeline-cards-manufacturing-history-state-matrix`) and shared parts as `<dc-import>` components that render.py can't draw. Check the canvas title before editing. On it (version 1793132250-e29e) `plates-26e3-project-print-history` and the state matrix were redrawn to the G-code design (matrix now 3 variants, 772 px tall). I also edited 26e3 on the frozen canvas by mistake (version 1793132033-a81d); at Kenneth's request it was restored byte-for-byte to the original BUILD 1 board in version 1793132895-0706.\n\n**How to apply:** when a memory note, commit message, doc or old plan cites a Figma frame, node id or value, treat it as history and check the artifact board instead. Edit the artifacts directly (recipe in [[jusprin-claude-design-system-artifact]]); never re-sync them from Figma, which would overwrite newer design.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9581e95e-bf17-41d0-9225-34a39eddb673","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
