{"parentUuid":"fd2ffd64-668f-4477-995e-d5db4d1e2c75","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011Cgg6usCWAEXThmvo1iLJ7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No, it was not a conscious decision. I never looked at the original onboarding boards when I designed the welcome, and I did not raise the email-code path with you, so it was dropped by omission.\n\nWhat I just confirmed:\n\n- **The original design had it.** The frozen canvas has the boards onboarding-01 (account entry), 02 (email code), 03 (code expired), 04 (Google in the browser) and 05 (browser return blocked). So the old flow offered a code typed into the app and a browser path as the fallback.\n- **The new flow has only the browser path.** The sign-in door opens the system browser and the app polls a loopback callback. I designed it that way because that is what the credits branch's sign-in code does, and the implementation session built what I briefed.\n- **Nothing in the code supports a code today.** Neither the app nor the gateway has a verification-code endpoint. The live Obico sign-up is email and password with a link-based verification, so an in-app code path would be new server work, not a port.\n\nWhether to bring it back is your call. The case for it is the one the old board 05 drew: the browser round trip can fail to return to the app, and a code typed into the app has no such failure. The case against is the server work and a second sign-in path to maintain."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13158,"cache_read_input_tokens":186052,"output_tokens":777,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":382},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13158,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":777,"cache_read_input_tokens":186052,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13158,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13158},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgg6uqus5rTWq6HkhZaL8","requestRef":"afe0b485-eb2d-48c8-bfca-59b09cbe9c73","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-1","type":"assistant","uuid":"9df27cc6-224d-40a1-9865-84ccd2e57617","timestamp":"2026-11-03T13:50:49.128Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
