{"parentUuid":"33b319b4-0281-4880-9d1a-54940c3ca34d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"batching_reminder_sent","text":"First privately list what you need next; then request every item that doesn't depend on another's result in this one response.","model":"claude-fable-5-1","clearAt":"next_user_message"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"f7ed7949-996a-4fc1-88b4-1e8ba14e4d0b","timestamp":"2026-11-03T13:53:10.363Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34/scratchpad/old-onboarding/project","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","hash":"a3aec504f280541fc02f9552eeba8af7cb866d60b0b8ec0f87a20134d81339e3","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Boards 00 to 03 are read. I'll extract the text from the other 21 saved boards in one pass rather than reading the raw HTML."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WG6oPpz7jDBDhopzydsgdP","name":"mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan","input":{"advance":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015ts6TvSVjnLRVfqM6EL8Uw","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34/scratchpad/old-onboarding/project && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re,html,glob\nskip={'onboarding-00-welcome-light','onboarding-01-account-entry-light','onboarding-02-email-code-light','onboarding-03-email-code-expired-light','onboarding-delivery-routes-10a'}\nfor f in sorted(glob.glob('*.dc.html')):\n    name=f.replace('.dc.html','')\n    if name in skip: continue\n    t=open(f).read()\n    body=t.split('<x-dc>',1)[1].split('</x-dc>',1)[0]\n    body=re.sub(r'<style>.*?</style>','',body,flags=re.S)\n    body=re.sub(r'<svg.*?</svg>','',body,flags=re.S)\n    # mark components/buttons\n    body=re.sub(r'<div data-c=\"(Button[^\"]*)\"[^>]*>',r' [\\1] ',body)\n    body=re.sub(r'<div data-c=\"(Field[^\"]*)\"[^>]*>',r' [\\1] ',body)\n    body=re.sub(r'<div data-n=\"([^\"]*)\"[^>]*>',r'\\n§\\1: ',body)\n    txt=re.sub(r'<[^>]+>',' ',body)\n    txt=html.unescape(txt)\n    txt=re.sub(r'[ \\t]+',' ',txt)\n    txt=re.sub(r'\\n\\s*\\n+','\\n',txt)\n    print('=====',name); print(txt.strip()[:3500])\nEOF","description":"Extract the visible text and controls from the remaining old onboarding boards"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","hash":"af6512a8b1680cb3f81a00f126b7c0559272e95cd5af97df621fd90dca2d9ffe","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WG6oPpz7jDBDhopzydsgdP","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Plan updated: step 2 of 3 is in progress."}]},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015ts6TvSVjnLRVfqM6EL8Uw","type":"tool_result","content":"===== ds-field-verification-code\n§State=Empty: Verification code \n§Single code input · six presentation cells: \n§Presentation cell 1 · not an input: \n§Presentation cell 2 · not an input: \n§Presentation cell 3 · not an input: \n§Presentation cell 4 · not an input: \n§Presentation cell 5 · not an input: \n§Presentation cell 6 · not an input: Enter all six digits. \n§State=Hover: Verification code \n§Single code input · six presentation cells: \n§Presentation cell 1 · not an input: \n§Presentation cell 2 · not an input: \n§Presentation cell 3 · not an input: \n§Presentation cell 4 · not an input: \n§Presentation cell 5 · not an input: \n§Presentation cell 6 · not an input: Enter all six digits. \n§State=Focused: Verification code \n§Single code input · six presentation cells: \n§Presentation cell 1 · not an input: \n§Presentation cell 2 · not an input: \n§Presentation cell 3 · not an input: \n§Presentation cell 4 · not an input: \n§Presentation cell 5 · not an input: \n§Presentation cell 6 · not an input: Enter all six digits. \n§State=Filled: Verification code \n§Single code input · six presentation cells: \n§Presentation cell 1 · not an input: 1 \n§Presentation cell 2 · not an input: 2 \n§Presentation cell 3 · not an input: 3 \n§Presentation cell 4 · not an input: 4 \n§Presentation cell 5 · not an input: 5 \n§Presentation cell 6 · not an input: 6 Enter all six digits. \n§State=Error: Verification code \n§Single code input · six presentation cells: \n§Presentation cell 1 · not an input: 1 \n§Presentation cell 2 · not an input: 2 \n§Presentation cell 3 · not an input: 3 \n§Presentation cell 4 · not an input: 4 \n§Presentation cell 5 · not an input: 5 \n§Presentation cell 6 · not an input: 6 Enter all six digits. The code is invalid. Enter six digits. \n§State=Disabled: Verification code \n§Single code input · six presentation cells: \n§Presentation cell 1 · not an input: \n§Presentation cell 2 · not an input: \n§Presentation cell 3 · not an input: \n§Presentation cell 4 · not an input: \n§Presentation cell 5 · not an input: \n§Presentation cell 6 · not an input: Enter all six digits.\n===== main-home-first-run-light\n§home-first-run-light: \n§top-bar: \n§top-bar-left: JusPrin Home \n§top-bar-right: \n§workspace: \n§project-gallery: \n§projects-header: PROJECTS 0 \n§empty-state: Drop a model or project to start STL, 3MF, STEP, OBJ, AMF, SVG or ZIP. JusPrin asks what the part is for, then plans the print for your Bambu Lab A1. New Open… Your projects will appear here, most recent first. \n§printer-cabinet: PRINTERS Bambu Lab A1 Idle PLA + Add printer\n===== onboarding-04-google-in-browser-light\n§04 · Google in browser · Light: \n§Application header: \n§Application identity: JusPrin Agent \n§Agent status: Agent not connected \n§Browser sign-in content: \n§Desktop sign-in: JusPrin desktop application GOOGLE SIGN-IN Finish in your browser. We’ll continue here after sign-in. [Button/Primary:State=Default] Open browser again Use email instead ‹ Cancel Waiting for browser sign-in · Agent not connected \n§System browser window: System browser ‹ accounts.google.com Google Choose an account to continue to JusPrin A alex@example.com › Use another account Representative browser view · Not exact Google UI or controlled by JusPrin. \n§Application footer: Account sign-in is the first step. Agent setup comes next.\n===== onboarding-05-browser-return-blocked-light\n§05 · Browser return blocked · Light: \n§Application header: \n§Application identity: JusPrin Agent \n§Agent status: Agent not connected \n§Browser sign-in content: \n§Desktop sign-in: JusPrin desktop application RETURN TO JUSPRIN We couldn’t return automatically. Your browser sign-in succeeded. Continue the same sign-in here. [Button/Primary:State=Default] Check sign-in Use email instead Checks only the sign-in you started from this device. ‹ Cancel Signed in with Google · Return pending · Agent not connected \n§System browser window: System browser ‹ accounts.google.com Google You’re signed in. Return to JusPrin to continue this sign-in. alex@example.com [Button/Primary:State=Default] Open JusPrin Representative browser view · Not exact Google UI or controlled by JusPrin. \n§Application footer: Account sign-in is the first step. Agent setup comes next.\n===== onboarding-06-account-verified-checking-ai-light\n§06 · Account verified · Checking AI · Light: \n§Application header: \n§Application identity: JusPrin Agent \n§App status: Signed in · Checking Agent \n§Setup content: \n§Setup card: ACCOUNT VERIFIED Getting your agent ready… ✓ Signed in as alex@example.com Checking AI access… Keep setting up locally while Agent is checked. Your next applicable local step will open. Continue locally \n§Application footer: Your account is signed in. Agent access is being checked.\n===== onboarding-07-signed-in-ai-unavailable-light\n§07 · Signed in · AI unavailable · Light: \n§Application header: \n§Application identity: JusPrin Agent \n§App status: Signed in · Agent unavailable \n§Setup content: \n§Setup card: ACCOUNT CONNECTED Your account is ready. AI is taking longer. ✓ Signed in as alex@example.com Agent unavailable Your account and Agent setup stay intact. Continue with the next local step or return to the task you came from. [Button/Primary:State=Default] Try again Continue locally \n§Application footer: Your account is signed in. You can continue without AI.\n===== onboarding-08-connected-resume-setup-light\n§08 · Connected · Resume setup · Light: \n§Application header: \n§Application identity: JusPrin Agent \n§App status: Signed in · Agent connected \n§Setup content: \n§Setup card: ✓ alex@example.com · Agent connected CONTINUE YOUR SETUP Bring your Orca profiles. We found settings you can keep using in JusPrin. Printer profiles Filament profiles [Button/Primary:State=Default] Import and continue Skip for now You can review or remove imported profiles later. \n§Application footer: Profile import is optional. Continue your setup in JusPrin.\n===== onboarding-09-orca-setup-found-light\n§09 · Orca setup found · Light: \n§Application header: \n§Application identity: JusPrin Agent \n§App status: Local mode · Agent not configured \n§Orca import content: \n§Orca import card: BRING YOUR SETTINGS Bring your Orca setup Select the presets to copy into JusPrin. OrcaSlicer local data ~/.config/OrcaSlicer/user/default Example local source · not scanned on this computer PRESETS TO IMPORT 3 selected Printer presets 1 Filament presets 1 Process presets 1 Review selection Bambu Lab A1 · 0.4 mm · Generic PLA · 0.20 mm Standard Copies settings into JusPrin. Orca stays intact. [Button/Primary:State=Default] Import selected [Button/Secondary:State=Default] Choose preset bundle Back Skip for now \n§Application footer: Import is optional. Continue with local setup without Agent.\n===== onboarding-10-confirm-physical-setup-light\n§10 · Confirm physical setup · Light: \n§Application header: \n§Application identity: JusPrin Agent \n§App status: Local mode · Agent not configured \n§Physical setup content: \n§Physical setup card: CONFIRM YOUR SETUP What will you print with? Match these values to the printer and supplies you’ll use. IMPORTED CONFIGURATION Example imported configuration · no printer connected Printer Bambu Lab A1 Nozzle 0.4 mm Plate Textured PEI Plate Material Generic PLA Process preset: 0.20 mm Standard Confirm the installed plate The preset uses Textured PEI. Check the plate on your printer. [Button/Primary:State=Default] Use this setup [Button/Secondary:State=Default] Change or find printer I don’t have a printer here Continue with an offline example. You can slice and check it locally; physical Send stays unavailable. \n§Application footer: Imported presets describe a configuration, not a discovered or connected printer.\n===== onboarding-10a-choose-printer-setup-path-light\n§10A · Choose printer setup path · Light: \n§Application header: \n§Application identity: JusPrin Agent \n§App status: Local mode · Agent not configured \n§Physical setup content: \n§Physical setup card: PRINTER SETUP How would you like to set up your printer? Choose a setup path if you don’t already have a usable configuration. You can continue locally without Agent. [Button/Primary:State=Default] Set up with Agent Identify your printer from a photo, model name, or local network. If Agent isn’t configured, connect it and return to this task. If it’s temporarily unavailable, retry or choose a local path. [Button/Secondary:State=Default] Configure manually Choose the printer model, nozzle, plate, and material yourself. [Button/Link:State=Normal, Appearance=Light] I don’t have a printer here Use a labeled offline example. You can prepare and review it locally. Physical Send stays unavailable without an eligible printer. [Button/Link:State=Normal, Appearance=Light] Back to Orca import Local setup does not require Agent. Printer configuration and connection are separate. \n§Application footer:\n===== onboarding-11-first-project-light\n§11 · First project · Light: \n§Application header: \n§Application identity: JusPrin Agent \n§Agent status: Local mode · Agent not configured \n§Project choice content: \n§Project choice: START A PROJECT Start with something you want to print Choose a project or model from your computer, or start with the example. [Button/Primary:State=Default] Open a project or model Opens the file picker · 3MF, STL or OBJ No file handy? [Button/Secondary:State=Default] Try the example Use the labeled example with local tools. No Agent or physical printer is required. Your source file stays unchanged. Work is saved locally in JusPrin. Back \n§Application footer: No project is open yet. Choose a file or the example to continue to Prepare.\n===== onboarding-11a-project-load-failed-light\n§11A · Project load failed · Light: \n§Reference identification: PROJECT-LOAD RECOVERY REFERENCE Illustrative / static · Sample reason for design only \n§Recovery content: \n§Failure heading: PROJECT LOAD FAILED [Button/Icon:State=Default] Couldn’t open the file. No existing work was replaced. \n§Loader reason: Reason This 3MF archive is incomplete. \n§Recovery actions: [Button/Primary:State=Default] Retry [Button/Secondary:State=Default] Choose another\n===== onboarding-17-no-orca-setup-found-light\n§17 · No Orca setup found · Light: \n§Application header: \n§Application identity: JusPrin Agent \n§App status: Local mode · Agent not configured \n§Orca import content: \n§Orca recovery card: BRING YOUR SETTINGS No Orca setup found No supported local Orca configuration was detected. If you don’t have an Orca setup, you can skip this step. Import from your local files Choose an exported preset bundle, or select your Orca configuration folder manually. Continue with the next local setup step. You don’t need imported settings or Agent. [Button/Primary:State=Default] Choose preset bundle [Button/Secondary:State=Default] Choose folder manually [Button/Link:State=Normal, Appearance=Light] Back [Button/Link:State=Normal, Appearance=Light] Skip for now \n§Application footer: Preset import is optional. Local migration uses fixed rules and does not depend on AI.\n===== onboarding-18-orca-import-partial-result-light\n§18 · Orca import partial result · Light: \n§Application header: \n§Application identity: JusPrin Agent \n§App status: Local mode · Agent not configured \n§Orca import content: \n§Orca import result card: BRING YOUR SETTINGS Some settings need attention OrcaSlicer local data ~/.config/OrcaSlicer/user/default Example source and result · not scanned on this computer Success 2 example items Generic PLA Filament preset · copied into JusPrin 0.20 mm Standard — Tuned → 0.20 mm Standard — Tuned (Orca copy) Conflict resolved: copy renamed and imported. Existing tuned preset kept untouched. Not imported 2 example items Bambu Lab A1 · 0.4 mm Copy failed · preset file could not be read. Retry available. Orca post-processing script Unsupported item · scripts are not imported into JusPrin. Orca source data is unchanged. Only the items in Success are available in JusPrin. [Button/Secondary:State=Default] Retry failed items [Button/Secondary:State=Default] Choose preset bundle [Button/Primary:State=Default] Continue with imported settings \n§Application footer: Continue with the settings that imported successfully. We’ll show only the local setup steps still needed.\n===== onboarding-19a-agent-temporarily-unavailable-light\n§19A · Agent temporarily unavailable · Light: PANE-STATE REFERENCE · PREPARE \n§spacer: Agent \n§spacer: \n§add-button: \n§spacer: \n§kebab-menu: \n§Agent recovery: \n§Availability explanation: Agent temporarily unavailable Agent isn’t available right now Your Agent setup is still configured. Your project and local tools remain available. \n§Recovery actions: [Button/Primary:State=Default] Retry Continue locally Retry won’t reset your account, setup, project, or draft.\n===== onboarding-delivery-behavior-11a\n§Delivery behavior · 11A: Delivery behavior · 11A Retry retains and retries the failed file candidate. Choose another opens the native file picker. Picker cancel or closing this notice returns to the originating onboarding screen or ordinary project task. Existing project/work is not replaced until a new file loads successfully. On success, open/restore the loaded project, then re-evaluate the onboarding gates; if a project is open, skip project selection. Show the native loader reason when available; do not invent one at runtime.\n===== onboarding-delivery-behavior-19a\n§Delivery behavior · 19A: Delivery behavior · pane-state reference Continue locally stays in the originating Prepare workspace. Retry preserves account, configuration, project, and draft. Late setup cancel returns to the originating project or printer/filament task.\n===== onboarding-delivery-contract-guidance-gates-and-contextual-return\n§Delivery contract · Guidance gates and contextua: Guidance gates and contextual return \n§RESTORE, THEN GATE: RESTORE, THEN GATE • Restore saved project, active plate/configuration, draft, and guidance flags before evaluating onboarding. • Agent configured? Skip Agent setup even during an outage. • Profiles already imported? Skip profile import. When there is no authoritative outcome, retain explicit skip/defer or accepted-partial guidance state \n§PERSISTENCE: PERSISTENCE • Use authoritative application state whenever it answers the outcome. • Persist data-folder guidance state only where no natural outcome exists: import deferred/skipped, partial-result acknowledged, offline-example path when it creates no usable saved setup, completion-cue dismissed, and overall onboarding status. • O \n§CALLER-SENSITIVE RETURNS: CALLER-SENSITIVE RETURNS • First-run Continue locally → next applicable local gate. • Late Agent setup Continue locally/cancel → originating project or printer/filament task, preserving project, plate, draft, choices, and pending task. • Prepare Continue locally/Keep exploring → remain in that workspace. • Picker cancel → its originating scree \n§NATIVE BOUNDARIES: NATIVE BOUNDARIES • Local Slice is independent of Agent. • Check print requires a valid slice matching current project, active plate, and configuration; edits/Undo invalidate it. • Restore/derive slice readiness from authoritative result matching, never a standalone persisted boolean. • Retain native Preview, Print/preflight, and explic\n===== onboarding-v1-01-imported-light\n§V1-01 · JusPrin v1 setup imported · Light: \n§Application header: \n§Application identity: JusPrin Welcome \n§App status: Signed in · Agent connected \n§Import content: \n§V1 import card: \n WELCOME BACK Your JusPrin v1 setup is here We copied it from JusPrin v1 on this computer. JusPrin v1 itself is unchanged. \n§Account: Signed in as alex@example.com The same account you used in JusPrin v1 \n§Imported list: \n IMPORTED \n Printers Bambu Lab A1 · Prusa MK4S 2 \n Filament and process presets Generic PLA, Silk PETG, 0.20 mm Strong and 7 more 10 \n Printer connections Prusa MK4S on PrusaLink 1 \n Preferences Units, language and recent files \n Chats from JusPrin v1 stay in JusPrin v1. \n Continue \n§Other source: Also have OrcaSlicer settings? Import from OrcaSlicer \n§Application footer: Imported presets are in your printer and filament menus. Rename or delete them there.\n===== onboarding-v1-02-partly-imported-light\n§V1-02 · JusPrin v1 setup partly imported · Light: \n§Application header: \n§Application identity: JusPrin Welcome \n§App status: Signed in · Agent connected \n§Import content: \n§V1 import card: \n WELCOME BACK Most of your JusPrin v1 setup is here We copied it from JusPrin v1 on this computer. JusPrin v1 itself is unchanged. \n§Account: Signed in as alex@example.com The same account you used in JusPrin v1 \n§Imported list: \n IMPORTED \n Printers Bambu Lab A1 · Prusa MK4S 2 \n Filament and process presets Generic PLA, Silk PETG, 0.20 mm Strong and 6 more 9 of 10 \n Printer connections Bambu Lab A1 needs its access code again. Add it from the printer menu. 1 of 2 \n Preferences Units, language and recent files \n “Fast draft” wasn’t copied: it is based on a printer JusPrin doesn’t have. Chats from JusPrin v1 stay in JusPrin v1. \n Continue \n§Other source: Also have OrcaSlicer settings? Import from OrcaSlicer \n§Application footer: Imported presets are in your printer and filament menus. Rename or delete them there.\n===== onboarding-v1-03-sign-in-expired-light\n§V1-03 · JusPrin v1 sign-in expired · Light: \n§Application header: \n§Application identity: JusPrin Welcome \n§App status: Not signed in · Agent not configured \n§Import content: \n§V1 import card: \n WELCOME BACK Your JusPrin v1 setup is here We copied it from JusPrin v1 on this computer. JusPrin v1 itself is unchanged. \n§Account: Sign in again to use the agent Your JusPrin v1 sign-in for alex@example.com has expired. Continue with JusPrin \n§Imported list: \n IMPORTED \n Printers Bambu Lab A1 · Prusa MK4S 2 \n Filament and process presets Generic PLA, Silk PETG, 0.20 mm Strong and 7 more 10 \n Printer connections Prusa MK4S on PrusaLink 1 \n Preferences Units, language and recent files \n Chats from JusPrin v1 stay in JusPrin v1. \n Continue \n§Other source: Also have OrcaSlicer settings? Import from OrcaSlicer \n§Application footer: Imported presets are in your printer and filament menus. Rename or delete them there.","is_error":false}]}}
