{"parentUuid":"fbe27ee4-ba2e-4e4f-a593-c9096b4f908d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1e41ac36-d262-4aa1-bb95-2f310367df08","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R5MnsQctiM5o6oXBct4BNV","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Plan updated: step 3 of 3 is in progress."}]}]},"uuid":"09ba2403-5e0a-4028-81e6-1c7586f4b54b","timestamp":"2026-11-03T13:53:56.204Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"Plan updated: step 3 of 3 is in progress."}],"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fbe27ee4-ba2e-4e4f-a593-c9096b4f908d","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
{"parentUuid":"09ba2403-5e0a-4028-81e6-1c7586f4b54b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011Cgg7A7RQQBGBJKUw8vKgk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01A2NmVAr8EMUenZMJjHqPap","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/old-onboarding-boards-review.md","content":"---\nname: old-onboarding-boards-review\ndescription: 2026-11-03 review of the original (frozen-canvas) onboarding boards against the built first-run flow; what the old flow had that the new one dropped, and which pieces were judged worth taking back.\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nKenneth asked (2026-11-03) whether the new first-run flow dropped the email-code sign-up on purpose. It did not: the welcome was designed from the credits branch's sign-in code without reading the old boards. He then asked for a look at the old flow for anything worth keeping.\n\n**Where the old flow is:** the frozen canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/VCEppdwfT7v32W4beUxL1v), boards `project/onboarding-00` … `-20`, `onboarding-v1-01..03`, the `onboarding-delivery-*` notes, and the design-system component `ds-field-verification-code`. Text of 26 of them extracted to the session scratchpad `old-onboarding/`.\n\n**What the old flow had that the built flow (claude/first-run-flow-f7be35) lacks:**\n- Sign-in: Google in the browser plus an email code typed in the app (six cells, auto-verify on the sixth digit, expired-code state, Resend / Change email / Use Google instead); a \"couldn't return automatically\" recovery with a Check sign-in button; a Terms and Privacy line. New flow: browser only, a waiting state with Cancel and one error line. No code endpoint exists on the server; the live Obico sign-up is email + password.\n- After sign-in: \"checking AI access\" and \"AI unavailable: Try again / Continue locally\". New flow goes straight to Printers; the account card showed no balance when the gateway 404'd.\n- OrcaSlicer import: choose the folder manually or a preset bundle when nothing is detected; a partial-result screen (conflicts renamed \"(Orca copy)\", failures with reasons, Retry failed items). New flow: one list, Import / Start fresh / Back; conflicts go through a yes/no dialog mid-import.\n- First project: \"Try the example\" (3DBenchy) beside Open. New Home empty state has only New / Open; the example was removed with the Project step.\n- v1 users: a Welcome back card listing what was copied, \"the same account you used in v1\", and a sign-in-expired variant. New flow keeps WelcomeBackWindow separately but the welcome's sign-in door still says \"Your first month: 500 credits\" to everyone.\n- Project load failed: \"No existing work was replaced\", native reason, Retry / Choose another. General file-open behaviour, not onboarding.\n\n**My ranking (Kenneth has not ruled yet):** take the example model on Home's empty state and a v1-aware sign-in door first; then the browser-return recovery and the Terms line; then the import result report. The email code is a server project and a second sign-in path; recommend deferring it.\n\n**How to apply:** when Kenneth rules, record the decision here and in [[first-run-flow-sequence]]; the boards named above are the reference for wording and states. Related: [[first-run-value-prop-decisions]], [[v1-subscribers-grandfathered]].\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4724,"cache_read_input_tokens":233552,"output_tokens":1771,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":324},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4724,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":1771,"cache_read_input_tokens":233552,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4724,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4724},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01A2NmVAr8EMUenZMJjHqPap":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/old-onboarding-boards-review.md","content":"---\nname: old-onboarding-boards-review\ndescription: 2026-11-03 review of the original (frozen-canvas) onboarding boards against the built first-run flow; what the old flow had that the new one dropped, and which pieces were judged worth taking back.\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nKenneth asked (2026-11-03) whether the new first-run flow dropped the email-code sign-up on purpose. It did not: the welcome was designed from the credits branch's sign-in code without reading the old boards. He then asked for a look at the old flow for anything worth keeping.\n\n**Where the old flow is:** the frozen canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/VCEppdwfT7v32W4beUxL1v), boards `project/onboarding-00` … `-20`, `onboarding-v1-01..03`, the `onboarding-delivery-*` notes, and the design-system component `ds-field-verification-code`. Text of 26 of them extracted to the session scratchpad `old-onboarding/`.\n\n**What the old flow had that the built flow (claude/first-run-flow-f7be35) lacks:**\n- Sign-in: Google in the browser plus an email code typed in the app (six cells, auto-verify on the sixth digit, expired-code state, Resend / Change email / Use Google instead); a \"couldn't return automatically\" recovery with a Check sign-in button; a Terms and Privacy line. New flow: browser only, a waiting state with Cancel and one error line. No code endpoint exists on the server; the live Obico sign-up is email + password.\n- After sign-in: \"checking AI access\" and \"AI unavailable: Try again / Continue locally\". New flow goes straight to Printers; the account card showed no balance when the gateway 404'd.\n- OrcaSlicer import: choose the folder manually or a preset bundle when nothing is detected; a partial-result screen (conflicts renamed \"(Orca copy)\", failures with reasons, Retry failed items). New flow: one list, Import / Start fresh / Back; conflicts go through a yes/no dialog mid-import.\n- First project: \"Try the example\" (3DBenchy) beside Open. New Home empty state has only New / Open; the example was removed with the Project step.\n- v1 users: a Welcome back card listing what was copied, \"the same account you used in v1\", and a sign-in-expired variant. New flow keeps WelcomeBackWindow separately but the welcome's sign-in door still says \"Your first month: 500 credits\" to everyone.\n- Project load failed: \"No existing work was replaced\", native reason, Retry / Choose another. General file-open behaviour, not onboarding.\n\n**My ranking (Kenneth has not ruled yet):** take the example model on Home's empty state and a v1-aware sign-in door first; then the browser-return recovery and the Terms line; then the import result report. The email code is a server project and a second sign-in path; recommend deferring it.\n\n**How to apply:** when Kenneth rules, record the decision here and in [[first-run-flow-sequence]]; the boards named above are the reference for wording and states. Related: [[first-run-value-prop-decisions]], [[v1-subscribers-grandfathered]].\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgg7A745kVU8dXgWYtL8h","requestRef":"c58bdb52-40a6-4ff8-b3a6-2bc4b16a73d9","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-1","type":"assistant","uuid":"6d2ba825-3adf-4b2a-873f-a07694b42a3d","timestamp":"2026-11-03T13:54:12.081Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
