{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","id":"c367bfeb-aa85-43a9-b3e4-196de0c9c1c6","timestamp":"2026-11-03T13:54:19.127Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"23f1d61ae8837bf8ac29a6fe9a1adfcdee338dbd56f5f4a09693cb2f7f92a77d","params":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":64000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"a0c280e9-9d33-4a96-acce-4f72b58d9497","keep":124,"tail":["77216d925c9c98073d27bc6cf4b54d2e939e2d727cdb6b387a7d84dce2633082","a0f20721210e9d02ae60950c749d1acaf94849284faf1bd387710d31b1ee3a07","08806fdb83d18ca9b6b308956361adcbfa3c7f9bec98071c41a7572c11db7d88","fd45c40b25ab2bc033d485d0e1d865199e6d98d240b67fae5912b30ba5e3b54c"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",126,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"51e98093cccb13979b6964b53247bf73c01aa693abeadbfc595f7142f7cee83f"}
{"parentUuid":"8951653f-56cf-419b-96dd-132d0f73df96","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011Cgg7CRzf59GxHsjd3YfqW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, and I have now done it. The original flow is the 26 onboarding boards on the frozen canvas. I compared them against what the Opus session built. The old flow was a longer wizard, and most of its length is what you decided against, but six things in it were dropped by omission rather than by decision.\n\n**Worth taking back, in my order**\n\n1. **The example model.** The old \"First project\" screen offered \"Try the example\" beside Open. The new Home empty state has only New and Open, because the example left with the Project step. The welcome clip shows a Benchy, so a person who just watched it gets nothing to click that matches. The credits branch still has the code that opens the bundled Benchy. This is the cheapest and highest-value piece.\n2. **A v1-aware sign-in door.** The old flow had a \"Welcome back\" card that said \"the same account you used in JusPrin v1\" and a variant for an expired v1 sign-in. The new flow still shows the separate Welcome back window, but the welcome's sign-in door says \"Your first month: 500 credits\" to everyone. A grandfathered v1 subscriber reads an offer that is not theirs. The door needs a returning-user variant.\n3. **The browser-return recovery.** The old board \"Browser return blocked\" handled the case where sign-in succeeded in the browser but the app never heard back, with a Check sign-in button and \"Use email instead\". The new waiting state has Cancel and one error line. The loopback callback can be blocked by a firewall or a browser that opens the link in another profile, so this state will happen.\n4. **A Terms and Privacy line** under the sign-in door. The old account screen had it. The new one has nothing, and a sign-up door with an offer on it should.\n5. **An import result.** The old flow reported what imported, what was renamed on conflict, and what failed with a reason, and offered Retry on the failures. The new flow asks a yes/no dialog mid-import for each conflict and shows no summary. Also worth taking from the old board: choose the folder by hand when nothing is detected, for people whose OrcaSlicer data is not in the default place.\n\n**Not worth taking now**\n\n- **The email code.** It is a real alternative to the browser round trip, and the design-system component for it exists. But neither the app nor the server has a code endpoint, and the live Obico sign-up is email and password with a link, so it is a server project and a second sign-in path to keep working. I would defer it and let the browser-return recovery cover the failure it was meant for.\n- The post-sign-in \"checking AI access\" and \"AI unavailable\" screens. The gateway returned 404 for the account endpoint during testing, so the case is real, but it belongs on Home's agent card as a \"try again\" state, not as onboarding screens.\n- The physical-setup confirmation, the offline example path and the preset-bundle import. The \"assumed\" mark and the add-printer form cover what they were for.\n\nThe comparison and the board names are saved in memory so whoever builds the chosen pieces can go to the exact old boards for wording and states."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":333,"cache_read_input_tokens":240329,"output_tokens":977,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":333,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":977,"cache_read_input_tokens":240329,"cache_creation_input_tokens":333,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":333},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgg7CRhJNvgc57epTozxE","requestRef":"c367bfeb-aa85-43a9-b3e4-196de0c9c1c6","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-1","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"c5a8d90a-324b-4297-8d58-39be35141b34","timestamp":"2026-11-03T13:54:36.567Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
{"parentUuid":"c5a8d90a-324b-4297-8d58-39be35141b34","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"stop_hook_summary","hookCount":4,"hookInfos":[{"command":"sh -c 'if ! command -v entire >/dev/null 2>&1; then exit 0; fi; exec entire hooks claude-code stop'","durationMs":18381},{"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-stop.sh","durationMs":62},{"command":"callback"},{"command":"callback"}],"hookErrors":[],"hookAdditionalContext":[],"preventedContinuation":false,"stopReason":"","hasOutput":false,"level":"suggestion","timestamp":"2026-11-03T13:54:58.226Z","uuid":"22ae4a43-cd5d-4b3a-8fa9-ef6fd8fbe5aa","toolUseID":"7f6098ab-4fa1-4888-95b5-7b6fcd84fca9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-flow-f7be35","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-03T14:39:18.571Z","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","content":"<!-- reply 3 -->\n> The example model. The old “First project” screen offered “Try the example” beside Open. The new Home empty state has only New and Open, because the example left with the Project step. The welcome clip shows a Benchy, so a person who just watched it gets nothing to click that matches. The credits branch still has the code that opens the bundled Benchy. This is the cheapest and highest-value piece.\n\nNo need for example models\n\n<!-- reply -->\n> A v1-aware sign-in door. The old flow had a “Welcome back” card that said “the same account you used in JusPrin v1” and a variant for an expired v1 sign-in. The new flow still shows the separate Welcome back window, but the welcome’s sign-in door says “Your first month: 500 credits” to everyone. A grandfathered v1 subscriber reads an offer that is not theirs. The door needs a returning-user variant.\n\nI'm worried that you missed the big chunk of work that we need to keep. Over the past three days we have decided on the pricing model, including the credits, etc. Check the branch that you inherited from to find the recent commits, understand what was built there. If possible, look at what artboards were changed for them as well. We need to make sure we keep all part of the new pricing model ported to our onboaridng flow.\n\n<!-- reply -->\n> The email code. It is a real alternative to the browser round trip, and the design-system component for it exists. But neither the app nor the server has a code endpoint, and the live Obico sign-up is email and password with a link, so it is a server project and a second sign-in path to keep working. I would defer it and let the browser-return recovery cover the failure it was meant for.\n\nThe problem with taking the users of the app into browser is not a the best user experience. Email code keeps the user in the app, right? And it's becoming more and more common and users are getting used to it. let's incorporate this into your design.\n\n\nI agree with all the things you said."}
