{"parentUuid":"7cda6c9f-a9d5-4209-80f0-5d7ad3d68a82","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3b8f975a-379e-4fed-8a28-01d66198f3b3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XUgXwqmr8gkXLJF1MBvvPb","type":"tool_result","content":"# Handoff: build JusPrin Cloud credits and finish the first-run onboarding\n\n**Decided 2026-11-02 evening, after Kenneth saw canvas version 73. These override anything below that says otherwise.**\n- Every credit is the same. There is no Standard-only lot. Any mention below of a `basic_only` flag, a \"trickle\" of Standard-only credits, \"Free Standard messages\" or \"Free Standard credits\" is superseded. free accounts (not subscribed) get 50 credits a month, expiring one month after grant, that pay for either tier; Kenneth to the design session: \"the 'everyone gets 50 credits' wording is wrong. I never said that.\" (Kenneth: \"let's just give free users 50/mo use-it-or-loose it credits\").\n- Workshop has no ceiling. Standard messages cost 0 credits on Workshop (Kenneth: \"no ceiling. It's probably easier just to say standard messages cost 0 credits\"). Anything below about 600, fair use, or a notice at 500 or 600 is superseded.\n- A balance is one number of credits, never a count of messages beside it. The panel shows one bar per lot, grouped only by when the credits expire: \"First-month credits · 62 of 500 left · Expires 1 Dec\", \"Bought credits · 500 of 500 left · Never expire\". Bought credits get a bar like the others (decision 13 closed).\n- \"New Standard chat\" and board 3d are gone: the case only existed because a Standard-only lot could not pay for an Expert chat. A chat that cannot be paid offers \"Get more credits\" only.\n- Prices in messages appear only on the picker options, the stop card for the chat's own tier, the pricing page's one sentence, the low-balance notice, and one scale line under the first-month offer (\"An Expert message is 5 credits\").\n- Kenneth reviewed the list of mechanisms that were mine, not his (2026-11-02, late evening). **Kept:** the launch offer (double credits on packs until a date); the low-balance notice, reworded to \"About 25 credits left\" (credits, not messages); \"Expiring credits are used first\" in the panel; the \"Alert me when a subscription would save me money\" switch, on by default; the Account page shape (30-day total, bar chart per day, table of chats); Standard as the default tier for a new chat after the first month; the v1 welcome-back fill-ins; the print-report form details; alias ids `slicer-1` and `slicer-basic` with image stripping. **Dropped:** the reverse savings alert and board 7c; the month-end and 7-day expiry notices (rule 4 on board 0 loses them); the daily cap on free app turns; the thinking picker on Standard (Expert only). **Expiry:** every expiring lot expires one month from the day it was granted, never at a calendar month end: first-month credits a month after sign-in, the free 50 a month after each grant, plan credits with the billing cycle.\n- Free credits, ruled 2026-11-02 late: \"no 50 credits for first month. only 500 initial credits. pack holders also get 50 credits a month.\" So the 50 a month goes to every account not on a subscription, starting after the first month; a pack holder gets it; during the first month there is only the 500. The balance example on 2a, 4a and 4b is 62 first-month + 500 bought = 562, with no Free credits bar. Footer: \"After your first month, accounts without a plan get 50 free credits a month.\"\n\nWritten 2026-11-02 for a coding agent who has not seen the design sessions. This is a working doc: keep it untracked, never commit it, never add it to `.gitignore` or `.git/info/exclude`. Kenneth tracks unfinished work by the untracked files in `git status`.\n\n## 1. What you are building, in one paragraph\n\nJusPrin 2 is a fork of OrcaSlicer with an in-app AI agent. The agent can run on the person's own API key (free, no account) or on JusPrin's hosted gateway (an Obico-server endpoint, `app.obico.io/ent/jusprin/v2/…`, live in production since 2026-10-25). The gateway is about to start charging in credits: a Standard message costs 1 credit, an Expert message 5. People get 500 credits in their first month, can buy packs that never expire, or subscribe (Hobby $10, Workshop $20). This work adds the credit ledger and charging to the gateway, the balance, prices and pre-send checks to the app's composer, the Account and pricing pages, print-report rewards, and finishes the first-run onboarding flow that a month-old branch started. Nothing of this is built yet; the design is done and reviewed.\n\n## 2. Read these first, in this order\n\n1. `pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md` (same folder). The whole technical plan: ledger tables, the charging algorithm, the `/account` JSON, the 402 body, alias config, Chargebee, rewards, section 11 \"Order of work and tests\", section 12 \"Decisions still Kenneth's\". Build from it.\n2. `pricing-touchpoints-design-2026-11.md`. Each point where a person meets credits, the five rules that apply everywhere, and the exact wording. When the plan and this doc disagree on words, this doc wins.\n3. The boards. Captures in `design-captures/credits-2026-11/` (one PNG per board, `credits-<board>-<slug>.png`, `-dark` variants where they exist). `MANIFEST.md` there lists every board with its canvas page and name; `CHANGELOG-v54-to-v69.md` records why each board looks the way it does. The live canvas is the JusPrin v2 design artifact, https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, at version 71. Figma is retired; do not design from it.\n4. `AGENTS.md` and `agent-docs/jusprin/README.md`, `fork-stewardship.md`, `design-system.md`. House rules; the ones that bite most often are repeated in section 7 below.\n\n## 3. Where the code lives\n\nYou run on Kenneth's Mac, the machine the design sessions ran on, so every path below is live. The three repositories are checked out here and on GitHub: the app at `~/Projects/JusPrin` (`git@github.com:TheSpaghettiDetective/JusPrin.git`, branch `jusprin-newui`), the gateway at `~/Projects/tsd-enterprise` (`git@github.com:kennethjiang/tsd-enterprise.git`, branch `master`, with `obico-server` as a submodule), and deployment at `~/Projects/ops` (`git@github.com:kennethjiang/ops.git`). Other agent sessions work in these checkouts at the same time: make your own worktree for each repository you change, never reuse one you did not create, and touch nothing in the main checkouts themselves. The working docs this brief names sit untracked at the root of `~/Projects/JusPrin`; read them from there and leave them where they are.\n\n**App (this repository).** Branch `jusprin-newui` at `69780c7af4`, in sync with `origin`. Work in your own worktree and branch; never reuse another session's worktree.\n- Composer, pickers, attachments, Preferences page: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/` (`Composer.tsx`, `ModelPickers.tsx`, `AttachmentChip.tsx`, `Preferences.tsx`, `WelcomeBack.tsx`).\n- Host side of the agent: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/` (`AgentHost.cpp` holds `chat_model_choice`, `use_chat_model`, `start_turn`; `ProviderAgent` sends the gateway headers and maps HTTP errors; `CloudAccount.cpp` and `ModelCatalog.cpp` hold the account's model list).\n- Home page and onboarding: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/` and `HomeUI/src/`. Preferences window: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Preferences/`. The v1 import and the welcome-back window: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/V1Import/`.\n- Tests: Catch2 under `tests/jusprin/` and `tests/brand/`; Vitest beside each TypeScript file; the shell harness under `tests/shell/` drives the built app without a screen.\n- Build: `cmake --build build/arm64 --config RelWithDebInfo --target all -- -j4`. The Mac is shared by several agent sessions: check `uptime` and `pgrep -fl ninja` first, one build per build directory, never restart a running build. Editing a CMake file rebuilds everything.\n\n**Gateway (tsd-enterprise).** Repository `~/Projects/tsd-enterprise`, branch from `master` (it moved 12 commits past the gateway merge, including the Python 3.12 / Django 5.2 bump), in your own worktree. The gateway is `web_ent/jusprin/v2/` (`aliases.py`, `upstream.py`, `gateway.py`, `stream.py`, `credits.py`, `auth.py`, `errors.py`, `views.py`, `urls.py`; tests in `tests/test_gateway.py` and `tests/test_aliases.py`, using the MockTransport injection the file already uses). `obico-server` is a git submodule: never stage or commit a submodule change. The local stack from the previous session is compose project `jusprin-cloud` on port 3434 (`docker-compose.local-ports.yml` in `~/Projects/tsd-enterprise-worktrees/jusprin-cloud`, whose `LOCAL_TEST_ACCOUNT.txt` holds a test account), with `web_ent/scripts/jusprin/fake_upstream.py --port 8765` standing in for the model vendor. The session cookie is scoped to `.localhost`, so pass it as a header from scripts.\n\n**Deployment (ops).** `~/Projects/ops`: the alias ConfigMap is `tsd/prod/jusprin-v2-gateway.yaml` and `tsd/stg/jusprin-v2-gateway.yaml`. Staging is `https://app-stg.obico.io` and runs the same image as production. Production is live for real users: do not change it. For any `gcloud` or `kubectl` command, first run `gcloud config set account ai-agent@tsdtechnology.iam.gserviceaccount.com`, and stay read-only on production.\n\n## 4. Step 0: the onboarding branch\n\n`onboarding-frontend-only` (one commit, `8f4588beae`, Kenneth, 2026-10-06; `origin/onboarding-frontend-only` is identical) adds the local first-run path to Home: welcome, import presets from an existing OrcaSlicer install, confirm or choose a printer setup, open a project or the bundled example. Its commit message is a good spec of what it does and what it deliberately left out. It is 139 commits behind `jusprin-newui`.\n\nA dry-run rebase on 2026-11-02 conflicted in 18 of its 27 files. Expect to resolve `HomeBackend.hpp`, `HomeHost.cpp`, `HomeHost.hpp`, `HomeSnapshot.hpp`, `OrcaHomeBackend.cpp`, `OrcaHomeBackend.hpp`, `resources/jusprin/home/protocol.json`, `HomeUI/src/App.tsx`, `App.test.tsx`, `bridge/protocol.ts`, `bridge/protocol.test.ts`, `state/store.ts`, `styles.css`, `styles.test.ts`, `tokens.ts`, `sources.cmake`, `tests/jusprin/test_home_host.cpp` and `test_home_snapshot.cpp`. Nine files apply cleanly, among them the three new ones (`OnboardingModel.cpp/.hpp`, `Onboarding.tsx`, `test_onboarding_model.cpp`). What changed underneath: the Home v3 page (`dbec3e3a38`), Print history (`ebbb2f8894`), JusPrin's own Preferences window (`641c17f13e`), every opened file becomes a new project (`d921c4b3dd`), the token sync (`7671e48504`). Most conflicts should be two additive hunks in the same place; keep both.\n\nAfter the rebase, bring the flow to the current design:\n- The canvas's \"On boarding experience\" page is the source of truth. The branch followed Figma frames; check each of its eight screens against the canvas before trusting its layout.\n- Boards 1a to 1d add the first-month offer as the headline on its own surface: \"Your first month: 500 credits\", under it \"An Expert message is 5 credits. Your own API key stays free.\", button \"Sign in for 500 credits\", \"Explore first\" below. 1a is the setup row in Preferences › Agent over a first-run Home, 1b the welcome screen, 1c the welcome-back window the app already builds for a returning v1 user (signing in is the primary button there), 1d that window once a v1 subscriber has signed in. Never the word \"trial\"; no dollar figure.\n- The branch's \"Set up JusPrin\" and \"Set up with Agent\" links to jusprin.com/account go away: since 2026-10-23 every entry point to agent setup opens Preferences › Agent.\n- The branch left two paths unverified in the real app: a preset import that leaves some presets behind, and staying on Home when the bundled example fails to open. Show both before calling the step done.\n\n## 5. Then the credits work, in the plan's order\n\nSection 11 of the plan has the steps and their tests. Summary of what each needs and what it waits on:\n\n| Step | What | Waits on |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Gateway ledger and charging, the `slicer-basic` alias with image stripping, `/account`, the 402 body | Nothing. Start here on the server side. |\n| 2 | App: prices in the pickers, pickers greyed after the person's first message, app-started turns on Expert without fixing the chat's model, the attachment row's picture notice, the ring and hover panel, the pre-send check, the failed card | Step 1's `/account` and 402 shapes, which the plan fixes already. The webview that opens Account and pricing waits with step 3. |\n| 3 | Chargebee plans, add-ons, coupon, webhooks; the Account and pricing pages; v1-subscriber carry-over | Kenneth's decisions 12 (pages served into a webview, or built in the app), 10 (domain) and the open parts of 8 (when v1 subscribers move, how to word it). Do not start the pages until he has answered. |\n| 4 | Cache ttl and the slice-polling guard | Nothing. |\n| 5 | Print-report rewards: endpoint, storage, admin review, the Print history button and form, the Home card line | Nothing; Print history exists on `jusprin-newui`. |\n| 6 | Savings alert, auto-reload, launch bonus | Steps 1 and 3. |\n\nSteps 0, 1, 2, 4 and 5 can be built now. Steps 1 and 2 can run in parallel in different repositories.\n\n## 6. Decisions you must not make yourself\n\nThe plan's section 12 lists them. The ones with a recommended or placeholder answer written in the plan (default tier, alias ids, the 50-a-day cap, the 50-credit trickle, the 600 ceiling, the 25-credit reward, the launch discount form, bars and the ring's total, \"New Standard chat\", the picture in a new chat, the thinking picker on Standard) you build as written and flag in your report. The ones with no answer (webview or in-app pages, the domain, v1 move timing and wording, Pix) you leave alone and ask Kenneth. If a board, the design doc and the plan disagree, say so rather than picking.\n\n## 7. Rules that bite\n\n- **Words.** The cheap tier is \"Standard\" everywhere a person reads (the config value stays `basic`, the alias id `slicer-basic`, the flag `basic_only`). Prices always carry their unit: \"1 credit a message\", never \"1 credit\". \"Your first month\", never \"trial\". Only messages the person sends cost credits. \"Get more credits\" is the one action outside the pricing page. A file is \"opened\", \"imported\", \"loaded\" or \"added\", never \"arrived\". Text the model reads calls the product \"the app\", never Orca. `AgentUI/src/wording.test.ts` guards some of this; extend it when you add model-facing text.\n- **Design tokens.** Every colour, radius, font and control size in UI code comes from the token file through `ShellTheme`, the shell recipes, or the CSS variables (`agent-docs/jusprin/design-system.md`, \"Writing UI code\"). A value with no token gets a token and a guard first. The two-line tooltip on board 2c needs a design-system change, since tooltips are one line today.\n- **OrcaSlicer-owned files.** Read `agent-docs/jusprin/fork-stewardship.md` before touching anything outside `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/`. Changes there are small, additive, and come with the rebase evidence that document asks for.\n- **Errors.** Do not catch what you cannot recover from; never turn an impossible state into a silent no-op; one generic error for rare failures. Section \"Error handling discipline\" in `AGENTS.md`.\n- **Tests.** Every behaviour change gets a test, and the real app must be exercised for anything a test cannot cover. Reproduce a bug in the real app before fixing it; a failing fake is not a reproduction.\n- **Model spend.** No live-model run (the shell harness against a real provider, the live prompt suite) without Kenneth approving that batch and its stated spend. The staging gateway at `app-stg.obico.io` counts.\n- **Git.** Commit only when asked; never commit submodule pointers; no attribution lines in commits or PR descriptions; working docs like this one stay untracked.\n\n## 8. How you will know it works\n\n- Gateway: the pytest list in plan section 11 step 1, plus one end-to-end run through the local compose stack with `fake_upstream.py`: sign-up lot created on first contact, a Standard turn charges 1 from the expiring lot first, an Expert turn skips basic-only credits, the 402 body carries `basic_only_credits`, an app-origin turn charges 0.\n- App: Vitest for `ModelPickers`, the new balance panel, the composer's disabled Send, the attachment row in a Standard chat; Catch2 for `ProviderAgent`'s headers and 402 handling and for an app-started turn leaving the chat's model unset until the person's first message; the Home and onboarding suites from the branch; one shell-harness run against staging at a spend Kenneth approves.\n- Report in four parts, under 500 words: the problem, what you built, what you tested and how, what remains. Say plainly what you did not verify.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8a5e5a9d-fd1a-429b-b18e-9841aaa783f9","timestamp":"2026-11-03T14:40:13.331Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Handoff: build JusPrin Cloud credits and finish the first-run onboarding\n\n**Decided 2026-11-02 evening, after Kenneth saw canvas version 73. These override anything below that says otherwise.**\n- Every credit is the same. There is no Standard-only lot. Any mention below of a `basic_only` flag, a \"trickle\" of Standard-only credits, \"Free Standard messages\" or \"Free Standard credits\" is superseded. free accounts (not subscribed) get 50 credits a month, expiring one month after grant, that pay for either tier; Kenneth to the design session: \"the 'everyone gets 50 credits' wording is wrong. I never said that.\" (Kenneth: \"let's just give free users 50/mo use-it-or-loose it credits\").\n- Workshop has no ceiling. Standard messages cost 0 credits on Workshop (Kenneth: \"no ceiling. It's probably easier just to say standard messages cost 0 credits\"). Anything below about 600, fair use, or a notice at 500 or 600 is superseded.\n- A balance is one number of credits, never a count of messages beside it. The panel shows one bar per lot, grouped only by when the credits expire: \"First-month credits · 62 of 500 left · Expires 1 Dec\", \"Bought credits · 500 of 500 left · Never expire\". Bought credits get a bar like the others (decision 13 closed).\n- \"New Standard chat\" and board 3d are gone: the case only existed because a Standard-only lot could not pay for an Expert chat. A chat that cannot be paid offers \"Get more credits\" only.\n- Prices in messages appear only on the picker options, the stop card for the chat's own tier, the pricing page's one sentence, the low-balance notice, and one scale line under the first-month offer (\"An Expert message is 5 credits\").\n- Kenneth reviewed the list of mechanisms that were mine, not his (2026-11-02, late evening). **Kept:** the launch offer (double credits on packs until a date); the low-balance notice, reworded to \"About 25 credits left\" (credits, not messages); \"Expiring credits are used first\" in the panel; the \"Alert me when a subscription would save me money\" switch, on by default; the Account page shape (30-day total, bar chart per day, table of chats); Standard as the default tier for a new chat after the first month; the v1 welcome-back fill-ins; the print-report form details; alias ids `slicer-1` and `slicer-basic` with image stripping. **Dropped:** the reverse savings alert and board 7c; the month-end and 7-day expiry notices (rule 4 on board 0 loses them); the daily cap on free app turns; the thinking picker on Standard (Expert only). **Expiry:** every expiring lot expires one month from the day it was granted, never at a calendar month end: first-month credits a month after sign-in, the free 50 a month after each grant, plan credits with the billing cycle.\n- Free credits, ruled 2026-11-02 late: \"no 50 credits for first month. only 500 initial credits. pack holders also get 50 credits a month.\" So the 50 a month goes to every account not on a subscription, starting after the first month; a pack holder gets it; during the first month there is only the 500. The balance example on 2a, 4a and 4b is 62 first-month + 500 bought = 562, with no Free credits bar. Footer: \"After your first month, accounts without a plan get 50 free credits a month.\"\n\nWritten 2026-11-02 for a coding agent who has not seen the design sessions. This is a working doc: keep it untracked, never commit it, never add it to `.gitignore` or `.git/info/exclude`. Kenneth tracks unfinished work by the untracked files in `git status`.\n\n## 1. What you are building, in one paragraph\n\nJusPrin 2 is a fork of OrcaSlicer with an in-app AI agent. The agent can run on the person's own API key (free, no account) or on JusPrin's hosted gateway (an Obico-server endpoint, `app.obico.io/ent/jusprin/v2/…`, live in production since 2026-10-25). The gateway is about to start charging in credits: a Standard message costs 1 credit, an Expert message 5. People get 500 credits in their first month, can buy packs that never expire, or subscribe (Hobby $10, Workshop $20). This work adds the credit ledger and charging to the gateway, the balance, prices and pre-send checks to the app's composer, the Account and pricing pages, print-report rewards, and finishes the first-run onboarding flow that a month-old branch started. Nothing of this is built yet; the design is done and reviewed.\n\n## 2. Read these first, in this order\n\n1. `pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md` (same folder). The whole technical plan: ledger tables, the charging algorithm, the `/account` JSON, the 402 body, alias config, Chargebee, rewards, section 11 \"Order of work and tests\", section 12 \"Decisions still Kenneth's\". Build from it.\n2. `pricing-touchpoints-design-2026-11.md`. Each point where a person meets credits, the five rules that apply everywhere, and the exact wording. When the plan and this doc disagree on words, this doc wins.\n3. The boards. Captures in `design-captures/credits-2026-11/` (one PNG per board, `credits-<board>-<slug>.png`, `-dark` variants where they exist). `MANIFEST.md` there lists every board with its canvas page and name; `CHANGELOG-v54-to-v69.md` records why each board looks the way it does. The live canvas is the JusPrin v2 design artifact, https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, at version 71. Figma is retired; do not design from it.\n4. `AGENTS.md` and `agent-docs/jusprin/README.md`, `fork-stewardship.md`, `design-system.md`. House rules; the ones that bite most often are repeated in section 7 below.\n\n## 3. Where the code lives\n\nYou run on Kenneth's Mac, the machine the design sessions ran on, so every path below is live. The three repositories are checked out here and on GitHub: the app at `~/Projects/JusPrin` (`git@github.com:TheSpaghettiDetective/JusPrin.git`, branch `jusprin-newui`), the gateway at `~/Projects/tsd-enterprise` (`git@github.com:kennethjiang/tsd-enterprise.git`, branch `master`, with `obico-server` as a submodule), and deployment at `~/Projects/ops` (`git@github.com:kennethjiang/ops.git`). Other agent sessions work in these checkouts at the same time: make your own worktree for each repository you change, never reuse one you did not create, and touch nothing in the main checkouts themselves. The working docs this brief names sit untracked at the root of `~/Projects/JusPrin`; read them from there and leave them where they are.\n\n**App (this repository).** Branch `jusprin-newui` at `69780c7af4`, in sync with `origin`. Work in your own worktree and branch; never reuse another session's worktree.\n- Composer, pickers, attachments, Preferences page: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/` (`Composer.tsx`, `ModelPickers.tsx`, `AttachmentChip.tsx`, `Preferences.tsx`, `WelcomeBack.tsx`).\n- Host side of the agent: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/` (`AgentHost.cpp` holds `chat_model_choice`, `use_chat_model`, `start_turn`; `ProviderAgent` sends the gateway headers and maps HTTP errors; `CloudAccount.cpp` and `ModelCatalog.cpp` hold the account's model list).\n- Home page and onboarding: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/` and `HomeUI/src/`. Preferences window: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Preferences/`. The v1 import and the welcome-back window: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/V1Import/`.\n- Tests: Catch2 under `tests/jusprin/` and `tests/brand/`; Vitest beside each TypeScript file; the shell harness under `tests/shell/` drives the built app without a screen.\n- Build: `cmake --build build/arm64 --config RelWithDebInfo --target all -- -j4`. The Mac is shared by several agent sessions: check `uptime` and `pgrep -fl ninja` first, one build per build directory, never restart a running build. Editing a CMake file rebuilds everything.\n\n**Gateway (tsd-enterprise).** Repository `~/Projects/tsd-enterprise`, branch from `master` (it moved 12 commits past the gateway merge, including the Python 3.12 / Django 5.2 bump), in your own worktree. The gateway is `web_ent/jusprin/v2/` (`aliases.py`, `upstream.py`, `gateway.py`, `stream.py`, `credits.py`, `auth.py`, `errors.py`, `views.py`, `urls.py`; tests in `tests/test_gateway.py` and `tests/test_aliases.py`, using the MockTransport injection the file already uses). `obico-server` is a git submodule: never stage or commit a submodule change. The local stack from the previous session is compose project `jusprin-cloud` on port 3434 (`docker-compose.local-ports.yml` in `~/Projects/tsd-enterprise-worktrees/jusprin-cloud`, whose `LOCAL_TEST_ACCOUNT.txt` holds a test account), with `web_ent/scripts/jusprin/fake_upstream.py --port 8765` standing in for the model vendor. The session cookie is scoped to `.localhost`, so pass it as a header from scripts.\n\n**Deployment (ops).** `~/Projects/ops`: the alias ConfigMap is `tsd/prod/jusprin-v2-gateway.yaml` and `tsd/stg/jusprin-v2-gateway.yaml`. Staging is `https://app-stg.obico.io` and runs the same image as production. Production is live for real users: do not change it. For any `gcloud` or `kubectl` command, first run `gcloud config set account ai-agent@tsdtechnology.iam.gserviceaccount.com`, and stay read-only on production.\n\n## 4. Step 0: the onboarding branch\n\n`onboarding-frontend-only` (one commit, `8f4588beae`, Kenneth, 2026-10-06; `origin/onboarding-frontend-only` is identical) adds the local first-run path to Home: welcome, import presets from an existing OrcaSlicer install, confirm or choose a printer setup, open a project or the bundled example. Its commit message is a good spec of what it does and what it deliberately left out. It is 139 commits behind `jusprin-newui`.\n\nA dry-run rebase on 2026-11-02 conflicted in 18 of its 27 files. Expect to resolve `HomeBackend.hpp`, `HomeHost.cpp`, `HomeHost.hpp`, `HomeSnapshot.hpp`, `OrcaHomeBackend.cpp`, `OrcaHomeBackend.hpp`, `resources/jusprin/home/protocol.json`, `HomeUI/src/App.tsx`, `App.test.tsx`, `bridge/protocol.ts`, `bridge/protocol.test.ts`, `state/store.ts`, `styles.css`, `styles.test.ts`, `tokens.ts`, `sources.cmake`, `tests/jusprin/test_home_host.cpp` and `test_home_snapshot.cpp`. Nine files apply cleanly, among them the three new ones (`OnboardingModel.cpp/.hpp`, `Onboarding.tsx`, `test_onboarding_model.cpp`). What changed underneath: the Home v3 page (`dbec3e3a38`), Print history (`ebbb2f8894`), JusPrin's own Preferences window (`641c17f13e`), every opened file becomes a new project (`d921c4b3dd`), the token sync (`7671e48504`). Most conflicts should be two additive hunks in the same place; keep both.\n\nAfter the rebase, bring the flow to the current design:\n- The canvas's \"On boarding experience\" page is the source of truth. The branch followed Figma frames; check each of its eight screens against the canvas before trusting its layout.\n- Boards 1a to 1d add the first-month offer as the headline on its own surface: \"Your first month: 500 credits\", under it \"An Expert message is 5 credits. Your own API key stays free.\", button \"Sign in for 500 credits\", \"Explore first\" below. 1a is the setup row in Preferences › Agent over a first-run Home, 1b the welcome screen, 1c the welcome-back window the app already builds for a returning v1 user (signing in is the primary button there), 1d that window once a v1 subscriber has signed in. Never the word \"trial\"; no dollar figure.\n- The branch's \"Set up JusPrin\" and \"Set up with Agent\" links to jusprin.com/account go away: since 2026-10-23 every entry point to agent setup opens Preferences › Agent.\n- The branch left two paths unverified in the real app: a preset import that leaves some presets behind, and staying on Home when the bundled example fails to open. Show both before calling the step done.\n\n## 5. Then the credits work, in the plan's order\n\nSection 11 of the plan has the steps and their tests. Summary of what each needs and what it waits on:\n\n| Step | What | Waits on |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Gateway ledger and charging, the `slicer-basic` alias with image stripping, `/account`, the 402 body | Nothing. Start here on the server side. |\n| 2 | App: prices in the pickers, pickers greyed after the person's first message, app-started turns on Expert without fixing the chat's model, the attachment row's picture notice, the ring and hover panel, the pre-send check, the failed card | Step 1's `/account` and 402 shapes, which the plan fixes already. The webview that opens Account and pricing waits with step 3. |\n| 3 | Chargebee plans, add-ons, coupon, webhooks; the Account and pricing pages; v1-subscriber carry-over | Kenneth's decisions 12 (pages served into a webview, or built in the app), 10 (domain) and the open parts of 8 (when v1 subscribers move, how to word it). Do not start the pages until he has answered. |\n| 4 | Cache ttl and the slice-polling guard | Nothing. |\n| 5 | Print-report rewards: endpoint, storage, admin review, the Print history button and form, the Home card line | Nothing; Print history exists on `jusprin-newui`. |\n| 6 | Savings alert, auto-reload, launch bonus | Steps 1 and 3. |\n\nSteps 0, 1, 2, 4 and 5 can be built now. Steps 1 and 2 can run in parallel in different repositories.\n\n## 6. Decisions you must not make yourself\n\nThe plan's section 12 lists them. The ones with a recommended or placeholder answer written in the plan (default tier, alias ids, the 50-a-day cap, the 50-credit trickle, the 600 ceiling, the 25-credit reward, the launch discount form, bars and the ring's total, \"New Standard chat\", the picture in a new chat, the thinking picker on Standard) you build as written and flag in your report. The ones with no answer (webview or in-app pages, the domain, v1 move timing and wording, Pix) you leave alone and ask Kenneth. If a board, the design doc and the plan disagree, say so rather than picking.\n\n## 7. Rules that bite\n\n- **Words.** The cheap tier is \"Standard\" everywhere a person reads (the config value stays `basic`, the alias id `slicer-basic`, the flag `basic_only`). Prices always carry their unit: \"1 credit a message\", never \"1 credit\". \"Your first month\", never \"trial\". Only messages the person sends cost credits. \"Get more credits\" is the one action outside the pricing page. A file is \"opened\", \"imported\", \"loaded\" or \"added\", never \"arrived\". Text the model reads calls the product \"the app\", never Orca. `AgentUI/src/wording.test.ts` guards some of this; extend it when you add model-facing text.\n- **Design tokens.** Every colour, radius, font and control size in UI code comes from the token file through `ShellTheme`, the shell recipes, or the CSS variables (`agent-docs/jusprin/design-system.md`, \"Writing UI code\"). A value with no token gets a token and a guard first. The two-line tooltip on board 2c needs a design-system change, since tooltips are one line today.\n- **OrcaSlicer-owned files.** Read `agent-docs/jusprin/fork-stewardship.md` before touching anything outside `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/`. Changes there are small, additive, and come with the rebase evidence that document asks for.\n- **Errors.** Do not catch what you cannot recover from; never turn an impossible state into a silent no-op; one generic error for rare failures. Section \"Error handling discipline\" in `AGENTS.md`.\n- **Tests.** Every behaviour change gets a test, and the real app must be exercised for anything a test cannot cover. Reproduce a bug in the real app before fixing it; a failing fake is not a reproduction.\n- **Model spend.** No live-model run (the shell harness against a real provider, the live prompt suite) without Kenneth approving that batch and its stated spend. The staging gateway at `app-stg.obico.io` counts.\n- **Git.** Commit only when asked; never commit submodule pointers; no attribution lines in commits or PR descriptions; working docs like this one stay untracked.\n\n## 8. How you will know it works\n\n- Gateway: the pytest list in plan section 11 step 1, plus one end-to-end run through the local compose stack with `fake_upstream.py`: sign-up lot created on first contact, a Standard turn charges 1 from the expiring lot first, an Expert turn skips basic-only credits, the 402 body carries `basic_only_credits`, an app-origin turn charges 0.\n- App: Vitest for `ModelPickers`, the new balance panel, the composer's disabled Send, the attachment row in a Standard chat; Catch2 for `ProviderAgent`'s headers and 402 handling and for an app-started turn leaving the chat's model unset until the person's first message; the Home and onboarding suites from the branch; one shell-harness run against staging at a spend Kenneth approves.\n- Report in four parts, under 500 words: the problem, what you built, what you tested and how, what remains. Say plainly what you did not verify.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7cda6c9f-a9d5-4209-80f0-5d7ad3d68a82","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-flow-f7be35","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
