nt","uuid":"b8563284-7865-4313-a3d4-f568d9c62109","timestamp":"2026-11-03T14:40:30.246Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-flow-f7be35","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
{"parentUuid":"b8563284-7865-4313-a3d4-f568d9c62109","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3b8f975a-379e-4fed-8a28-01d66198f3b3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017kAsUGZvc2khponQ4i3gXG","type":"tool_result","content":"9:- Kenneth reviewed the list of mechanisms that were mine, not his (2026-11-02, late evening). **Kept:** the launch offer (double credits on packs until a date); the low-balance notice, reworded to \"About 25 credits left\" (credits, not messages); \"Expiring credits are used first\" in the panel; the \"Alert me when a subscription would save me money\" switch, on by default; the Account page shape (30-day total, bar chart per day, table of chats); Standard as the default tier for a new chat after the first month; the v1 welcome-back fill-ins; the print-report form details; alias ids `slicer-1` and `slicer-basic` with image stripping. **Dropped:** the reverse savings alert and board 7c; the month-end and 7-day expiry notices (rule 4 on board 0 loses them); the daily cap on free app turns; the thinking picker on Standard (Expert only). **Expiry:** every expiring lot expires one month from the day it was granted, never at a calendar month end: first-month credits a month after sign-in, the free 50 a month after each grant, plan credits with the billing cycle.\n14:Where the boards live on the canvas (decided 2026-11-02: boards sit with the flow they change, not on a feature page): the onboarding boards (1a to 1d, 6a, 6b) on \"On boarding experience\"; the composer states (2a to 2c, 3a to 3d, 7a to 7c) on \"Compositions\" beside the Composer; the Account boards (4a to 4c) on \"Agent setup & Preferences\"; the report boards (8a to 8d) on \"Print history\". \"Credits & plans\" keeps only what has no flow of its own: the five rules (board 0), the pricing page (5a, 5b) and the states overview (9). Every board has \"Credits\" in its canvas name so a search finds the set.\n37:### 1. First launch: own key or JusPrin account (boards 1a to 1d)\n39:Where: the Agent setup in Preferences › Agent (the one setup flow, decided 2026-10-23) and the welcome screen.\n41:Kenneth's reaction to the first draft, which put the offer as a small line under \"Set up JusPrin\": \"the most non-obvious way to urge user to sign up\". Opinion, as drawn: the offer is the headline on its own surface, \"Your first month: 500 credits\", with the translation under it, \"An Expert message is 5 credits. Your own API key stays free.\", and the button names the reward, \"Sign in for 500 credits\". \"Explore first\" moves below it. Never \"trial\" (decided): a trial promises a wall at the end. No dollar figure. The same hierarchy is on the setup row (1a), the welcome screen (1b) and the welcome-back window for a returning v1 user (1c), where signing in is the primary button and Continue secondary. It is \"Your own API key\", not \"your own key\" (Kenneth, board 1a).\n43:v1 subscribers (Kenneth, board 1c: \"make it clear that JusPrin v1 subscribers grandfathered to the $10/mo tier with the original price\", \"in addition to getting 500 credits\"). 1c adds the line \"Subscribed to JusPrin v1? You get these 500 credits and keep your original price, on the $10 Hobby plan.\", conditional because the app cannot know until sign-in. Board 1d is what that person sees once signed in: \"Hobby, at your original $6.99 a month. 750 credits a month. Plus 500 more for your first month. New subscribers pay $10. You keep this price while subscribed.\" Nothing to choose, no upgrade prompt; the annual plan reads \"at your original $59.99 a year\". The design session's fill-ins, not yet confirmed: the price holds \"while subscribed\"; the 500 stack on the 750 in the first month; and when the move happens (at sign-in or at term end) and how to say that v1 was \"unlimited\" and Hobby is not are open. v1 has 20 active subscriptions, 15 annual and 5 monthly.\n138:- v1 subscribers: the price holds \"while subscribed\"; 1,250 credits in the first month; the move at sign-in or at term end; how to say v1 was unlimited and Hobby is not.\n143:- A stray \"Your text here\" box on board 1a, hidden behind the Preferences window, from a page save of Kenneth's before version 64.\n145:Decided 2026-11-01 and 2026-11-02, so no longer open: the unit is \"credits\"; prices always carry \"a message\"; the plans are Hobby, Workshop and Pay as you go; the sign-up grant is \"your first month\", never \"trial\"; every balance is shown translated; a chat keeps its model; the composer shows only a ring, the count is in the hover panel; a bar per kind of expiring credit; \"Get more credits\" is the one action outside the pricing page; \"New Standard chat\" never under 5 spendable credits; the offer is the headline on the sign-in screens and the button names the reward; \"Your own API key\"; v1 subscribers keep their original price on Hobby and get the 500; \"Obico Premium Subscriber\"; the report button lives in Print history, not the chat; boards live with their flows; the cheap tier is \"Standard\"; a picture in a Standard chat is dropped and the attachment row says so with a \"New Expert chat\" button (board 3e); app-started turns run on Expert, free, without fixing the chat's model.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"1530b51b-d9ce-473a-96bf-49c70d94b50f","timestamp":"2026-11-03T14:40:30.325Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"9:- Kenneth reviewed the list of mechanisms that were mine, not his (2026-11-02, late evening). **Kept:** the launch offer (double credits on packs until a date); the low-balance notice, reworded to \"About 25 credits left\" (credits, not messages); \"Expiring credits are used first\" in the panel; the \"Alert me when a subscription would save me money\" switch, on by default; the Account page shape (30-day total, bar chart per day, table of chats); Standard as the default tier for a new chat after the first month; the v1 welcome-back fill-ins; the print-report form details; alias ids `slicer-1` and `slicer-basic` with image stripping. **Dropped:** the reverse savings alert and board 7c; the month-end and 7-day expiry notices (rule 4 on board 0 loses them); the daily cap on free app turns; the thinking picker on Standard (Expert only). **Expiry:** every expiring lot expires one month from the day it was granted, never at a calendar month end: first-month credits a month after sign-in, the free 50 a month after each grant, plan credits with the billing cycle.\n14:Where the boards live on the canvas (decided 2026-11-02: boards sit with the flow they change, not on a feature page): the onboarding boards (1a to 1d, 6a, 6b) on \"On boarding experience\"; the composer states (2a to 2c, 3a to 3d, 7a to 7c) on \"Compositions\" beside the Composer; the Account boards (4a to 4c) on \"Agent setup & Preferences\"; the report boards (8a to 8d) on \"Print history\". \"Credits & plans\" keeps only what has no flow of its own: the five rules (board 0), the pricing page (5a, 5b) and the states overview (9). Every board has \"Credits\" in its canvas name so a search finds the set.\n37:### 1. First launch: own key or JusPrin account (boards 1a to 1d)\n39:Where: the Agent setup in Preferences › Agent (the one setup flow, decided 2026-10-23) and the welcome screen.\n41:Kenneth's reaction to the first draft, which put the offer as a small line under \"Set up JusPrin\": \"the most non-obvious way to urge user to sign up\". Opinion, as drawn: the offer is the headline on its own surface, \"Your first month: 500 credits\", with the translation under it, \"An Expert message is 5 credits. Your own API key stays free.\", and the button names the reward, \"Sign in for 500 credits\". \"Explore first\" moves below it. Never \"trial\" (decided): a trial promises a wall at the end. No dollar figure. The same hierarchy is on the setup row (1a), the welcome screen (1b) and the welcome-back window for a returning v1 user (1c), where signing in is the primary button and Continue secondary. It is \"Your own API key\", not \"your own key\" (Kenneth, board 1a).\n43:v1 subscribers (Kenneth, board 1c: \"make it clear that JusPrin v1 subscribers grandfathered to the $10/mo tier with the original price\", \"in addition to getting 500 credits\"). 1c adds the line \"Subscribed to JusPrin v1? You get these 500 credits and keep your original price, on the $10 Hobby plan.\", conditional because the app cannot know until sign-in. Board 1d is what that person sees once signed in: \"Hobby, at your original $6.99 a month. 750 credits a month. Plus 500 more for your first month. New subscribers pay $10. You keep this price while subscribed.\" Nothing to choose, no upgrade prompt; the annual plan reads \"at your original $59.99 a year\". The design session's fill-ins, not yet confirmed: the price holds \"while subscribed\"; the 500 stack on the 750 in the first month; and when the move happens (at sign-in or at term end) and how to say that v1 was \"unlimited\" and Hobby is not are open. v1 has 20 active subscriptions, 15 annual and 5 monthly.\n138:- v1 subscribers: the price holds \"while subscribed\"; 1,250 credits in the first month; the move at sign-in or at term end; how to say v1 was unlimited and Hobby is not.\n143:- A stray \"Your text here\" box on board 1a, hidden behind the Preferences window, from a page save of Kenneth's before version 64.\n145:Decided 2026-11-01 and 2026-11-02, so no longer open: the unit is \"credits\"; prices always carry \"a message\"; the plans are Hobby, Workshop and Pay as you go; the sign-up grant is \"your first month\", never \"trial\"; every balance is shown translated; a chat keeps its model; the composer shows only a ring, the count is in the hover panel; a bar per kind of expiring credit; \"Get more credits\" is the one action outside the pricing page; \"New Standard chat\" never under 5 spendable credits; the offer is the headline on the sign-in screens and the button names the reward; \"Your own API key\"; v1 subscribers keep their original price on Hobby and get the 500; \"Obico Premium Subscriber\"; the report button lives in Print history, not the chat; boards live with their flows; the cheap tier is \"Standard\"; a picture in a Standard chat is dropped and the attachment row says so with a \"New Expert chat\" button (board 3e); app-started turns run on Expert, free, without fixing the chat's model.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b8563284-7865-4313-a3d4-f568d9c62109","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-flow-f7be35","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
