{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","hash":"8f4031e68d268f3edef0dca1b51dd73afe2e1ee3d1d46bdcd7ee964a25d1432c","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FNCbCWYXyKT9Fqizk2bsrf","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin && git show -s --format='%s%n%n%b' 48ec76705d | head -90; echo \"==================\"; git show -s --format='%s%n%n%b' 445ee541bd | head -60; echo \"==================\"; git show -s --format='%s%n%n%b' 4af9ded841 | head -20","description":"Read the credits branch's commit messages"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LqSg7P1Qy5NrSF5zbb4gG4","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin && cat design-captures/credits-2026-11/MANIFEST.md 2>/dev/null | head -80; echo \"== captures\"; ls design-captures/credits-2026-11/ | head -60","description":"List the credits boards from the capture manifest"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017kAsUGZvc2khponQ4i3gXG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin && grep -n -i -E '\\b1a\\b|\\b1b\\b|\\b1c\\b|\\b1d\\b|welcome|first-run|first run|onboarding|sign in|sign-in' pricing-touchpoints-design-2026-11.md | head -40","description":"Find the onboarding touchpoints in the pricing design doc"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ECMR1U1qUxtkxguyoiu7QA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin && echo \"== AgentUI changes credits->first-run\"; git diff --stat credits-integration-2026-11..claude/first-run-flow-f7be35 -- src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/V1Import src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Preferences | cat; echo \"== BalancePanel / Preferences / PreferencesApp diffs\"; git diff credits-integration-2026-11..claude/first-run-flow-f7be35 -- src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/BalancePanel.tsx src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/Preferences.tsx src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/PreferencesApp.tsx | head -120","description":"See what the first-run branch changed in the credits UI"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","hash":"5c843e7b97babc437dd8e404952a32a50ee87711e53ccacd54ad5369c25e51db","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FNCbCWYXyKT9Fqizk2bsrf","type":"tool_result","content":"Add JusPrin Cloud credits and the first-run path on Home\n\nThe app now shows and spends JusPrin Cloud credits, and a new install starts\non Home with a first-run path. This is steps 0, 1, 2, 4 and 5 of the credits\nplan on the app side. Step 3 (Chargebee, the served Account and pricing pages,\nv1 carry-over) is not here. It needs the gateway change on tsd-enterprise\nbranch claude/credits-ledger.\n\nOnboarding, ported from 8f4588beae and brought to the current boards:\n- Home walks through the welcome, importing presets from an OrcaSlicer install,\n  choosing a printer, and opening a project or the bundled example.\n- save_onboarding passed const char* to AppConfig::set, which saved every field\n  as \"true\". It now saves each value.\n- \"I don't have a printer here\" refused on a fresh install, because no vendor\n  was installed. It now installs Generic Klipper Printer and saves it under its\n  own name, as normal printer setup does, so the chip shows no warning.\n- The example opens handy_models/3DBenchy.drc. The earlier example file had\n  three stacked objects, three filaments and a collision warning.\n- An empty project is no longer listed on Home when its only history is\n  printer, filament or process choices. A chat on an empty plate stays listed.\n- The welcome-back window's kept-price box is hidden behind\n  V1_PRICE_CARRIES_OVER until step 3 ships.\n\nCredits:\n- Model pickers show each model's price and are greyed once the person has sent\n  a message in the chat. The account's balance shows as a ring with a hover\n  panel, and the composer offers \"Get more credits\" when a message can't be paid\n  for. A 402 from the gateway ends in a failed card.\n- Turns the app starts itself send X-JusPrin-Request: note and run on Expert\n  without changing the chat's model. RecordConversion turns one format's stored\n  turn into the other's, the same bytes each time, so provider caches still hit.\n- A Standard chat leaves out the picture tools and says so on the attachment\n  row, with a \"New Expert chat\" button.\n\nCost and rewards:\n- A turn that polls for its own slice is answered with busy, and the third\n  refused poll ends the turn. The note turn that reports the slice still runs.\n- Print history has a report form with a photo, and Home shows the credit line\n  when signed in to the account.\n\nTests: AgentUI Vitest (651) and HomeUI Vitest (130) with tsc, jusprin_tests\n(151), agent_bridge_tests (506), shell_theme_tests (14), brand_tokens_tests and\nthe shell harness default run (600 checks) and --fresh-example pass on macOS.\nThe real app ran the fresh-install example on an empty data folder, and three\nlive chats ran through a local gateway. Windows and Linux were not run.\ntests/shell/shell_harness.cpp also fixes three harness defects on macOS that\nwere there before this work: a null title bar menu in --print-history, page\nreads cut at about 1000 characters, and fake-printer control writes within one\nsecond being ignored.\n\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M6EJ644FNDCPRA5S3703D1BX\n\n==================\nApply the final credit rules in the app\n\nKenneth reviewed the credits boards and changed the rules. Every credit is now\nthe same, a balance is one number of credits, and the app stops translating it\ninto messages.\n\n- The balance panel has one bar per lot, grouped by expiry, and bought credits\n  get a bar too. Workshop's bar adds \"Unused credits don't carry over.\"\n- Prices in messages stay only on the model menu and the stop card. The\n  first-month offer now reads \"An Expert message is 5 credits. Your own API key\n  stays free.\" Welcome-back reads \"750 credits a month.\"\n- The low-balance notice reads \"About 25 credits left\" at 25 credits or less on\n  any model that charges, once, with Get more credits and a close button. The\n  rounding to the nearest 5 is a fill-in, not Kenneth's.\n- \"New Standard chat\" and \"New Expert chat\" are gone, along with the host's\n  chatModel and draft path and the error details that fed them. A chat that\n  cannot be paid offers Get more credits only.\n- A picture in a Standard chat now shows as a warning on its chip, with Remove.\n- A new chat on the account starts on Expert while a first-month lot is live and\n  on Standard after it, as on board 6a. This was unbuilt until now.\n- Standard has no thinking picker, because its alias now has no efforts.\n\nFixed along the way: the two-line rows in the model menu overlapped, because menu\nrows have a fixed height. Vitest does not apply CSS, so a real-app screenshot\nfound it. No automated test guards it.\n\nNot done: the pricing page, the savings alert and the Account switch belong to\nlater steps and are not built. Open bug: on a Standard chat the app can show\n\"The automatic chat title could not be generated\", because the model sometimes\nanswers the message instead of writing a title (4 of 12 direct tries were too\nlong to use).\n\nTested: Agent page 654 tests, agent bridge 506, JusPrin 151. The real app ran\nagainst a local gateway with real keys: 0, 1 and 5 credits charged as intended on\na file-opened turn, a Standard message and an Expert message. The shell harness\nlast ran before the low-balance and report-limit changes. Windows, Linux and dark\nmode were not run.\n\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M6EZ6J03KW501EDCY1FCPDZR\n\n==================\nStop handling print reports that earn nothing\n\nKenneth removed the daily limit and the stop after invalid reports, so a report\nalways earns its 25 credits. The form's \"earned no credits\" screen, its two\nsentences and its Done button can no longer be reached, and neither can the\nnoReward field carried from the gateway through the host to the page.\n\nThe gateway side of this is on claude/credits-ledger in tsd-enterprise; the two\ngo together.\n\nTested: Home page 129 tests, agent bridge 506, JusPrin 151. Not run in the real\napp or the shell harness; a search of the harness found no use of what was\nremoved.\n\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M6EZ75WGREMC5K4S12BKD919","is_error":false},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LqSg7P1Qy5NrSF5zbb4gG4","type":"tool_result","content":"# Credits & plans boards, 2026-11-01\n\nThe boards are on the JusPrin v2 canvas, https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ (version 79, 1793642611-3f5d), each on the page of its flow: 1a to 1d, 6a and 6b on \"On boarding experience\"; 2a to 2c, 3a to 3c, 3e, 7a and 7b on \"Compositions\" beside the Composer; 4a to 4c on \"Agent setup & Preferences\"; 8a to 8d on \"Print history\"; 0 (the five rules), 5a, 5b and 9 on \"Credits & plans\". Nothing is committed. PNGs are in `/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/credits-2026-11/` (untracked, not ignored).\n\n| PNG | Board | What it shows |\n|---|---|---|\n| credits-00-rules | 0 | The five rules from pricing-touchpoints-design-2026-11.md |\n| credits-01a-agent-setup | 1a | Preferences › Agent over a first-run Home, with the pitch on the account row (also -dark) |\n| credits-01b-welcome | 1b | The canvas's proposed welcome screen, pitch under Set up JusPrin (also -dark) |\n| credits-01c-welcome-back | 1c | The welcome window the app builds today, pitch in the account box (also -dark) |\n| credits-01d-welcome-back-v1-subscriber | 1d | Welcome window for a signed-in JusPrin v1 subscriber: Hobby at their original price (also -dark) |\n| credits-02a-balance-hover | 2a | Greyed model and thinking pickers, ring only, hover usage panel with a bar per kind of credit |\n| credits-02b-tier-picker | 2b | New chat, picker open: Basic and Expert with price per message and clause, own-key models without price |\n| credits-02c-pickers-greyed-tooltip | 2c | Chat under way: tooltip on the greyed pickers with the reason and the price |\n| credits-03a-low-notice | 3a | \"About 25 credits left\", ring in the warning colour |\n| credits-03b-send-with-basic | 3b | 3 credits: Send disabled, note, Get more credits, typed text kept (file name kept for the comment anchor) |\n| credits-03c-failed-card | 3c | Gateway 402 card at 3 credits with Get more credits |\n| credits-03e-picture-in-standard-chat | 3e | Standard chat with a photo staged: the row's second line warns it won't be sent, Remove is the only action, Send enabled |\n| credits-04a-account-over-prepare | 4a | Preferences › Account at window size over Prepare |\n| credits-04b-account-first-month | 4b | Whole Account section, first month plus a pack (also -dark) |\n| credits-04c-account-workshop | 4c | Whole Account section on Workshop as an Obico member; its \"+25\" print-report row is decided, 25 credits, one per G-code (also -dark) |\n| credits-05a-pricing | 5a | Pricing page, three cards, launch note (also -dark) |\n| credits-05b-pricing-obico | 5b | Same page with the member price as the price |\n| credits-06a-first-month-ended | 6a | First launch after the first month: new chat on Standard, with the ring, no thinking picker and no line about free credits |\n| credits-06b-first-month-ended-picker | 6b | Same new chat with the picker open on Expert |\n| credits-07a-alert-hobby | 7a | Savings alert, Pay as you go to Hobby |\n| credits-07b-alert-hobby-sums | 7b | Same with the arithmetic open |\n| credits-08a-report-button | 8a | \"Tell us how it printed · 25 credits\" on the Print history entry, beside Print again and Export |\n| credits-08b-report-form | 8b | Report form over Print history: photo, a few sentences, outcome |\n| credits-08c-report-sent | 8c | The button replaced by a \"Report sent · 25 credits added\" row on the entry |\n| credits-08d-home-way-in | 8d | Home with the report line on a project card, opening Print history filtered to that project |\n| credits-09-states | 9 | Balance and tier label states, light and dark panels |\n\n## Numbers corrected in canvas version 70\n\n1. The translation of the balance now reads \"612 Basic or 112 Expert messages\", because the 50 free Basic messages can't pay for Expert: (612 − 50) / 5 = 112.\n2. The savings alert now says $5.00. 820 credits cost $16.40 Pay as you go, against $10 + 70 × 2¢ = $11.40 on Hobby.\n3. The balance is now 62 first-month + 50 free Basic + 500 bought = 612. A 500 pack can't stand at 450 while first-month credits remain, because expiring credits are used first. Usage is 438 credits (500 − 62), and 4b's \"+25\" print report row became \"Bought 500 credits, +500\", because an unspent reward would be a never-expiring lot the balance doesn't show.\n\n## Kenneth's decisions applied in canvas version 71 (2026-11-02)\n\n1. The cheap tier is \"Standard\", on every board. Older lines in this file say \"Basic\" because they describe what was true then. The file names credits-03b-send-with-basic and credits-03d-expert-chat-free-basic keep the old word, so comment anchors and capture names hold. \"Bambu PLA Basic\" is a filament and stays. The orange note lost its item about the docs allowing a mid-chat switch; its Thinking picker item is still open, so it stays.\n2. New board 3e. Kenneth then changed it directly, 2026-11-02: \"remove 'new expert chat' button\" and \"style it as warning. with color and icon.\" So the row is the usual thumbnail, name, second line and Remove, and the second line is the design system's warning: the triangle-alert glyph in status-warning beside Body Small in primary ink. The colour is on the glyph only, because #D49A2A as text is hard to read on the light surface. The board shows a chat under way.\n3. The turn the app starts when a file opens runs on Expert, is free, and doesn't fix the chat's model. 2b's caption says so, and 2b, 6b and board 9 now say \"the person's first message\". 2c's tooltip is unchanged.\n\n## Kenneth's decision applied in canvas version 73 (2026-11-02)\n\nBalances are shown in credits only. He said that showing a number of messages and credits at the same time is confusing. The rule he agreed with: a number of messages appears only where the person chooses or is stopped, never on a balance. This replaces the translations described in the older lines of this file, including item 1 under \"Numbers corrected in canvas version 70\".\n\n- 2a, 4a, 4b, 4c: the headline stands alone, \"612 credits left\" (\"640 credits left\" on 4c). The free lot is \"Free Standard credits\", and its note line starts \"Standard only\". No board has a tag component, so the marker is words on the note line.\n- 1a, 1b, 1c: the line under the offer is \"An Expert message is 5 credits. Your own API key stays free.\"\n- 1d: \"750 credits a month.\"\n- 5a, 5b: the translation line is gone from all three cards. The launch offer ends \"$10 buys 1,000 credits.\"\n- Not in the brief, changed because they would be false otherwise: the captions of 4c (\"on free Standard credits\") and 5a (no longer says the cards state the price in messages).\n- Boards 0, 1a's kept \"Your text here\" box, 2b, 2c, 3a to 3e, 6a, 6b, 7a to 7c, 8a to 8d and 9 are unchanged. Board 9 moved up 40 px on the canvas because 5b above it got shorter.\n\n## Canvas version 74 (2026-11-02), the pricing session's follow-up to version 73\n\nChanged: 6a and 6b's composer line is \"50 free Standard credits this month\"; 3d's title, caption and notice say \"free Standard credits\"; board 0's rule 1 is headed \"One word, one unit, credits only.\" and says a balance is a number of credits and nothing else. On 6b the line sits behind the open menu, as it did before.\n\nKept, because the pricing session says they describe allowances or ceilings, not a balance: 5a and 5b's \"Everyone also gets 50 free Standard messages a month.\"; board 9's \"used 500 of 600 free Standard messages this month\" and the notice at 600; 2c's caption \"while free messages last\".\n\nRule 1 now says prices in messages appear only on the picker options, the stop card, the pricing page sentence and one scale line under the first-month offer. Three things drawn elsewhere don't fit that list, left as they are because both briefs kept them: 3a's \"About 5 Expert messages left\" (a low-balance count in messages), 2c's tooltip \"Each message you send in this chat costs 5 credits.\", and 4c's note \"After 600, Standard is 1 credit a message until then.\"\n\n## Kenneth's decisions applied in canvas version 75 (2026-11-02)\n\nHis words, relayed by the pricing session: \"no ceiling. It's probably easier just to say standard messages cost 0 credits\" (Workshop) and \"let's just give free users 50/mo use-it-or-loose it credits\". He also agreed that bought credits get a bar like the others. These replace the Standard-only lot, the 600 ceiling and the plain number for bought credits described in the older lines of this file.\n\n1. Every credit is the same. The free allowance is 50 credits a month that expire at month end and pay for either tier. 2a, 4a, 4b show \"First-month credits 62 of 500 left, Expires 1 Dec\", \"Free credits 50 of 50 left, Resets 1 Dec\", \"Bought credits 500 of 500 left, Never expire\". The total stays 612.\n2. Workshop is 1,000 credits a month, and Standard messages cost 0 credits. 4c has one bar, \"Workshop credits 640 of 1,000 left\", because this subscriber has no bought credits and the total stays 640. 5a and 5b's Workshop card and footer changed as asked. Board 9 lost the notices at 500 and 600. 2b's caption gives \"Standard · 0 credits a message\" for a Workshop subscriber; no board draws that menu.\n3. Board 3d is removed, its PNG too, and 3e moved left into its place. New Standard chat is gone from the captions of 3b and 3c.\n\nChanged beyond the brief, because the new rules make them false:\n- 6b's menu showed \"Standard · free\". It now shows \"Standard · 1 credit a message\", because a Standard message spends a free credit.\n- Captions: 2a, 2c (\"free this month\" is gone), 4b, 4c, 6a (pointed at 3d, now 3b), 6b.\n- Board 0: rule 3 lost \"Never a bare number that mixes kinds\", because the total is a plain sum; rule 4 lost \"fair use\". Rule 5 never mentioned New Standard chat, and board 0 had no Workshop line, so the Workshop sentence went into rule 2.\n- The blue note on the credits page lost its items about 188 of 600, New Standard chat, Standard · free and the Workshop 600 line.\n\nOpen questions:\n- Closed in version 76, from Kenneth directly: \"No. the \"everyone gets 50 credits\" wording is wrong. I never sadi that.\" A Workshop subscriber doesn't get the 50, so 4c is right as drawn. 5a and 5b's footer now reads \"Free accounts get 50 credits a month. Unused ones don't carry over. Your own API key stays free and never uses credits.\" `pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md` line 142 still says \"Everyone\".\n== captures\nCHANGELOG-v54-to-v69.md\nMANIFEST.md\ncredits-00-rules.png\ncredits-01a-agent-setup-dark.png\ncredits-01a-agent-setup.png\ncredits-01b-welcome-dark.png\ncredits-01b-welcome.png\ncredits-01c-welcome-back-dark.png\ncredits-01c-welcome-back.png\ncredits-01d-welcome-back-v1-subscriber-dark.png\ncredits-01d-welcome-back-v1-subscriber.png\ncredits-02a-balance-hover.png\ncredits-02b-tier-picker.png\ncredits-02c-pickers-greyed-tooltip.png\ncredits-03a-low-notice.png\ncredits-03b-send-with-basic.png\ncredits-03c-failed-card.png\ncredits-03e-picture-in-standard-chat.png\ncredits-04a-account-over-prepare.png\ncredits-04b-account-first-month-dark.png\ncredits-04b-account-first-month.png\ncredits-04c-account-workshop-dark.png\ncredits-04c-account-workshop.png\ncredits-05a-pricing-dark.png\ncredits-05a-pricing.png\ncredits-05b-pricing-obico.png\ncredits-06a-first-month-ended.png\ncredits-06b-first-month-ended-picker.png\ncredits-07a-alert-hobby.png\ncredits-07b-alert-hobby-sums.png\ncredits-08a-report-button.png\ncredits-08b-report-form.png\ncredits-08c-report-sent.png\ncredits-08d-home-way-in.png\ncredits-09-states-dark.png\ncredits-09-states.png","is_error":false},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017kAsUGZvc2khponQ4i3gXG","type":"tool_result","content":"9:- Kenneth reviewed the list of mechanisms that were mine, not his (2026-11-02, late evening). **Kept:** the launch offer (double credits on packs until a date); the low-balance notice, reworded to \"About 25 credits left\" (credits, not messages); \"Expiring credits are used first\" in the panel; the \"Alert me when a subscription would save me money\" switch, on by default; the Account page shape (30-day total, bar chart per day, table of chats); Standard as the default tier for a new chat after the first month; the v1 welcome-back fill-ins; the print-report form details; alias ids `slicer-1` and `slicer-basic` with image stripping. **Dropped:** the reverse savings alert and board 7c; the month-end and 7-day expiry notices (rule 4 on board 0 loses them); the daily cap on free app turns; the thinking picker on Standard (Expert only). **Expiry:** every expiring lot expires one month from the day it was granted, never at a calendar month end: first-month credits a month after sign-in, the free 50 a month after each grant, plan credits with the billing cycle.\n14:Where the boards live on the canvas (decided 2026-11-02: boards sit with the flow they change, not on a feature page): the onboarding boards (1a to 1d, 6a, 6b) on \"On boarding experience\"; the composer states (2a to 2c, 3a to 3d, 7a to 7c) on \"Compositions\" beside the Composer; the Account boards (4a to 4c) on \"Agent setup & Preferences\"; the report boards (8a to 8d) on \"Print history\". \"Credits & plans\" keeps only what has no flow of its own: the five rules (board 0), the pricing page (5a, 5b) and the states overview (9). Every board has \"Credits\" in its canvas name so a search finds the set.\n37:### 1. First launch: own key or JusPrin account (boards 1a to 1d)\n39:Where: the Agent setup in Preferences › Agent (the one setup flow, decided 2026-10-23) and the welcome screen.\n41:Kenneth's reaction to the first draft, which put the offer as a small line under \"Set up JusPrin\": \"the most non-obvious way to urge user to sign up\". Opinion, as drawn: the offer is the headline on its own surface, \"Your first month: 500 credits\", with the translation under it, \"An Expert message is 5 credits. Your own API key stays free.\", and the button names the reward, \"Sign in for 500 credits\". \"Explore first\" moves below it. Never \"trial\" (decided): a trial promises a wall at the end. No dollar figure. The same hierarchy is on the setup row (1a), the welcome screen (1b) and the welcome-back window for a returning v1 user (1c), where signing in is the primary button and Continue secondary. It is \"Your own API key\", not \"your own key\" (Kenneth, board 1a).\n43:v1 subscribers (Kenneth, board 1c: \"make it clear that JusPrin v1 subscribers grandfathered to the $10/mo tier with the original price\", \"in addition to getting 500 credits\"). 1c adds the line \"Subscribed to JusPrin v1? You get these 500 credits and keep your original price, on the $10 Hobby plan.\", conditional because the app cannot know until sign-in. Board 1d is what that person sees once signed in: \"Hobby, at your original $6.99 a month. 750 credits a month. Plus 500 more for your first month. New subscribers pay $10. You keep this price while subscribed.\" Nothing to choose, no upgrade prompt; the annual plan reads \"at your original $59.99 a year\". The design session's fill-ins, not yet confirmed: the price holds \"while subscribed\"; the 500 stack on the 750 in the first month; and when the move happens (at sign-in or at term end) and how to say that v1 was \"unlimited\" and Hobby is not are open. v1 has 20 active subscriptions, 15 annual and 5 monthly.\n138:- v1 subscribers: the price holds \"while subscribed\"; 1,250 credits in the first month; the move at sign-in or at term end; how to say v1 was unlimited and Hobby is not.\n143:- A stray \"Your text here\" box on board 1a, hidden behind the Preferences window, from a page save of Kenneth's before version 64.\n145:Decided 2026-11-01 and 2026-11-02, so no longer open: the unit is \"credits\"; prices always carry \"a message\"; the plans are Hobby, Workshop and Pay as you go; the sign-up grant is \"your first month\", never \"trial\"; every balance is shown translated; a chat keeps its model; the composer shows only a ring, the count is in the hover panel; a bar per kind of expiring credit; \"Get more credits\" is the one action outside the pricing page; \"New Standard chat\" never under 5 spendable credits; the offer is the headline on the sign-in screens and the button names the reward; \"Your own API key\"; v1 subscribers keep their original price on Hobby and get the 500; \"Obico Premium Subscriber\"; the report button lives in Print history, not the chat; boards live with their flows; the cheap tier is \"Standard\"; a picture in a Standard chat is dropped and the attachment row says so with a \"New Expert chat\" button (board 3e); app-started turns run on Expert, free, without fixing the chat's model.","is_error":false},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ECMR1U1qUxtkxguyoiu7QA","type":"tool_result","content":"== AgentUI changes credits->first-run\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/PreferencesApp.tsx          |  9 +++++++++\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/bridge/protocol.ts          |  3 +++\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/BalancePanel.tsx |  7 ++++---\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/Preferences.tsx  |  9 +++++++--\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Preferences/PreferencesWindow.cpp       | 10 +++++++++-\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Preferences/PreferencesWindow.hpp       |  6 ++++++\n 6 files changed, 38 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)\n== BalancePanel / Preferences / PreferencesApp diffs\ndiff --git a/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/PreferencesApp.tsx b/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/PreferencesApp.tsx\nindex db438e5117..7a8e8a4c0c 100644\n--- a/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/PreferencesApp.tsx\n+++ b/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/PreferencesApp.tsx\n@@ -33,6 +33,14 @@ export function PreferencesApp({ getTransport }: { getTransport: () => Transport\n     applyAppearance(state.appearance);\n   }, [state.appearance]);\n \n+  // A window opened for one task closes itself once it is done.\n+  const closeWhenDone = Boolean(state.preferences?.closeWhenDone);\n+  const finish = (done: 'key' | 'tool') => client.send('shell_action', { action: 'close', done });\n+  useEffect(() => {\n+    if (closeWhenDone && state.setup.phase === 'verified') finish('key');\n+    // eslint-disable-next-line react-hooks/exhaustive-deps\n+  }, [closeWhenDone, state.setup.phase]);\n+\n   const actions = useMemo<PreferencesActions>(\n     () => ({\n       set: (name, value) => client.send('preferences_action', { action: 'set', name, value }),\n@@ -71,6 +79,7 @@ export function PreferencesApp({ getTransport }: { getTransport: () => Transport\n         mcpPreview={state.mcpPreview}\n         mcpStatus={state.mcpStatus}\n         actions={actions}\n+        onToolDone={closeWhenDone ? () => finish('tool') : undefined}\n       />\n     </div>\n   );\ndiff --git a/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/BalancePanel.tsx b/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/BalancePanel.tsx\nindex 7c693c22e1..5b4d9da825 100644\n--- a/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/BalancePanel.tsx\n+++ b/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/BalancePanel.tsx\n@@ -29,9 +29,10 @@ function lotName(lot: CreditLot, account: CreditAccount): string {\n   }\n }\n \n-interface Row { key: string; name: string; left: number; of: number; date: string }\n+export interface Row { key: string; name: string; left: number; of: number; date: string }\n \n-function rows(account: CreditAccount): Row[] {\n+// Also Home's account card, which draws the same bars.\n+export function balanceRows(account: CreditAccount): Row[] {\n   const expiring = account.credits.lots.filter((lot) => lot.expires_at).map((lot) => ({\n     key: `${lot.kind}-${lot.expires_at}`, name: lotName(lot, account), left: lot.credits, of: lot.granted, at: lot.expires_at!,\n     date: `Expires ${shortDate(lot.expires_at!)}${lot.kind === 'subscription' ? '. Unused credits don’t carry over.' : ''}`,\n@@ -90,7 +91,7 @@ export function BalancePanel({ account, low, onGetMore, onSeeUsage }: {\n         <strong>{creditCount(account.credits.total)} left</strong>\n       </div>\n       <div className=\"credit-panel-lots\">\n-        {rows(account).map((row) => <div key={row.key} className=\"credit-lot\">\n+        {balanceRows(account).map((row) => <div key={row.key} className=\"credit-lot\">\n           <div className=\"credit-lot-line\">\n             <strong>{row.name}</strong>\n             <span>{creditNumber(row.left)} of {creditNumber(row.of)} left</span>\ndiff --git a/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/Preferences.tsx b/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/Preferences.tsx\nindex cfa01f4469..fa5da3aca1 100644\n--- a/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/Preferences.tsx\n+++ b/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/Preferences.tsx\n@@ -68,6 +68,8 @@ export interface PreferencesProps {\n   mcpPreview: McpPreviewPayload | null;\n   mcpStatus: McpStatusPayload;\n   actions: PreferencesActions;\n+  // Done on an AI tool, for a window opened to close once one is connected.\n+  onToolDone?: () => void;\n }\n \n // The JusPrin account row, as Account and Agent both draw it.\n@@ -455,7 +457,7 @@ function rememberedSection(): PreferencesSection | null {\n   }\n }\n \n-export function Preferences({ preferences, setup, savedKeys, account, mcpCatalog, mcpPreview, mcpStatus, actions }: PreferencesProps) {\n+export function Preferences({ preferences, setup, savedKeys, account, mcpCatalog, mcpPreview, mcpStatus, actions, onToolDone }: PreferencesProps) {\n   // Opened where the app was asked to open it; the list moves on from there.\n   const [section, setSection] = useState<PreferencesSection>(() => rememberedSection() ?? preferences.section);\n   // The AI tool being connected, which takes the Agent section's place.\n@@ -504,7 +506,10 @@ export function Preferences({ preferences, setup, savedKeys, account, mcpCatalog\n             onConnect={actions.connectTool}\n             onReveal={actions.revealTool}\n             onBack={() => setTool(null)}\n-            onDone={() => setTool(null)}\n+            onDone={() => {\n+              setTool(null);\n+              onToolDone?.();\n+            }}\n           />\n         ) : (\n           <AgentSection agent={preferences.agent} setup={setup} savedKeys={savedKeys} account={account} mcpCatalog={mcpCatalog}","is_error":false}]}}
