{"parentUuid":"b8f03ac6-001c-4d20-82b9-7b390edd5dd6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3b8f975a-379e-4fed-8a28-01d66198f3b3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ULY125JrGJHSQrwzmMEMux","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"django-allauth changelog \"login by code\" sign up unknown email version 65 \"ACCOUNT_LOGIN_BY_CODE_ENABLED\" headless\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"File python-django-allauth.changes of Package python-django-allauth\",\"url\":\"https://build.opensuse.org/projects/home:jloehel:paperless/packages/python-django-allauth/files/python-django-allauth.changes?expand=0\"},{\"title\":\"python django allauth.changes\",\"url\":\"https://build.opensuse.org/projects/home:dirkmueller:acdc/packages/python-django-allauth/files/python-django-allauth.changes?expand=1\"},{\"title\":\"65.18.0 (2026-05-29)#\",\"url\":\"https://docs.allauth.org/en/dev/release-notes/recent.html\"},{\"title\":\"dwww Home | Show directory contents | Find package\",\"url\":\"https://doc.duckcorp.org/cgi-bin/dwww/usr/share/doc/python3-django-allauth/changelog.gz\"},{\"title\":\"alpinelinux.org\",\"url\":\"https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports/-/merge_requests/72813\"},{\"title\":\"upgrade guide\",\"url\":\"https://www.mintlify.com/pennersr/django-allauth/migration/upgrade-guide\"},{\"title\":\"65.13.1 (2025-11-20)#\",\"url\":\"https://docs.allauth.org/en/dev/release-notes/2025.html\"}]\n\nThe one search didn't turn up a changelog entry about login-by-code sign-up for unknown emails, or about `ACCOUNT_LOGIN_BY_CODE_ENABLED` specifically. The results do cover nearby login-by-code changes in the 65.x line:\n\n- **65.0.x:** Login by code gained a setting that requires every user to enter an emailed confirmation code, via ACCOUNT_LOGIN_BY_CODE_REQUIRED. A related breaking change means that accessing the login/signup page now redirects to the pending login stage when a user is partly logged in, including during login by code.\n- **65.15.1 (2026-04-02):** Optional support for requesting new login codes was added, controlled by ACCOUNT_LOGIN_BY_CODE_SUPPORTS_RESEND.\n- **65.18.0 (2026-05-29):** Login by code got a \"Trust this browser?\" option, controlled by ACCOUNT_LOGIN_BY_CODE_TRUST_ENABLED, per the release notes at docs.allauth.org.\n\nThe results also show that headless mode now needs the `headless` extra installed (pip install django-allauth[headless]), but they don't say whether that applies to the sign-up behavior you asked about.\n\nFor the unknown-email sign-up question, the best next step is the official ChangeLog.rst in the django-allauth repository, or the release notes at docs.allauth.org for the 65.x versions. Those would confirm whether `ACCOUNT_LOGIN_BY_CODE_ENABLED` exists and how it behaves.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c66dbbdc-cb5c-4aa5-81ab-463ad290f98e","timestamp":"2026-11-03T14:41:25.282Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"django-allauth changelog \"login by code\" sign up unknown email version 65 \"ACCOUNT_LOGIN_BY_CODE_ENABLED\" headless","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01VsyW9h4FXasN1HFEJkXAKN","content":[{"title":"File python-django-allauth.changes of Package python-django-allauth","url":"https://build.opensuse.org/projects/home:jloehel:paperless/packages/python-django-allauth/files/python-django-allauth.changes?expand=0"},{"title":"python django allauth.changes","url":"https://build.opensuse.org/projects/home:dirkmueller:acdc/packages/python-django-allauth/files/python-django-allauth.changes?expand=1"},{"title":"65.18.0 (2026-05-29)#","url":"https://docs.allauth.org/en/dev/release-notes/recent.html"},{"title":"dwww Home | Show directory contents | Find package","url":"https://doc.duckcorp.org/cgi-bin/dwww/usr/share/doc/python3-django-allauth/changelog.gz"},{"title":"alpinelinux.org","url":"https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports/-/merge_requests/72813"},{"title":"upgrade guide","url":"https://www.mintlify.com/pennersr/django-allauth/migration/upgrade-guide"},{"title":"65.13.1 (2025-11-20)#","url":"https://docs.allauth.org/en/dev/release-notes/2025.html"}]},"The one search didn't turn up a changelog entry about login-by-code sign-up for unknown emails, or about `ACCOUNT_LOGIN_BY_CODE_ENABLED` specifically. The results do cover nearby login-by-code changes in the 65.x line:\n\n- **65.0.x:** Login by code gained a setting that requires every user to enter an emailed confirmation code, via ACCOUNT_LOGIN_BY_CODE_REQUIRED. A related breaking change means that accessing the login/signup page now redirects to the pending login stage when a user is partly logged in, including during login by code.\n- **65.15.1 (2026-04-02):** Optional support for requesting new login codes was added, controlled by ACCOUNT_LOGIN_BY_CODE_SUPPORTS_RESEND.\n- **65.18.0 (2026-05-29):** Login by code got a \"Trust this browser?\" option, controlled by ACCOUNT_LOGIN_BY_CODE_TRUST_ENABLED, per the release notes at docs.allauth.org.\n\nThe results also show that headless mode now needs the `headless` extra installed (pip install django-allauth[headless]), but they don't say whether that applies to the sign-up behavior you asked about.\n\nFor the unknown-email sign-up question, the best next step is the official ChangeLog.rst in the django-allauth repository, or the release notes at docs.allauth.org for the 65.x versions. Those would confirm whether `ACCOUNT_LOGIN_BY_CODE_ENABLED` exists and how it behaves."],"durationSeconds":5.863706207998097,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b8f03ac6-001c-4d20-82b9-7b390edd5dd6","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-flow-f7be35","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
{"parentUuid":"b6f6cd05-6c56-43d2-8e17-60c6ac7419cf","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3b8f975a-379e-4fed-8a28-01d66198f3b3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012S5boityofZShSHTRx3k2M","type":"tool_result","content":"**Login by code**\n\n- **`ACCOUNT_LOGIN_BY_CODE_ENABLED`** (default `False`)\n  - Quote: \"“Login by email” offers an alternative method of logging in.\" (61 characters)\n  - Unknown emails: Not stated.\n\n- **`ACCOUNT_LOGIN_BY_CODE_REQUIRED`** (default `False`)\n  - Quote: \"When enabled (in case of True), every user logging in is required to input a login confirmation code sent by email.\" (117 characters)\n  - Unknown emails: Not stated.\n\n- **`ACCOUNT_LOGIN_BY_CODE_MAX_ATTEMPTS`** (default `3`)\n  - Quote: \"This setting controls the maximum number of attempts the user has at inputting a valid code.\" (93 characters)\n  - Unknown emails: Not stated.\n\n- **`ACCOUNT_LOGIN_BY_CODE_TIMEOUT`** (default `180`)\n  - Quote: \"The code that is emailed has a limited life span. It expires this many seconds after which it was sent.\" (103 characters)\n  - Unknown emails: Not stated.\n\n**Signup by code**\n\n- **`ACCOUNT_SIGNUP_BY_CODE`**\n  - This setting does not appear in the provided content.\n\n- **`ACCOUNT_EMAIL_VERIFICATION_BY_CODE_ENABLED`** (default `False`)\n  - Quote: \"Controls whether email verification is performed by means of following a link in the email\" (91 characters)\n  - Unknown emails: Not stated.\n\nThe page does not say whether unknown email addresses are signed up under any of these settings. The only related setting it describes is `ACCOUNT_EMAIL_UNKNOWN_ACCOUNTS`, which applies to password reset attempts, not login or verification by code."}]},"uuid":"48b17ec9-9ea8-4824-97cb-7e821f8aa294","timestamp":"2026-11-03T14:41:28.107Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":97764,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**Login by code**\n\n- **`ACCOUNT_LOGIN_BY_CODE_ENABLED`** (default `False`)\n  - Quote: \"“Login by email” offers an alternative method of logging in.\" (61 characters)\n  - Unknown emails: Not stated.\n\n- **`ACCOUNT_LOGIN_BY_CODE_REQUIRED`** (default `False`)\n  - Quote: \"When enabled (in case of True), every user logging in is required to input a login confirmation code sent by email.\" (117 characters)\n  - Unknown emails: Not stated.\n\n- **`ACCOUNT_LOGIN_BY_CODE_MAX_ATTEMPTS`** (default `3`)\n  - Quote: \"This setting controls the maximum number of attempts the user has at inputting a valid code.\" (93 characters)\n  - Unknown emails: Not stated.\n\n- **`ACCOUNT_LOGIN_BY_CODE_TIMEOUT`** (default `180`)\n  - Quote: \"The code that is emailed has a limited life span. It expires this many seconds after which it was sent.\" (103 characters)\n  - Unknown emails: Not stated.\n\n**Signup by code**\n\n- **`ACCOUNT_SIGNUP_BY_CODE`**\n  - This setting does not appear in the provided content.\n\n- **`ACCOUNT_EMAIL_VERIFICATION_BY_CODE_ENABLED`** (default `False`)\n  - Quote: \"Controls whether email verification is performed by means of following a link in the email\" (91 characters)\n  - Unknown emails: Not stated.\n\nThe page does not say whether unknown email addresses are signed up under any of these settings. The only related setting it describes is `ACCOUNT_EMAIL_UNKNOWN_ACCOUNTS`, which applies to password reset attempts, not login or verification by code.","durationMs":9691,"url":"https://docs.allauth.org/en/latest/account/configuration.html"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b6f6cd05-6c56-43d2-8e17-60c6ac7419cf","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-flow-f7be35","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
