{"parentUuid":"1b17df9d-046d-4877-9d3d-fa17627e3238","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CggAxkaBZ7SMqLSNRJBa2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018yX99C9ZUCCG8Zh6JQBfvR","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"S=/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34/scratchpad/tag; D=/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/first-run-2026-11; cp \"$S/si-a-email-door.png\" \"$D/12a-sign-in-email-door.png\"; cp \"$S/si-b-code.png\" \"$D/12b-sign-in-code.png\"; cp \"$S/si-c-code-expired.png\" \"$D/12c-sign-in-code-expired.png\"; cp \"$S/si-d-browser-waiting.png\" \"$D/12d-sign-in-browser-waiting.png\"; cp \"$S/si-sheet.png\" \"$D/12-sign-in-sheet.png\"; cp \"$S/build8.py\" \"$D/../value-prop-2026-11/tagline/build8.py\"; ls \"$D\" | grep 12\nM=/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory\ncat >> \"$M/old-onboarding-boards-review.md\" <<'EOF'\n\n**Kenneth's rulings, 2026-11-03 morning:** no example model (\"No need for example models\"); the email code goes in (\"taking the users of the app into browser is not the best user experience. Email code keeps the user in the app\"); everything else I listed he agreed with (v1-aware door, browser-return recovery, Terms line, import result, \"checking AI\" belongs on Home's agent card). He also asked for proof that the pricing work on `credits-integration-2026-11` is fully carried into the flow.\n\n**Pricing audit result:** the first-run branch touched only the onboarding screens, Home's agent group (reusing `balanceRows`) and Preferences' close-when-done; pickers, ring and panel, pre-send check, 402 card, low-balance notice, print-report form, the welcome-back window (boards 1c/1d) and the Preferences account row (1a) are untouched from the credits branch. One drift: the scale line under the offer reads \"Then paid, or your own key.\" and must be the decided \"An Expert message is 5 credits. Your own API key stays free.\" Step 3 (Chargebee, Account and pricing pages, v1 carry-over) is unbuilt on both branches, and production's gateway lacks the ledger branch, which is why the account card showed no balance.\n\n**Email-code design (renders `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/12a..12d`, generator `value-prop-2026-11/tagline/build8.py`):** the offer card keeps the decided headline, scale line and \"Sign in for 500 credits\" button, with an email field beside the button; under it \"We email you a 6-digit code. No password.\" and a link to the browser (Google or a password); a Terms and Privacy line. Pressing the button swaps the card for \"Check your email.\" with six cells that sign in on the sixth digit, Resend / Change email / Use the browser instead / Cancel; an expired or wrong code turns the cells red with \"Send a new code\". The browser state gains \"Nothing happened? Open the browser again · Check sign-in\" and \"Use an email code instead\". Placeholder address is always alex@example.com.\n\n**Server facts for the code:** the gateway authenticates OAuth2 bearer tokens of any application (`web_ent/jusprin/v2/auth.py`); the app's OAuth app is \"JusPrin2\" (public, PKCE). The Obico server runs django-allauth 0.63.6, whose login-by-code only serves existing users and has no API in that version, so the code sign-in is two new gateway endpoints (request a code; confirm it and issue a JusPrin2 access token), creating the user when the email is unknown the way the adapter does (username `email_syndicateid`). Trap: `ACCOUNT_UNIQUE_EMAIL = False`, so one email can own several accounts; the confirm step must pick deterministically (most recently active in the JusPrin syndicate) and say so in a comment.\nEOF\necho saved","description":"Save the renders beside the other captures and record the rulings and audit in memory"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6645,"cache_read_input_tokens":291530,"output_tokens":2302,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":798},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6645,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2302,"cache_read_input_tokens":291530,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6645,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6645},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018yX99C9ZUCCG8Zh6JQBfvR":{"command":"S=/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34/scratchpad/tag; D=/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/first-run-2026-11; cp \"$S/si-a-email-door.png\" \"$D/12a-sign-in-email-door.png\"; cp \"$S/si-b-code.png\" \"$D/12b-sign-in-code.png\"; cp \"$S/si-c-code-expired.png\" \"$D/12c-sign-in-code-expired.png\"; cp \"$S/si-d-browser-waiting.png\" \"$D/12d-sign-in-browser-waiting.png\"; cp \"$S/si-sheet.png\" \"$D/12-sign-in-sheet.png\"; cp \"$S/build8.py\" \"$D/../value-prop-2026-11/tagline/build8.py\"; ls \"$D\" | grep 12\nM=/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory\ncat >> \"$M/old-onboarding-boards-review.md\" <<'EOF'\n\n**Kenneth's rulings, 2026-11-03 morning:** no example model (\"No need for example models\"); the email code goes in (\"taking the users of the app into browser is not the best user experience. Email code keeps the user in the app\"); everything else I listed he agreed with (v1-aware door, browser-return recovery, Terms line, import result, \"checking AI\" belongs on Home's agent card). He also asked for proof that the pricing work on `credits-integration-2026-11` is fully carried into the flow.\n\n**Pricing audit result:** the first-run branch touched only the onboarding screens, Home's agent group (reusing `balanceRows`) and Preferences' close-when-done; pickers, ring and panel, pre-send check, 402 card, low-balance notice, print-report form, the welcome-back window (boards 1c/1d) and the Preferences account row (1a) are untouched from the credits branch. One drift: the scale line under the offer reads \"Then paid, or your own key.\" and must be the decided \"An Expert message is 5 credits. Your own API key stays free.\" Step 3 (Chargebee, Account and pricing pages, v1 carry-over) is unbuilt on both branches, and production's gateway lacks the ledger branch, which is why the account card showed no balance.\n\n**Email-code design (renders `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/12a..12d`, generator `value-prop-2026-11/tagline/build8.py`):** the offer card keeps the decided headline, scale line and \"Sign in for 500 credits\" button, with an email field beside the button; under it \"We email you a 6-digit code. No password.\" and a link to the browser (Google or a password); a Terms and Privacy line. Pressing the button swaps the card for \"Check your email.\" with six cells that sign in on the sixth digit, Resend / Change email / Use the browser instead / Cancel; an expired or wrong code turns the cells red with \"Send a new code\". The browser state gains \"Nothing happened? Open the browser again · Check sign-in\" and \"Use an email code instead\". Placeholder address is always alex@example.com.\n\n**Server facts for the code:** the gateway authenticates OAuth2 bearer tokens of any application (`web_ent/jusprin/v2/auth.py`); the app's OAuth app is \"JusPrin2\" (public, PKCE). The Obico server runs django-allauth 0.63.6, whose login-by-code only serves existing users and has no API in that version, so the code sign-in is two new gateway endpoints (request a code; confirm it and issue a JusPrin2 access token), creating the user when the email is unknown the way the adapter does (username `email_syndicateid`). Trap: `ACCOUNT_UNIQUE_EMAIL = False`, so one email can own several accounts; the confirm step must pick deterministically (most recently active in the JusPrin syndicate) and say so in a comment.\nEOF\necho saved","description":"Save the renders beside the other captures and record the rulings and audit in memory"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CggAxjgr8ShjgtadFCPtj","requestRef":"49f8aa8a-b8c4-41cb-a85a-c02a8c2f1762","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-1","type":"assistant","uuid":"22c371a7-9bb4-4447-be05-1e5209ab4a2f","timestamp":"2026-11-03T14:44:15.033Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34/scratchpad/tag","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-flow-f7be35","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
