{"parentUuid":"22c371a7-9bb4-4447-be05-1e5209ab4a2f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3b8f975a-379e-4fed-8a28-01d66198f3b3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018yX99C9ZUCCG8Zh6JQBfvR","type":"tool_result","content":"12-sign-in-sheet.png\n12a-sign-in-email-door.png\n12b-sign-in-code.png\n12c-sign-in-code-expired.png\n12d-sign-in-browser-waiting.png\nsaved","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f1e4b6c1-0400-45fd-a73a-42ffcbabd3c3","timestamp":"2026-11-03T14:44:15.650Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"12-sign-in-sheet.png\n12a-sign-in-email-door.png\n12b-sign-in-code.png\n12c-sign-in-code-expired.png\n12d-sign-in-browser-waiting.png\nsaved","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/tagline/build8.py","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":86,"lines":["+\"\"\"The welcome's sign-in door with an email code: four states of the right column. Reuses build6's frame.\"\"\"","+import subprocess, sys, tempfile","+from pathlib import Path","+HERE = Path(__file__).parent","+sys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))","+import build6 as b","+from build import CHROME","+","+PRIMARY = 'display:inline-flex;gap:6px;padding:var(--space-8) var(--space-16);justify-content:center;align-items:center;background:var(--action-primary);color:var(--action-on-primary);border-radius:var(--radius-medium);white-space:nowrap'","+FIELD = 'flex:1;height:36px;display:flex;align-items:center;padding:0 var(--space-12);background:var(--surface-canvas);border-radius:var(--radius-small);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px var(--border-subtle)'","+LINK = 'color:var(--action-primary)'","+EMAIL = 'alex@example.com'","+LOCKUP43 = '<img src=\"lockup.svg\" style=\"height:43px;position:absolute;left:24px;top:24px\">'","+","+def card(inner):","+    return f'<div class=\"card sel\" style=\"padding:var(--space-16);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--space-8)\">{inner}</div>'","+","+def cells(filled='', error=False):","+    ring = 'var(--status-danger)' if error else 'var(--border-subtle)'","+    out = ''","+    for i in range(6):","+        ch = filled[i] if i < len(filled) else ''","+        focus = '' if error or i != len(filled) else ';box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 2px var(--border-focus)'","+        out += f'<div style=\"width:40px;height:44px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;background:var(--surface-canvas);border-radius:var(--radius-small);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px {ring}{focus}\" class=\"body-bold\">{ch}</div>'","+    return f'<div style=\"display:flex;gap:var(--space-8)\">{out}</div>'","+","+def links(*items):","+    return '<span class=\"label-bold\">' + ' <span style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">·</span> '.join(f'<span style=\"{LINK}\">{t}</span>' for t in items) + '</span>'","+","+OFFER_HEAD = '<span class=\"section\">Your first month: 500 credits</span><span class=\"body-small\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">An Expert message is 5 credits. Your own API key stays free.</span>'","+TERMS = '<span class=\"label\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">By signing in you agree to the <span style=\"' + LINK + '\">Terms</span> and <span style=\"' + LINK + '\">Privacy Policy</span>.</span>'","+","+# a. The door at rest: email field and the button that names the reward.","+A = card(OFFER_HEAD + f'''","+<div style=\"display:flex;gap:var(--space-8);margin-top:var(--space-8)\"><div style=\"{FIELD}\"><span class=\"body\" style=\"color:var(--text-tertiary)\">you@example.com</span></div><span class=\"body-small-bold\" style=\"{PRIMARY}\">Sign in for 500 credits</span></div>","+<span class=\"label\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">We email you a 6-digit code. No password. <span style=\"{LINK}\">Use Google or a password in the browser instead</span></span>","+{TERMS}''')","+","+# b. The code, typed in the app.","+B = card(f'''<span class=\"section\">Check your email.</span><span class=\"body-small\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">We sent a 6-digit code to {EMAIL}.</span>","+<div style=\"margin-top:var(--space-8)\">{cells('41')}</div>","+<span class=\"label\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">The sixth digit signs you in. Read the email on any device.</span>","+<div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;margin-top:var(--space-4)\">{links('Resend code', 'Change email', 'Use the browser instead')}<span class=\"label-bold\" style=\"{LINK}\">Cancel</span></div>''')","+","+# c. The code expired or was wrong.","+C = card(f'''<span class=\"section\">Check your email.</span><span class=\"body-small\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">We sent a 6-digit code to {EMAIL}.</span>","+<div style=\"margin-top:var(--space-8)\">{cells('418203', error=True)}</div>","+<span class=\"label\" style=\"color:var(--status-danger)\">That code has expired. We can send a new one.</span>","+<div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;margin-top:var(--space-4)\"><span class=\"body-small-bold\" style=\"{PRIMARY}\">Send a new code</span>{links('Change email', 'Use the browser instead')}</div>''')","+","+# d. The browser path, with the way back when the browser never returns.","+D = card(f'''<span class=\"section\" style=\"display:flex;gap:var(--space-8);align-items:center\"><span style=\"width:14px;height:14px;border-radius:50%;border:2px solid var(--border-subtle);border-top-color:var(--action-primary);display:inline-block\"></span>Finish signing in in your browser.</span>","+<span class=\"body-small\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">The app continues on its own once the browser is done.</span>","+<span class=\"label\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary);margin-top:var(--space-8)\">Nothing happened? {links('Open the browser again', 'Check sign-in')}</span>","+<div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;margin-top:var(--space-4)\">{links('Use an email code instead')}<span class=\"label-bold\" style=\"{LINK}\">Cancel</span></div>''')","+","+FREE = ''.join([","+  b.ns['door']('Your own API key', 'Free'),","+  b.ns['door']('Claude Code or Claude Desktop', 'Free · MCP server'),","+  '<span class=\"label-bold\" style=\"color:var(--action-primary);padding:var(--space-4) 0\">Just slice for now</span>',","+])","+LABEL = '<span class=\"label\" style=\"color:var(--text-secondary)\">Pick how the agent should think. Change it any time in Preferences › Agent.</span>'","+","+def screen(door, free=True):","+    doors = LABEL + door + (FREE if free else '')","+    return f'''{b.HEAD}<div class=\"screen\">{LOCKUP43}","+<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;justify-content:center;align-items:center\">","+ <div style=\"width:1120px;display:flex;gap:var(--space-48);align-items:center\">","+  {b.CLIP}","+  <div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--space-20)\">","+   <div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--space-8)\">{b.TITLE}</div>","+   <div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--space-8)\">{doors}</div>","+  </div>","+ </div></div>","+</div></body></html>'''","+","+SCREENS = (('si-a-email-door', screen(A)), ('si-b-code', screen(B)), ('si-c-code-expired', screen(C)), ('si-d-browser-waiting', screen(D)))","+","+if __name__ == '__main__':","+    for name, html in SCREENS:","+        (HERE / f'{name}.html').write_text(html)","+        png = HERE / f'{name}.png'","+        subprocess.run([CHROME, '--headless=new', '--disable-gpu', '--no-first-run', f'--user-data-dir={tempfile.mkdtemp()}', '--hide-scrollbars',","+                        '--window-size=1280,800', '--force-device-scale-factor=2', '--virtual-time-budget=4000', f'--screenshot={png}',","+                        f'file://{HERE}/{name}.html'], check=True, capture_output=True, timeout=90)","+        print(png)"]}],"created":true}],"moreFiles":5,"changedFiles":["/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/first-run-2026-11/12-sign-in-sheet.png","/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/first-run-2026-11/12a-sign-in-email-door.png","/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/first-run-2026-11/12b-sign-in-code.png","/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/first-run-2026-11/12c-sign-in-code-expired.png","/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/first-run-2026-11/12d-sign-in-browser-waiting.png","/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/tagline/build8.py"]}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"22c371a7-9bb4-4447-be05-1e5209ab4a2f","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34/scratchpad/tag","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-flow-f7be35","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
{"parentUuid":"c356c3d4-b412-427c-a1a9-17a49f5df364","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3b8f975a-379e-4fed-8a28-01d66198f3b3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q9AL2vKYq7oDu5Lusvzoff","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Plan updated: step 5 of 5 is in progress."}]}]},"uuid":"61c52e71-4014-4977-922f-746efdfd669e","timestamp":"2026-11-03T14:44:15.701Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"Plan updated: step 5 of 5 is in progress."}],"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c356c3d4-b412-427c-a1a9-17a49f5df364","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34/scratchpad/tag","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-flow-f7be35","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
{"parentUuid":"61c52e71-4014-4977-922f-746efdfd669e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/old-onboarding-boards-review.md","snippet":"18\t- OrcaSlicer import: choose the folder manually or a preset bundle when nothing is detected; a partial-result screen (conflicts renamed \"(Orca copy)\", failures with reasons, Retry failed items). New flow: one list, Import / Start fresh / Back; conflicts go through a yes/no dialog mid-import.\n19\t- First project: \"Try the example\" (3DBenchy) beside Open. New Home empty state has only New / Open; the example was removed with the Project step.\n20\t- v1 users: a Welcome back card listing what was copied, \"the same account you used in v1\", and a sign-in-expired variant. New flow keeps WelcomeBackWindow separately but the welcome's sign-in door still says \"Your first month: 500 credits\" to everyone.\n21\t- Project load failed: \"No existing work was replaced\", native reason, Retry / Choose another. General file-open behaviour, not onboarding.\n22\t\n23\t**My ranking (Kenneth has not ruled yet):** take the example model on Home's empty state and a v1-aware sign-in door first; then the browser-return recovery and the Terms line; then the import result report. The email code is a server project and a second sign-in path; recommend deferring it.\n24\t\n25\t**How to apply:** when Kenneth rules, record the decision here and in [[first-run-flow-sequence]]; the boards named above are the reference for wording and states. Related: [[first-run-value-prop-decisions]], [[v1-subscribers-grandfathered]].\n26\t\n27\t**Kenneth's rulings, 2026-11-03 morning:** no example model (\"No need for example models\"); the email code goes in (\"taking the users of the app into browser is not the best user experience. Email code keeps the user in the app\"); everything else I listed he agreed with (v1-aware door, browser-return recovery, Terms line, import result, \"checking AI\" belongs on Home's agent card). He also asked for proof that the pricing work on `credits-integration-2026-11` is fully carried into the flow.\n28\t\n29\t**Pricing audit result:** the first-run branch touched only the onboarding screens, Home's agent group (reusing `balanceRows`) and Preferences' close-when-done; pickers, ring and panel, pre-send check, 402 card, low-balance notice, print-report form, the welcome-back window (boards 1c/1d) and the Preferences account row (1a) are untouched from the credits branch. One drift: the scale line under the offer reads \"Then paid, or your own key.\" and must be the decided \"An Expert message is 5 credits. Your own API key stays free.\" Step 3 (Chargebee, Account and pricing pages, v1 carry-over) is unbuilt on both branches, and production's gateway lacks the ledger branch, which is why the account card showed no balance.\n30\t\n31\t**Email-code design (renders `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/12a..12d`, generator `value-prop-2026-11/tagline/build8.py`):** the offer card keeps the decided headline, scale line and \"Sign in for 500 credits\" button, with an email field beside the button; under it \"We email you a 6-digit code. No password.\" and a link to the browser (Google or a password); a Terms and Privacy line. Pressing the button swaps the card for \"Check your email.\" with six cells that sign in on the sixth digit, Resend / Change email / Use the browser instead / Cancel; an expired or wrong code turns the cells red with \"Send a new code\". The browser state gains \"Nothing happened? Open the browser again · Check sign-in\" and \"Use an email code instead\". Placeholder address is always alex@example.com.\n32\t\n33\t**Server facts for the code:** the gateway authenticates OAuth2 bearer tokens of any application (`web_ent/jusprin/v2/auth.py`); the app's OAuth app is \"JusPrin2\" (public, PKCE). The Obico server runs django-allauth 0.63.6, whose login-by-code only serves existing users and has no API in that version, so the code sign-in is two new gateway endpoints (request a code; confirm it and issue a JusPrin2 access token), creating the user when the email is unknown the way the adapter does (username `email_syndicateid`). Trap: `ACCOUNT_UNIQUE_EMAIL = False`, so one email can own several accounts; the confirm step must pick deterministically (most recently active in the JusPrin syndicate) and say so in a comment."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"25a0afe9-1b0a-48a0-ae45-896df63d3d8b","timestamp":"2026-11-03T14:44:15.708Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/old-onboarding-boards-review.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n18\t- OrcaSlicer import: choose the folder manually or a preset bundle when nothing is detected; a partial-result screen (conflicts renamed \"(Orca copy)\", failures with reasons, Retry failed items). New flow: one list, Import / Start fresh / Back; conflicts go through a yes/no dialog mid-import.\n19\t- First project: \"Try the example\" (3DBenchy) beside Open. New Home empty state has only New / Open; the example was removed with the Project step.\n20\t- v1 users: a Welcome back card listing what was copied, \"the same account you used in v1\", and a sign-in-expired variant. New flow keeps WelcomeBackWindow separately but the welcome's sign-in door still says \"Your first month: 500 credits\" to everyone.\n21\t- Project load failed: \"No existing work was replaced\", native reason, Retry / Choose another. General file-open behaviour, not onboarding.\n22\t\n23\t**My ranking (Kenneth has not ruled yet):** take the example model on Home's empty state and a v1-aware sign-in door first; then the browser-return recovery and the Terms line; then the import result report. The email code is a server project and a second sign-in path; recommend deferring it.\n24\t\n25\t**How to apply:** when Kenneth rules, record the decision here and in [[first-run-flow-sequence]]; the boards named above are the reference for wording and states. Related: [[first-run-value-prop-decisions]], [[v1-subscribers-grandfathered]].\n26\t\n27\t**Kenneth's rulings, 2026-11-03 morning:** no example model (\"No need for example models\"); the email code goes in (\"taking the users of the app into browser is not the best user experience. Email code keeps the user in the app\"); everything else I listed he agreed with (v1-aware door, browser-return recovery, Terms line, import result, \"checking AI\" belongs on Home's agent card). He also asked for proof that the pricing work on `credits-integration-2026-11` is fully carried into the flow.\n28\t\n29\t**Pricing audit result:** the first-run branch touched only the onboarding screens, Home's agent group (reusing `balanceRows`) and Preferences' close-when-done; pickers, ring and panel, pre-send check, 402 card, low-balance notice, print-report form, the welcome-back window (boards 1c/1d) and the Preferences account row (1a) are untouched from the credits branch. One drift: the scale line under the offer reads \"Then paid, or your own key.\" and must be the decided \"An Expert message is 5 credits. Your own API key stays free.\" Step 3 (Chargebee, Account and pricing pages, v1 carry-over) is unbuilt on both branches, and production's gateway lacks the ledger branch, which is why the account card showed no balance.\n30\t\n31\t**Email-code design (renders `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/12a..12d`, generator `value-prop-2026-11/tagline/build8.py`):** the offer card keeps the decided headline, scale line and \"Sign in for 500 credits\" button, with an email field beside the button; under it \"We email you a 6-digit code. No password.\" and a link to the browser (Google or a password); a Terms and Privacy line. Pressing the button swaps the card for \"Check your email.\" with six cells that sign in on the sixth digit, Resend / Change email / Use the browser instead / Cancel; an expired or wrong code turns the cells red with \"Send a new code\". The browser state gains \"Nothing happened? Open the browser again · Check sign-in\" and \"Use an email code instead\". Placeholder address is always alex@example.com.\n32\t\n33\t**Server facts for the code:** the gateway authenticates OAuth2 bearer tokens of any application (`web_ent/jusprin/v2/auth.py`); the app's OAuth app is \"JusPrin2\" (public, PKCE). The Obico server runs django-allauth 0.63.6, whose login-by-code only serves existing users and has no API in that version, so the code sign-in is two new gateway endpoints (request a code; confirm it and issue a JusPrin2 access token), creating the user when the email is unknown the way the adapter does (username `email_syndicateid`). Trap: `ACCOUNT_UNIQUE_EMAIL = False`, so one email can own several accounts; the confirm step must pick deterministically (most recently active in the JusPrin syndicate) and say so in a comment.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34/scratchpad/tag","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-flow-f7be35","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
