\" and \"Use an email code instead\". Placeholder address is always alex@example.com.\n32\t\n33\t**Server facts for the code:** the gateway authenticates OAuth2 bearer tokens of any application (`web_ent/jusprin/v2/auth.py`); the app's OAuth app is \"JusPrin2\" (public, PKCE). The Obico server runs django-allauth 0.63.6, whose login-by-code only serves existing users and has no API in that version, so the code sign-in is two new gateway endpoints (request a code; confirm it and issue a JusPrin2 access token), creating the user when the email is unknown the way the adapter does (username `email_syndicateid`). Trap: `ACCOUNT_UNIQUE_EMAIL = False`, so one email can own several accounts; the confirm step must pick deterministically (most recently active in the JusPrin syndicate) and say so in a comment.\n\n<total_tokens>14941192 tokens left</total_tokens>\n\nPlain output style is active. Remember to follow the specific guidelines for this style."}]}}
