{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","id":"be4ee8b1-bc86-4961-b97a-f1750c46a4c3","timestamp":"2026-11-03T14:44:27.955Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"23f1d61ae8837bf8ac29a6fe9a1adfcdee338dbd56f5f4a09693cb2f7f92a77d","params":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":64000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"e20a2ede-ce25-4e93-94d4-e6f455394794","keep":170,"tail":["e71b7500ecd6867e2e623675aa6904b6eefd8ac027898e23a465c87a06f9c144","eb0d212a58559aab0c32d6f07cd897ca1a3279b44f65c2daf65d13e116d9e95e","dc508a92cb3656988e5b4c931d04cb46647f68c8b1a7eb1ad428e56381547878","fd45c40b25ab2bc033d485d0e1d865199e6d98d240b67fae5912b30ba5e3b54c"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",172,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"b464db2c3062740341a6e65a063890cd50f9dd07076aa23086cd16d3fcd64d18"}
{"parentUuid":"3bde713d-6e98-4033-8ecc-635e5e5c53f7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CggB2E8TcZM1y3EVZYQir","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Three things done: the pricing audit you asked for, the email-code door design, and the rulings recorded.\n\n**The pricing work is carried over.** The credits branch's app-side work is four commits: the ledger and charging on the gateway side, and in the app the priced model pickers, the balance ring and hover panel, the pre-send check and 402 card, the low-balance notice, app-started turns on Expert, the Standard-chat picture warning, the print-report form, and the onboarding boards 1a to 1d. The first-run session changed only the onboarding screens, Home's agent group, and a close-when-done switch on Preferences. Everything else is byte-for-byte the credits branch, including the welcome-back window for v1 users with its \"keep your original price\" lines and the Preferences account row. I found one drift to fix: the line under the offer reads \"Then paid, or your own key.\" and the decided wording is \"An Expert message is 5 credits. Your own API key stays free.\" Two things are missing on both branches and were always planned as later steps: Chargebee with the Account and pricing pages, and the ledger branch is not deployed to production, which is why the account card showed no balance.\n\n**The email-code door** keeps your decided hierarchy. The offer stays the headline and the button still names the reward, with the email field beside it. Under it, one line says a 6-digit code arrives by email with no password, and a link keeps the browser as the way to use Google or an existing password. A Terms and Privacy line sits at the bottom of the card. Pressing the button swaps the card for the code entry, six cells that sign the person in on the sixth digit, with Resend, Change email, Use the browser instead, and Cancel. An expired or wrong code turns the cells red and offers a new code. The browser path gains the recovery you agreed to: \"Nothing happened? Open the browser again · Check sign-in\" and a way back to the code.\n\n**What the code sign-in costs on the server.** The Obico server's django-allauth is version 0.63.6. Its login-by-code only signs in existing accounts and has no API in that version, so this is two new gateway endpoints: request a code for an email, and confirm the code and issue a JusPrin2 access token, creating the account when the email is new the way the existing adapter does. One trap is that the Obico server does not require unique emails, so the confirm step has to choose an account deterministically when one address owns several.\n\nNot drawn yet, to be built from the old boards: the import result screen and a manual folder choice, and the v1 line on the door when a v1 import was found."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":928,"cache_read_input_tokens":302292,"output_tokens":817,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":928,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":817,"cache_read_input_tokens":302292,"cache_creation_input_tokens":928,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":928},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CggB2DhB3FPjKT5tLRHfw","requestRef":"be4ee8b1-bc86-4961-b97a-f1750c46a4c3","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-1","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"242ed419-51fb-455a-a1ea-205bfe8b9c86","timestamp":"2026-11-03T14:44:41.872Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34/scratchpad/tag","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-flow-f7be35","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
